4	{"Folded both dated updates into a single Current Status covering race week and the Oct 18 and Oct 25 long runs.","Added an Achilles watchpoint from the Wed Oct 14 run to Injuries and constraints.","Updated Shoes to reflect Endorphin Speed 4 for MP long runs and Ghost 16 for taper easy portions.","Dropped the summer heat HR cap guidance and the VO2/800s note, both superseded by the taper.","Next tidy-up due Wed Nov 18."}	# About you\n\n## Stance\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\n\n## Goal\nLakeshore Marathon on Sun Nov 15, your fourth marathon. Target 3:30. Your current best is 3:41 from two years ago.\n\n## Schedule\nYou run five days a week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are fixed rest days because of work travel and cannot move. Weekday runs are early, around 6 am, up to an hour. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Total 6 to 7 hours a week, more on long-run weeks. You travel for work roughly one week in six.\n\n## Running history\nThree marathons done, best 3:41. You eased off in June, then built back to about 30 miles a week through July. Easy runs sit near 9:20 to 9:40/mi.\n\n## Injuries and constraints\nYou had shin splints in your first marathon block, so you prefer a careful ramp. Achilles watchpoint is open after a brief whisper at mile 7 on your Wed Oct 14 run that settled on its own; keep up the heel drops and flag anything that lingers. Monday and Friday rest days are non-negotiable.\n\n## Preferences\nFlat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, with a hillier route on Thursdays. Long run on Sunday. You want to know why each session is in the plan. Happy to work hard on quality days, but easy days must stay properly easy. Imperial units.\n\n## Shoes\nBrooks Ghost 16 for daily easy miles on Tue, Wed and Sat, and for the easy portions of the taper long runs on Sun Nov 1 and Sun Nov 8. Saucony Endorphin Speed 4 for workouts and for long runs that include a marathon-pace block, including Sun Oct 18 and Sun Oct 25, and it is fine for any short MP touch inside the taper long runs.\n\n## Heart rate zones\nCustom zones. Z1 112-131, Z2 131-150, Z3 150-164, Z4 164-177, Z5 177-188.\n\n## Current Status\nAbout four weeks out from Lakeshore Marathon on Sun Nov 15. Training is healthy and on track at roughly 30 miles a week across five runs. Achilles is the one thing to watch after the brief whisper on Wed Oct 14 that settled - monitoring only, no change to the plan. Sun Oct 18 is 15 miles with 4 at marathon pace. Sun Oct 25 is the peak long run with 6 to 8 at marathon pace. Taper long runs follow on Sun Nov 1 and Sun Nov 8, with the easy portion in the Ghost 16. Quality work stays marathon-pace focused through the taper.	audit	pending	2026-10-14 23:20:40.628587+00	\N	\N	\N
