:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:01/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:06/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:06/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:15/mi / 7:60/mi / 8:03/mi / 8:04/mi\\n\\nBack half avg pace: 8:48/mi vs front 9:10/mi (faster than front half by 23s/mi) ✓ negative split\\n\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? Yes (paced up or HR above easy cap)\\n\\n## Trends\\n\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi → 9:20/mi → 9:14/mi ▁▁▃█\\n\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 143 → 144 → 144 ▁█▁▁\\n\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi → 11.94 mi → 17.18 mi ▃▁▃█\\n\\n## Notable\\n\\n- Relative effort (317) ≥ 1.3× 3-wk avg (223) — possible overload\\n\\n## Subjective recap\\n\\nSleep avg this week: 7.5 hrs (range 7–8)\\n\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\n\\nStress level: Low.\\n\\nBody check: Legs tired after the long run but nothing sore. Achilles quiet.\\n\\nGoing into next week feeling: Good. The last three miles at marathon pace were hard but I could have held it.\\n\\n## Questions for coach\\n\\n1. How should the final weeks before the race look?\\n", "weekSessionId": "42d956f4-8b0a-4145-98ff-a058741c4904", "prescribedWeek": {"days": [{"date": "2026-09-28", "notes": "Fixed rest/travel. 10 min mobility if you feel like it — calves and ankles. Slow heel drops as prescribed.", "dayType": "rest", "strength": "Optional mobility (10 min)"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:30–9:50/mi, HR Z2", "distanceM": 8047, "structure": "5-min walk warm-up, then 5 mi conversational on the canal path"}, "date": "2026-09-29", "notes": "Shake-out from Sunday. Conversational, flat canal path. 5-min walk warm-up before you start running.", "dayType": "easy"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:25–9:45/mi, HR Z2", "distanceM": 11265, "structure": "5-min walk warm-up, then 7 mi easy + 6×20s strides after the run"}, "date": "2026-09-30", "notes": "Primary aerobic day. Strides are relaxed turnover, not sprints — on flat ground with full walk recovery between.", "dayType": "easy", "strength": "Strength session 1 (30–40 min): hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work"}, {"run": {"type": "quality", "shoes": "Saucony Endorphin Speed 4", "paceOrHr": "MP reps 7:55–8:05/mi (mid-Z3/low-Z4); WU/CD 9:40–10:00/mi", "distanceM": 12875, "structure": "5-min walk warm-up, then 8 mi total: 2 mi WU → 2 × 2 mi @ goal MP (8:00/mi) with 3:00 easy jog between → 1.5 mi CD"}, "date": "2026-10-01", "notes": "Returning to MP intervals. First rep should feel controlled, not racing — if mile 1 is under 7:50 you went too hot. Hilly Thursday route is fine; hold effort on climbs and let pace drift 5–10 sec. If anything grumbles in the Achilles during warm-up, convert to an easy 6 and we'll try again next week.", "dayType": "quality"}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "notes": "Fixed rest. Hydrate and eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts here.", "dayType": "rest"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:45–10:05/mi, HR Z2", "distanceM": 6437, "structure": "5-min walk warm-up, then 4 mi very easy on flat canal path"}, "date": "2026-10-03", "notes": "Pre-long flush. Slower is better.", "dayType": "easy", "strength": "Strength session 2 (20–25 min): core + calves"}, {"run": {"type": "long", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "HR ≤150; pace likely 9:30–9:50/mi", "distanceM": 21726, "structure": "5-min walk warm-up, then 13.5 mi steady on the canal path, HR-capped. Out-and-back."}, "date": "2026-10-04", "notes": "Long run back to 13.5. No MP finish this week — just honest aerobic time on feet with HR cap. Fuel every 30–35 min with a gel (3 gels total), fluids with electrolytes. Start pre-sunrise if warm. If HR drifts above 150 and won't come back, walk 30s and resume slower.", "dayType": "long"}], "week": "2026-W40"}}, {"isoWeek": "2026-W39", "analysis": "## Headline\\nGood news dominates: the Achilles backed down, Sunday's long run was pain-free with no afterward stiffness, and your physio has cleared you to keep running — including one short tempo this week if morning stiffness stays gone. Easy pace and HR behavior are unchanged (143 avg, 91% Z1+Z2), which tells me the aerobic engine held together through the quiet week. We're going to rebuild carefully: ~32 mi, a short controlled tempo on Thursday, and a long run back out to 11 miles.\\n\\n## Your questions\\n**1. Can we put a short tempo in?** Yes — exactly as your physio framed it. Thursday is a short, honest tempo (2 miles continuous at ~8:00/mi, your goal MP), not a hammer session. The pre-conditions are the ones she set: no morning stiffness in the Achilles the day of the run, and no sharpening pain during. If either shows up, we convert to easy and move on. No heroics.\\n\\n**2. Does the missed week change what's realistic on Nov 15?** Honestly: 3:30 is still on the table but it's tighter now. You lost one quality week and shortened a long run, not a block. What matters most now is stacking 3–4 clean weeks of progression (long runs back to 15, 17, then 18–19) with MP work mixed in. I'd rather commit to a goal after your next long run at 13–14 mi tells us how the Achilles handles the extra time on feet. Right now the plan is still built around 3:30 — we'll calibrate honestly in 2–3 weeks.\\n\\n## Why each session\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out, flat canal, Z2. Nothing to prove.\\n- **Wed easy 6**: aerobic volume. No strides this week — leg speed can wait one more week while the Achilles settles further.\\n- **Thu short tempo**: 1.5 mi WU → 2 mi @ ~8:00/mi → 1.5 mi CD. Flat route, not the hillier one, to keep load off the tendon. Workout shoes OK; if the Achilles feels anything other than normal first-mile stiffness, downshift to easy.\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long flush, slower end of easy.\\n- **Sun long 11**: +3 mi from last Sunday, HR-capped at 150. No MP finish this week — we're earning volume back before adding intensity to the long run.\\n\\n## Flags\\n- Keep up the slow heel drops twice a day as prescribed — that's the single most important thing you're doing right now.\\n- Morning stiffness is your canary. If it reappears for more than the first few steps, email me before Thursday's workout and we'll pull it.\\n- Mileage ~32 mi — a ~6 mi bump from last week. Fine on paper, but your tendon is the governor, not the number.", "recapMarkdown": "# Weekly Recap — 2026-W39 (Mon Sep 21 – Sun Sep 27, 2026)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Mileage | 34.83 mi | 25.95 mi | 33.86 mi | +1.0 |\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\n| Total time | 5h 20m | 4h 4m | 5h 15m | +5m |\\n| Total elevation | 722 ft | 525 ft | 741 ft | -20 ft |\\n| Relative effort | 274 | 171 | 241 | +33 |\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 143 | 144 | +0 |\\n\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\n\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.2%   (4m)\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80.3%   (4h 17m)\\nZ3 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  12.1%   (39m)\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  6.4%   (21m)\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\n\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.51%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\n\\n## Run-by-run\\n\\n### Tue Sep 22 — Easy Run — 5.16 mi / 48m 4s\\n\\nPace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\n\\nSplits: 9:17/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:17/mi\\n\\nHR drift: 138.5 → 144.1 (+5.5 bpm)\\n\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\n\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\n\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\n\\nRelative effort: 34\\n\\nSimilar route: n/a\\n\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\n\\n### Wed Sep 23 — Easy Run — 6.86 mi / 1h 3m\\n\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\n\\nSplits: 9:07/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi\\n\\nHR drift: 145.1 → 150.3 (+5.2 bpm)\\n\\nTime