ing into next week feeling: Keen. The heat is the main thing, it was 25 degrees at 6 am by Sunday.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is 3:30 realistic for me from where I am now?\\\\n\\"}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W34\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-08-17T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-08-24T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-08-17\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-08-23\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "medium"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgRhVF8vWjG7XjiN1BKfF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Given the jump to 37.74 mi last week and being 14 weeks out, I'm leaning toward a slight consolidation with a small bump to roughly 36-38 mi, swapping the 800s for marathon-pace work since the intervals felt too fast. I'm starting to lay out the week with Monday rest, Tuesday and Wednesday easy mileage, and continuing to build out the rest of the schedule.\\n\\n20 gets marathon-pace work on hills, then the week fills in with easy runs, rest, and a 14-mile long run kept easy given heat concerns rather than adding MP segments. That lands around 39 miles total, a reasonable small step up from last week. For the heat question, I'll tell them to run the long run by effort and heart rate rather than chasing a set pace.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JQ1LAHRckPLTd1JLmGX5ze","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"analysis":"## Headline\\nYou're building nicely — 14 weeks out, 37.7 mi last week, long run up to 13 mi at 9:41/mi with HR behaving (144 easy, no upward trend). This week we hold mileage roughly flat (~38 mi), swap the 800s for marathon-pace work (addresses your concern that reps went too hot early), and push the long run to 14 mi by effort, not pace.\\n\\n## Why these sessions\\n- **Thursday quality — MP intervals on the hilly route**: You flagged the 800s felt too hot early. At 14 weeks out we don't need pure VO2; we need the marathon-pace engine. 4 × 1 mi @ ~8:00/mi (your 3:30 target pace) teaches pacing discipline and rhythm with low injury cost. Hills give strength without the pounding of flat speed.\\n- **Sunday long run — 14 mi easy**: Progressing +1 mi from last week. Keep it a conversational Z2 effort. In heat, HR tells the truth and pace lies.\\n- **Easy days stay easy**: Your Z1+Z2 was 81% last week — right on target. Keep Tue/Wed/Sat honest at 9:40–9:50/mi so Thursday and Sunday can land.\\n\\n## Answer to your question\\n**Should I slow the long run in the heat?** Yes — run by effort/HR, not pace. In 25°C+ at 6 am, expect to add 15–30 sec/mi versus a cool day to keep HR in Z2 (131–150). If HR drifts above 155 and won't come back, walk 30 sec at aid stops or cut it short. Pace will come back when the weather does; aerobic time on feet is what we're banking.\\n\\n## Flags\\n- Last week's relative effort (304) is climbing fast — three straight weeks of +4 mi. We hold mileage flat this week to let adaptations catch up before the next bump.\\n- Sleep averaging 6.9 hr is on the low side. If you can nudge toward 7.5 on quality-day eves, Thursday will feel better.\\n- Shin history noted — nothing bothering you now, but if anything starts whispering, tell me early.","prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W34","days":[{"date":"2026-08-17","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel/rest day. Walk if you can, otherwise fully off."},{"date":"2026-08-18","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"structure":"5 mi easy, flat loop","paceOrHr":"9:40–9:55/mi, HR in Z2 (131–150)","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"notes":"Shake-out. Properly easy — nose-breathing pace."},{"date":"2026-08-19","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":12875,"structure":"8 mi easy, canal path","paceOrHr":"9:35–9:50/mi, HR Z2","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"notes":"Steady aerobic. If HR creeps into Z3, back off pace."},{"date":"2026-08-20","dayType":"quality","run":{"type":"quality","distanceM":11265,"structure":"2 mi WU @ 9:45/mi, then 4 × 1 mi @ 8:00/mi (goal MP) with 2:00 jog recovery, 1.5 mi CD","paceOrHr":"MP reps ~8:00/mi, HR upper Z3/low Z4","shoes":"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4"},"notes":"Hillier Thursday route is fine — run reps by effort on any rises. First mile should feel controlled, not racing. If pace drifts under 7:50, pull back; this is a rhythm session, not a time trial."},{"date":"2026-08-21","dayType":"rest","notes":"Travel/rest. Full off day."},{"date":"2026-08-22","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"structure":"5 mi easy","paceOrHr":"9:45–10:00/mi, HR Z2","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"notes":"Pre-long shakeout. Keep it boring."},{"date":"2026-08-23","dayType":"long","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":22531,"structure":"14 mi easy, steady effort","paceOrHr":"Target 9:40–9:55/mi in cool conditions; in heat, add 15–30 sec/mi to hold HR ≤150","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"notes":"Fuel every 30–40 min, carry fluid, start before sunrise if you can. Back half should not be slower by more than ~15 sec/mi — if it is, we dial future long runs by HR."}]},"settingsProposalBullets":["Long-run guidance in heat: run by HR cap (≤150) rather than pace","Next quality block will keep MP focus; revisit VO2/800s later in the build"]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9119,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2192,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":385}},"diagnostics":null}	200	35773	tool_use	9119	2192	0	0	ok	\N	385
ed340751-9120-4422-9dd6-419df84a6980	2026-08-23 20:00:51.323512+00	weekly_reply	anthropic	claude-opus-4-7	dev	673db0ec-b22b-4732-9a14-3b48998783a8	\N	{"model": "claude-opus-4-7", "tools": [{"name": "submit_weekly_reply", "description": "Submit the weekly coaching analysis and structured 7-day prescribed week.", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["analysis", "prescribedWeek"], "properties": {"analysis": {"type": "string", "description": "Headline read, concerns/flags, and answers (markdown or plain prose)."}, "prescribedWeek": {"type": "object", "required": ["week", "days"], "properties": {"days": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["date", "dayType"], "properties": {"run": {"type": ["object", "null"], "required": ["type", "distanceM"], "properties": {"type": {"enum": ["easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "shoes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "paceOrHr": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "distanceM": {"type": "number"}, "structure": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "Local calendar date YYYY-MM-DD"}, "notes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "dayType": {"enum": ["rest", "easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "strength": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 7, "minItems": 7}, "week": {"type": "string", "description": "ISO week id, e.g. 2026-W43"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "safetyCallouts": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["title", "body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string"}, "title": {"type": "string"}, "severity": {"enum": ["info", "caution", "urgent"], "type": "string"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "description": "Visible safety callouts when red flags appear — escalate to professionals; do not diagnose."}, "settingsProposalBullets": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Optional soft-gate dossier/settings proposal bullets (short)."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}], "stream": true, "system": "You are Coach Cade, a running coach producing a weekly training plan. You are Coach Cade, a running coach. Use only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative. Do not sign off with your name or refer to yourself by name or in the third person unless the athlete asks who you are. Speak to the athlete in plain running language. Never use internal terms such as dossier, proposal, soft-gate, packet, recap, subjective or artifact. Say \\"what I know about you\\", \\"your weekly report\\", \\"your check-in\\" or \\"the plan\\" instead, and never tell the athlete to open a page by name. Week ids such as 2026-W43 are internal: never write them or a short form such as W43 or W43's. Name a week the way the athlete reads it: \\"this week\\", \\"next week\\", \\"the week of Oct 19\\", \\"Oct 19 – 25\\" or \\"4 weeks out from the race\\". Safety callouts: - Never diagnose injury, illness, or medical conditions; do not prescribe treatment. - Coach running from the athlete's volunteered context and Tempo-derived training data. - When red flags appear (pain that worsens, chest pain, dizziness, sudden injury, illness), emit safetyCallouts and urge a qualified professional. - Each callout needs a short title, athlete-facing body (escalate, do not diagnose), and optional severity (info|caution|urgent). - Keep each callout body under 600 characters: one or two short paragraphs. - Keep the training plan/reply conservative when callouts are present. Think it through first, then call the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer. Do not write the answer as plain text.", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Reviewed week (already happened): 2026-W34\\nPlan week ISO label: 2026-W35\\nPlan week Monday (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-08-24\\nprescribedWeek.days must use these exact dates Mon–Sun: 2026-08-24, 2026-08-25, 2026-08-26, 2026-08-27, 2026-08-28, 2026-08-29, 2026-08-30\\nPrescribe one coherent week of running training for this athlete.\\nCall the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer.\\nInclude analysis with headline, concerns/flags, and answers.\\nWhen red flags appear, populate safetyCallouts (escalate; do not diagnose).\\nModel packet (redacted; no identity PII or GPS):\\n{\\"dossier\\":{\\"versionId\\":2,\\"body\\":\\"# About you\\\\n\\\\n## Stance\\\\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Goal\\\\nLakeshore Marathon on Sun Nov 15, your fourth marathon. Target 3:30. Your current best is 3:41 from two years ago.\\\\n\\\\n## Schedule\\\\nYou run five days a week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are fixed rest days because of work travel and cannot move. Weekday runs are early, around 6 am, up to an hour. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Total 6 to 7 hours a week, more on long-run weeks. You travel for work roughly one week in six.\\\\n\\\\n## Running history\\\\nThree marathons done, best 3:41. You eased off in June, then built back to about 30 miles a week through July. Recent long run was about 10.8 miles at roughly 9:47/mi; easy runs sit near 9:20 to 9:40/mi.\\\\n\\\\n## Injuries and constraints\\\\nNothing bothering you now. You had shin splints in your first marathon block, so you prefer a careful ramp. Monday and Friday rest days are non-negotiable.\\\\n\\\\n## Preferences\\\\nFlat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, with a hillier route on Thursdays. Long run on Sunday. You want to know why each session is in the plan. Happy to work hard on quality days, but easy days must stay properly easy. Imperial units.\\\\n\\\\n## Shoes\\\\nBrooks Ghost 16 for daily miles. Saucony Endorphin Speed 4 for workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## Heart rate zones\\\\nCustom zones. Z1 112-131, Z2 131-150, Z3 150-164, Z4 164-177, Z5 177-188.\\\\n\\\\n## Current status\\\\nHealthy, about 30 miles per week, 5 runs per week, roughly 14 weeks out from race day.\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W34)\\\\n\\\\n- Long-run guidance in heat: run by HR cap (≤150) rather than pace\\\\n- Next quality block will keep MP focus; revisit VO2/800s later in the build\\\\n\\"},\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W34 (Mon Aug 17 – Sun Aug 23, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 42.55 mi | 37.74 mi | 35.36 mi | +7.2 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 6h 44m | 5h 57m | 5h 40m | +1h 4m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 988 ft | 745 ft | 720 ft | +268 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 342 | 304 | 272 | +70 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.1%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80.9%   (5h 27m)\\\\nZ3 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  11.2%   (45m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  6.8%   (28m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **82.01%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Aug 18 — Easy Run — 6.17 mi / 59m 43s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:38/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139 → 144.2 (+5.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1.7% · Z2 98.3% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑82 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 42\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Aug 19 — Easy Run — 7.89 mi / 1h 15m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:35/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:31/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.6 → 149.5 (+3.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 96% · Z3 4% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑161 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 53\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 20 — Tempo Run — 8.14 mi / 1h 11m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 151 (80.3% max)  ·  Max HR 173  ·  Cad 352 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:43/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:54/mi / 7:47/mi / 7:39/mi / 7:45/mi / 7:42/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:54/mi / 9:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 136.1 → 140.3 (+4.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.8% · Z2 53.3% · Z3 5.6% · Z4 38.3% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑223 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 108\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 22 — Easy Run — 5.18 mi / 50m 48s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 345 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:52/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:44/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.2 → 143.9 (+5.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2% · Z2 98% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 36\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 23 — Long Run — 15.17 mi / 2h 26m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144 → 151.3 (+7.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 73.6% · Z3 26.1% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑420 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 103\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 23 — 15.17 mi / 2h 26m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 144 → 151.3 (+7.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:36/mi vs front 9:35/mi (vs front half; Δ -1s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 6.4 hrs (range 5.5–7.2)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Too tired Wednesday evening.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: High. Deadline at work, late nights Tuesday and Wednesday.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Tired more than sore. Saturday's easy run felt like work.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Hoping the next week eases off a bit.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. My schedule gets tight when I travel for work. How should I handle missed runs?\\\\n\\",\\"thread\\":[],\\"attachments\\":[],\\"week\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W34\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-08-17T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-08-24T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"673db0ec-b22b-4732-9a14-3b48998783a8\\"},\\"recentHistory\\":[{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W33\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"89597b69-9acd-416c-a37d-3865024c449b\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W33 (Mon Aug 10 – Sun Aug 16, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 37.74 mi | 35.77 mi | 33.43 mi | +4.3 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 57m | 5h 43m | 5h 25m | +32m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 745 ft | 764 ft | 664 ft | +81 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 304 | 289 | 244 | +60 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.3%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  79.8%   (4h 46m)\\\\nZ3 █████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  13.3%   (48m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  5.3%   (19m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0.3%   (1m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.07%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Aug 11 — Easy Run — 4.93 mi / 47m 57s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:44/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:44/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 144.5 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Aug 12 — Easy Run — 7.92 mi / 1h 16m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:38/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:38/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.3 → 149.5 (+4.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 90.2% · Z3 9.8% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑138 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 53\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 13 — Interval Run — 6.95 mi / 59m 12s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:32/mi  ·  Avg HR 154 (81.9% max)  ·  Max HR 180  ·  Cad 350 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:43/mi / 9:41/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:36/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:41/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:51/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.8 → 143.5 (+3.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.4% · Z2 40% · Z3 22.8% · Z4 32.1% · Z5 1.7%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑92 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 95\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 8/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 15 — Easy Run — 4.92 mi / 48m 22s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:44/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:54/mi / 9:43/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.2 → 143.9 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑108 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 16 — Long Run — 13.03 mi / 2h 6m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 155  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:39/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:41/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.3 → 151.2 (+6.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.4% · Z2 78.4% · Z3 21.2% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑305 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 88\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 16 — 13.03 mi / 2h 6m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 144.3 → 151.2 (+6.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:39/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:41/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:38/mi vs front 9:38/mi (vs front half; Δ -1s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:50/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi ▁▁▅█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 9.89 mi → 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 6.9 hrs (range 6–7.6)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: All fine. Sunday was a slog in the humidity but nothing hurts.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Good. A bit worried the 800s were too fast early on.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Should I slow the long run down when it is this hot, or hold the pace?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nStrong week of Aug 3–9: 35.8 mi, long run out to 12.1 mi, and 83% of time in Z1+Z2 — exactly the aerobic base we want 14 weeks out. Thursday's tempo was quality work and the Sunday long run was steady with modest drift. Nice job.\\\\n\\\\nBecause mileage jumped ~10% and relative effort (289) was well above your 3-week average (217), the week of Aug 10–16 is a **consolidation week at the same volume** — no mileage bump. We'll sharpen one quality session, keep easy days properly easy (especially in the heat), and then push the long run again the following week.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags / things I'm watching\\\\n- **Heat**: 25°C at 6 am on Sunday is real. Z3 creep on Wed and Sun long run (both ~17–20% Z3) is likely heat as much as effort. Start the easy days 10–15 sec/mi slower when it's muggy and let HR, not pace, lead.\\\\n- **Thursday tempo pace**: 7:45–7:52/mi is faster than goal marathon pace (3:30 ≈ 8:00/mi) and closer to half-marathon effort. Fine occasionally, but this week I want you to practice *marathon* pace so your body learns that gear.\\\\n- **Shin splint history**: nothing flaring now, but we hold volume this week rather than stacking another jump on top of last week's +4.3 mi.\\\\n- **Strength**: 1 of 2 done. Try to get both in — hips/calves/feet are your shin insurance.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — is 3:30 realistic?\\\\nHonest answer: it's a stretch but not unreasonable. 3:30 is ~8:00/mi. Your easy runs at 9:20–9:40 and HR ~144 (76% max) suggest aerobic fitness is building nicely, and your tempo splits at 7:45–7:52 show you have the raw speed. The gap from a 3:41 PR to 3:30 is 11 minutes, which is big but doable in 14 weeks given you're healthy and ramping sensibly. I'd call it a stretch \\\\\\"A\\\\\\" goal, with 3:35 as a very realistic \\\\\\"B\\\\\\". We'll know more after a couple of MP-specific long runs in September — I'll re-benchmark then.\\\\n\\\\n## Why each session this week\\\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out after Sunday's 12, pure Z2.\\\\n- **Wed easy 6 + strides**: aerobic volume plus 6×20s strides to keep leg turnover sharp without taxing you.\\\\n- **Thu quality — MP intervals on your hilly route**: 4 × 1 mi at goal marathon pace (8:00/mi) with 90s jog. Shorter and more pace-specific than last week's tempo. Hills on recoveries are fine.\\\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long-run flush, keep it slow.\\\\n- **Sun long 12 with MP finish**: same distance as last week, but finish the last 2 miles at ~8:00/mi. Teaches you to close strong on tired legs.\\\\n\\\\nTotal ~35 mi, same as last week. We'll bump to ~37–38 the week after.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-10\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest day. Optional mobility/foam roll — calves and hips.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Optional: 10 min mobility (ankles, hips)\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30–9:50/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi easy, conversational. Let HR lead in heat — aim mid-Z2 (138–148).\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-11\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake-out after Sunday long run. Keep it truly easy.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30–9:50/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi easy + 6×20s strides on flat with full walk recovery after the run. Strides are relaxed, controlled turnover — not sprints.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-12\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 1: hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work (30–40 min)\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP reps 7:55–8:05/mi; warm-up/cool-down 9:40–10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi total on the hilly route. 1.5 mi warm-up → 4 × 1 mi at goal marathon pace (8:00/mi) with 90s easy jog between → 1.5 mi cool-down. If a rep rolls uphill, hold effort not pace. Target avg HR for reps: upper Z3 / low Z4.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-13\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shorter and more marathon-specific than last week's tempo. If legs feel heavy after 3 reps, stop at 3 — do not grind.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-14\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest day. Hydrate well, eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts today.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40–10:00/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi very easy on flat canal path. If it's hot, go even slower.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-15\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 2 (short, 20–25 min): core + calves. Skip if legs are flat.\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Easy 9:40–9:55/mi; MP close 7:55–8:05/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":19312,\\"structure\\":\\"12 mi: first 10 mi easy (Z2), last 2 mi at goal MP (~8:00/mi). Start out ~9:50/mi, let HR settle, then roll into MP for the final 2. Carry fluids and start before sunrise if possible.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-16\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Practice marathon fueling: a gel every 30–35 min. Bail on the MP finish if HR is drifting into Z4 — heat trumps pace targets.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W33\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W32\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"94b17220-2c8a-4ce5-925e-991f6cf5d703\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W32 (Mon Aug 3 – Sun Aug 9, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 35.77 mi | 32.56 mi | 31.50 mi | +4.3 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 43m | 5h 19m | 5h 10m | +33m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 764 ft | 650 ft | 596 ft | +168 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 289 | 223 | 217 | +72 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.2%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 █████████████████████████████░░░░░░  81.9%   (4h 41m)\\\\nZ3 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  11.2%   (38m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  5.8%   (20m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **83.01%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Aug 4 — Easy Run — 4.88 mi / 47m 33s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:44/mi  ·  Avg HR 141 (75% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:38/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:46/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.1 → 143.1 (+5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.2% · Z2 96.8% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑75 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Aug 5 — Easy Run — 6.94 mi / 1h 7m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:43/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:41/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.3 → 150.7 (+5.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 82.9% · Z3 17.1% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑190 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 47\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 6 — Tempo Run — 6.87 mi / 1h 2m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:02/mi  ·  Avg HR 150 (79.8% max)  ·  Max HR 174  ·  Cad 351 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:54/mi / 9:46/mi / 7:50/mi / 7:52/mi / 7:45/mi / 9:59/mi / 9:57/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 136.2 → 139.7 (+3.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.4% · Z2 59% · Z3 6.4% · Z4 32.2% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑157 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 93\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 8 — Easy Run — 4.99 mi / 49m 9s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:51/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:52/mi / 9:49/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:52/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.9 → 144.1 (+5.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1% · Z2 99% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑154 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 9 — Long Run — 12.08 mi / 1h 57m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:43/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:31/mi / 9:31/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:49/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.9 → 151.3 (+7.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.4% · Z2 80.1% · Z3 19.5% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑187 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 82\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 9 — 12.08 mi / 1h 57m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:43/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 143.9 → 151.3 (+7.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:31/mi / 9:31/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:49/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:40/mi vs front 9:38/mi (vs front half; Δ -2s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:54/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi ▁▃▃█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 143 → 144 → 144 → 144 █▁▁▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.07 mi → 9.89 mi → 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi ▁▁▃█\\\\n\\\\n## Notable\\\\n\\\\n- Relative effort (289) ≥ 1.3× 3-wk avg (217) — possible overload\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.1 hrs (range 6.3–7.8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Skipped Friday, travelled for work.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate. Normal work week.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Fine. Legs a bit heavy on Thursday after the tempo.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Keen. The heat is the main thing, it was 25 degrees at 6 am by Sunday.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is 3:30 realistic for me from where I am now?\\\\n\\"}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W35\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-08-24T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-08-31T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-08-24\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-08-30\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "medium"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgRhYNm9PoE4fwVYALPte","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Given the big jump last week and signs of fatigue, I'm scaling back to a down week around 35-37 miles, trimming the long run to roughly 12-13 miles, and keeping just one quality session focused on marathon pace while skipping VO2 work.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Tegz1BM1jzihcQAi9W3tHM","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"analysis":"## Headline\\nBig week — 42.5 mi, long run out to 15.2, and still 82% in Z1+Z2. Impressive work, especially stacked on top of a tough stretch at work (late nights, 6.4 hrs sleep, Saturday felt like a slog). But that's also a +7 mi jump over your 3-week average and relative effort climbed from 272 to 342. You asked for an easier week — you've earned it, and the training calls for it. This week of Aug 24–30 is a planned cutback: ~36 mi, long run back to 12, and one marathon-pace session that's crisp but short. We'll push again next week from a fresher starting point.\\n\\n## Flags / things I'm watching\\n- **Load spike + low sleep + high stress**: classic combo that precedes a niggle, especially with your shin-splint history. Nothing hurts yet, so we take the cutback *now* rather than after a problem shows up.\\n- **Long-run HR drift**: 144 → 151 over 15 miles on Sunday is on the higher side — the heat is biting. Keep the HR cap of 150 on long runs for now; let pace fall where it does.\\n- **Thursday tempo**: 7:39–7:47/mi is faster than goal MP (8:00/mi). You have the top-end gear; this week I want you back on honest MP so the pace feels automatic.\\n- **Strength**: 1 of 2 again. On a down week with less fatigue, two short sessions are very doable.\\n\\n## Your question — handling missed runs when you travel\\nSimple rules, in priority order:\\n1. **Never skip the long run** if you can help it. If travel kills Sunday, move it to Saturday or do it on the road the day you fly.\\n2. **Protect one quality session per week**. If the Thursday workout is at risk, shift it to Wednesday or Tuesday and make the other day easy.\\n3. **Easy miles are the most droppable.** If you lose 1–2 easy days to travel, don't try to cram them in — just land on the plane rested and resume.\\n4. **Don't stack a missed long run onto the next week.** Pick up where the plan is, don't try to \\"make up\\" miles — that's how injuries happen.\\n5. Give me a heads-up on travel weeks in your check-in and I'll shape the plan around the fixed slots you'll have.\\n\\n## Why each session this week\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out, pure Z2.\\n- **Wed easy 7 + strides**: aerobic volume plus 6×20s strides for leg turnover without stress.\\n- **Thu quality — 3 × 1 mi at MP**: shorter rep set on the hilly route. Goal is to groove 8:00/mi, not to grind.\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long flush.\\n- **Sun long 12, HR-capped**: distance comes down intentionally. Run by HR (≤150), let pace be whatever it is. No MP finish this week — the point is recovery adaptation.\\n\\nTotal ~36 mi (down from 42.5). Next week we rebuild toward ~40 with an MP long run.","prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W35","days":[{"date":"2026-08-24","dayType":"rest","notes":"Fixed rest. Prioritize sleep tonight — you're down on it. 10 min easy mobility if you feel like moving.","strength":"Optional mobility: ankles, hips, calves (10 min)"},{"date":"2026-08-25","dayType":"easy","notes":"Shake-out. Keep it genuinely easy — no pushing the pace even if you feel fresh.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"paceOrHr":"9:40–10:00/mi, Z2 (HR 138–148)","structure":"5 mi conversational on the canal path. Let HR lead if it's humid.","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"}},{"date":"2026-08-26","dayType":"easy","notes":"Try for strength tonight — the week is lighter on purpose to let you fit it in.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":11265,"paceOrHr":"9:30–9:50/mi, Z2","structure":"7 mi easy + 6×20s strides on flat with full walk recovery after the run. Strides are relaxed, controlled turnover — not sprints.","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"strength":"Strength session 1 (30–40 min): hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work"},{"date":"2026-08-27","dayType":"quality","notes":"Short and sharp. If the 2nd rep is already a struggle, pull the plug after 2 — this is a cutback week and nothing is proved by grinding.","run":{"type":"quality","distanceM":11265,"paceOrHr":"MP reps 7:55–8:05/mi; WU/CD 9:40–10:00/mi","structure":"7 mi total on the hilly route. 2 mi warm-up → 3 × 1 mi @ goal MP (8:00/mi) with 90s easy jog between → 1.5 mi cool-down. Hold effort on uphill reps, don't force pace.","shoes":"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4"}},{"date":"2026-08-28","dayType":"rest","notes":"Fixed rest. Hydrate and eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts today."},{"date":"2026-08-29","dayType":"easy","notes":"Pre-long flush. Slower is better here.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"paceOrHr":"9:45–10:05/mi, Z2","structure":"5 mi very easy on flat canal path.","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"strength":"Strength session 2 (20–25 min): core + calves. Skip if legs are flat."},{"date":"2026-08-30","dayType":"long","notes":"Cutback long run. HR cap, no MP work. Fuel every 30–35 min with a gel to keep practicing race fueling. Start before sunrise if it's going to be warm.","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":19312,"paceOrHr":"HR ≤150 (mid-Z2); pace will likely land 9:40–9:55/mi","structure":"12 mi steady, HR-capped. If HR drifts above 150, walk 30s and resume slower. No fast finish this week — this is recovery-oriented aerobic volume.","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"}}]},"safetyCallouts":[{"title":"Load + sleep combo — watch the shins","body":"You've had a few weeks of climbing mileage, lower sleep (6.4 hrs avg), and high work stress. Nothing is hurting now, which is the right time to pull back — not after. If you notice shin tenderness, aching along the bone, or any pain that worsens during or after a run, pause running and check in with a sports physio or doctor rather than training through it. Don't try to make up this week's miles later.","severity":"caution"}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":14423,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3076,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":442}},"diagnostics":null}	200	50951	tool_use	14423	3076	0	0	ok	\N	442
1856dd82-57b5-47af-9e36-e00a2b21cddb	2026-08-30 20:00:43.080851+00	weekly_reply	anthropic	claude-opus-4-7	dev	cc5d18d4-c308-481b-b011-dd3c99e03ba0	\N	{"model": "claude-opus-4-7", "tools": [{"name": "submit_weekly_reply", "description": "Submit the weekly coaching analysis and structured 7-day prescribed week.", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["analysis", "prescribedWeek"], "properties": {"analysis": {"type": "string", "description": "Headline read, concerns/flags, and answers (markdown or plain prose)."}, "prescribedWeek": {"type": "object", "required": ["week", "days"], "properties": {"days": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["date", "dayType"], "properties": {"run": {"type": ["object", "null"], "required": ["type", "distanceM"], "properties": {"type": {"enum": ["easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "shoes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "paceOrHr": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "distanceM": {"type": "number"}, "structure": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "Local calendar date YYYY-MM-DD"}, "notes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "dayType": {"enum": ["rest", "easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "strength": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 7, "minItems": 7}, "week": {"type": "string", "description": "ISO week id, e.g. 2026-W43"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "safetyCallouts": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["title", "body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string"}, "title": {"type": "string"}, "severity": {"enum": ["info", "caution", "urgent"], "type": "string"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "description": "Visible safety callouts when red flags appear — escalate to professionals; do not diagnose."}, "settingsProposalBullets": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Optional soft-gate dossier/settings proposal bullets (short)."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}], "stream": true, "system": "You are Coach Cade, a running coach producing a weekly training plan. You are Coach Cade, a running coach. Use only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative. Do not sign off with your name or refer to yourself by name or in the third person unless the athlete asks who you are. Speak to the athlete in plain running language. Never use internal terms such as dossier, proposal, soft-gate, packet, recap, subjective or artifact. Say \\"what I know about you\\", \\"your weekly report\\", \\"your check-in\\" or \\"the plan\\" instead, and never tell the athlete to open a page by name. Week ids such as 2026-W43 are internal: never write them or a short form such as W43 or W43's. Name a week the way the athlete reads it: \\"this week\\", \\"next week\\", \\"the week of Oct 19\\", \\"Oct 19 – 25\\" or \\"4 weeks out from the race\\". Safety callouts: - Never diagnose injury, illness, or medical conditions; do not prescribe treatment. - Coach running from the athlete's volunteered context and Tempo-derived training data. - When red flags appear (pain that worsens, chest pain, dizziness, sudden injury, illness), emit safetyCallouts and urge a qualified professional. - Each callout needs a short title, athlete-facing body (escalate, do not diagnose), and optional severity (info|caution|urgent). - Keep each callout body under 600 characters: one or two short paragraphs. - Keep the training plan/reply conservative when callouts are present. Think it through first, then call the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer. Do not write the answer as plain text.", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Reviewed week (already happened): 2026-W35\\nPlan week ISO label: 2026-W36\\nPlan week Monday (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-08-31\\nprescribedWeek.days must use these exact dates Mon–Sun: 2026-08-31, 2026-09-01, 2026-09-02, 2026-09-03, 2026-09-04, 2026-09-05, 2026-09-06\\nPrescribe one coherent week of running training for this athlete.\\nCall the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer.\\nInclude analysis with headline, concerns/flags, and answers.\\nWhen red flags appear, populate safetyCallouts (escalate; do not diagnose).\\nModel packet (redacted; no identity PII or GPS):\\n{\\"dossier\\":{\\"versionId\\":2,\\"body\\":\\"# About you\\\\n\\\\n## Stance\\\\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Goal\\\\nLakeshore Marathon on Sun Nov 15, your fourth marathon. Target 3:30. Your current best is 3:41 from two years ago.\\\\n\\\\n## Schedule\\\\nYou run five days a week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are fixed rest days because of work travel and cannot move. Weekday runs are early, around 6 am, up to an hour. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Total 6 to 7 hours a week, more on long-run weeks. You travel for work roughly one week in six.\\\\n\\\\n## Running history\\\\nThree marathons done, best 3:41. You eased off in June, then built back to about 30 miles a week through July. Recent long run was about 10.8 miles at roughly 9:47/mi; easy runs sit near 9:20 to 9:40/mi.\\\\n\\\\n## Injuries and constraints\\\\nNothing bothering you now. You had shin splints in your first marathon block, so you prefer a careful ramp. Monday and Friday rest days are non-negotiable.\\\\n\\\\n## Preferences\\\\nFlat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, with a hillier route on Thursdays. Long run on Sunday. You want to know why each session is in the plan. Happy to work hard on quality days, but easy days must stay properly easy. Imperial units.\\\\n\\\\n## Shoes\\\\nBrooks Ghost 16 for daily miles. Saucony Endorphin Speed 4 for workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## Heart rate zones\\\\nCustom zones. Z1 112-131, Z2 131-150, Z3 150-164, Z4 164-177, Z5 177-188.\\\\n\\\\n## Current status\\\\nHealthy, about 30 miles per week, 5 runs per week, roughly 14 weeks out from race day.\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W34)\\\\n\\\\n- Long-run guidance in heat: run by HR cap (≤150) rather than pace\\\\n- Next quality block will keep MP focus; revisit VO2/800s later in the build\\\\n\\"},\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W35 (Mon Aug 24 – Sun Aug 30, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 33.72 mi | 42.55 mi | 38.69 mi | -5.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 18m | 6h 44m | 6h 8m | -49m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 587 ft | 988 ft | 832 ft | -245 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 271 | 342 | 312 | -41 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80%   (4h 15m)\\\\nZ3 ██████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  15.9%   (51m)\\\\nZ4 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  2.7%   (9m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.45%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Aug 25 — Easy Run — 5.04 mi / 48m 15s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:35/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:33/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 143.9 (+5.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑105 ft\