143.5 → 156.9 (+13.4 bpm) ⚠ above target (target ≤10 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 73% · Z3 19.1% · Z4 7.6% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑397 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 105\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 6 — 16.10 mi / 2h 29m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 149  ·  Drift: 143.5 → 156.9 (+13.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 7:58/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:07/mi vs front 9:25/mi (faster than front half by 18s/mi) ✓ negative split\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? Yes (paced up or HR above easy cap)\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi ▁▁▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi ▃▅▁█\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.2 hrs (range 6.5–7.9)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low to moderate.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Legs a little heavy after the long run, otherwise good.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Confident. Marathon pace felt controlled for the first time.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is it worth trying a gel on the long run next week, or keep it simple?\\\\n\\",\\"thread\\":[],\\"attachments\\":[],\\"week\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W36\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-08-31T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-09-07T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"140f5949-e890-44f8-9296-6ffd441831a4\\"},\\"recentHistory\\":[{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W35\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"cc5d18d4-c308-481b-b011-dd3c99e03ba0\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W35 (Mon Aug 24 – Sun Aug 30, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 33.72 mi | 42.55 mi | 38.69 mi | -5.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 18m | 6h 44m | 6h 8m | -49m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 587 ft | 988 ft | 832 ft | -245 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 271 | 342 | 312 | -41 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80%   (4h 15m)\\\\nZ3 ██████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  15.9%   (51m)\\\\nZ4 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  2.7%   (9m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.45%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Aug 25 — Easy Run — 5.04 mi / 48m 15s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:35/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:33/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 143.9 (+5.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑105 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Aug 26 — Easy Run — 6.92 mi / 1h 5m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:30/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.2 → 150 (+4.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 92.4% · Z3 7.6% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑108 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 46\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 27 — Interval Run — 5.99 mi / 52m 53s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 153 (80.9% max)  ·  Max HR 176  ·  Cad 349 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:43/mi / 9:39/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:41/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:34/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:36/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 140.2 → 146.3 (+6.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.8% · Z2 35.7% · Z3 44.4% · Z4 16.1% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑108 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 85\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 29 — Easy Run — 4.90 mi / 47m 18s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:39/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:36/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.9 → 144.4 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑79 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 30 — Long Run — 10.86 mi / 1h 44m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 155  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:30/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143 → 151.6 (+8.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.5% · Z2 78.4% · Z3 21.2% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑187 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 73\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 30 — 10.86 mi / 1h 44m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 143 → 151.6 (+8.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:30/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:31/mi vs front 9:28/mi (vs front half; Δ -3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi ▁▃▃█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi ▃▅█▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.4 hrs (range 6.8–8.1)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low. Deadline done.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Best I've felt in a month. Legs have some bounce again.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Ready to go again.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. What should I be eating and drinking on the long runs? I've mostly gone without so far.\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nBig week — 42.5 mi, long run out to 15.2, and still 82% in Z1+Z2. Impressive work, especially stacked on top of a tough stretch at work (late nights, 6.4 hrs sleep, Saturday felt like a slog). But that's also a +7 mi jump over your 3-week average and relative effort climbed from 272 to 342. You asked for an easier week — you've earned it, and the training calls for it. This week of Aug 24–30 is a planned cutback: ~36 mi, long run back to 12, and one marathon-pace session that's crisp but short. We'll push again next week from a fresher starting point.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags / things I'm watching\\\\n- **Load spike + low sleep + high stress**: classic combo that precedes a niggle, especially with your shin-splint history. Nothing hurts yet, so we take the cutback *now* rather than after a problem shows up.\\\\n- **Long-run HR drift**: 144 → 151 over 15 miles on Sunday is on the higher side — the heat is biting. Keep the HR cap of 150 on long runs for now; let pace fall where it does.\\\\n- **Thursday tempo**: 7:39–7:47/mi is faster than goal MP (8:00/mi). You have the top-end gear; this week I want you back on honest MP so the pace feels automatic.\\\\n- **Strength**: 1 of 2 again. On a down week with less fatigue, two short sessions are very doable.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — handling missed runs when you travel\\\\nSimple rules, in priority order:\\\\n1. **Never skip the long run** if you can help it. If travel kills Sunday, move it to Saturday or do it on the road the day you fly.\\\\n2. **Protect one quality session per week**. If the Thursday workout is at risk, shift it to Wednesday or Tuesday and make the other day easy.\\\\n3. **Easy miles are the most droppable.** If you lose 1–2 easy days to travel, don't try to cram them in — just land on the plane rested and resume.\\\\n4. **Don't stack a missed long run onto the next week.** Pick up where the plan is, don't try to \\\\\\"make up\\\\\\" miles — that's how injuries happen.\\\\n5. Give me a heads-up on travel weeks in your check-in and I'll shape the plan around the fixed slots you'll have.\\\\n\\\\n## Why each session this week\\\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out, pure Z2.\\\\n- **Wed easy 7 + strides**: aerobic volume plus 6×20s strides for leg turnover without stress.\\\\n- **Thu quality — 3 × 1 mi at MP**: shorter rep set on the hilly route. Goal is to groove 8:00/mi, not to grind.\\\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long flush.\\\\n- **Sun long 12, HR-capped**: distance comes down intentionally. Run by HR (≤150), let pace be whatever it is. No MP finish this week — the point is recovery adaptation.\\\\n\\\\nTotal ~36 mi (down from 42.5). Next week we rebuild toward ~40 with an MP long run.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-24\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Prioritize sleep tonight — you're down on it. 10 min easy mobility if you feel like moving.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Optional mobility: ankles, hips, calves (10 min)\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40–10:00/mi, Z2 (HR 138–148)\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi conversational on the canal path. Let HR lead if it's humid.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-25\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake-out. Keep it genuinely easy — no pushing the pace even if you feel fresh.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30–9:50/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi easy + 6×20s strides on flat with full walk recovery after the run. Strides are relaxed, controlled turnover — not sprints.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-26\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Try for strength tonight — the week is lighter on purpose to let you fit it in.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 1 (30–40 min): hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP reps 7:55–8:05/mi; WU/CD 9:40–10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi total on the hilly route. 2 mi warm-up → 3 × 1 mi @ goal MP (8:00/mi) with 90s easy jog between → 1.5 mi cool-down. Hold effort on uphill reps, don't force pace.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-27\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Short and sharp. If the 2nd rep is already a struggle, pull the plug after 2 — this is a cutback week and nothing is proved by grinding.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-28\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Hydrate and eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts today.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:05/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi very easy on flat canal path.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-29\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Pre-long flush. Slower is better here.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 2 (20–25 min): core + calves. Skip if legs are flat.\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"HR ≤150 (mid-Z2); pace will likely land 9:40–9:55/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":19312,\\"structure\\":\\"12 mi steady, HR-capped. If HR drifts above 150, walk 30s and resume slower. No fast finish this week — this is recovery-oriented aerobic volume.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-30\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Cutback long run. HR cap, no MP work. Fuel every 30–35 min with a gel to keep practicing race fueling. Start before sunrise if it's going to be warm.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W35\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W34\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"673db0ec-b22b-4732-9a14-3b48998783a8\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W34 (Mon Aug 17 – Sun Aug 23, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 42.55 mi | 37.74 mi | 35.36 mi | +7.2 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 6h 44m | 5h 57m | 5h 40m | +1h 4m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 988 ft | 745 ft | 720 ft | +268 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 342 | 304 | 272 | +70 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.1%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80.9%   (5h 27m)\\\\nZ3 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  11.2%   (45m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  6.8%   (28m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **82.01%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Aug 18 — Easy Run — 6.17 mi / 59m 43s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:38/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139 → 144.2 (+5.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1.7% · Z2 98.3% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑82 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 42\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Aug 19 — Easy Run — 7.89 mi / 1h 15m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:35/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:31/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.6 → 149.5 (+3.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 96% · Z3 4% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑161 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 53\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 20 — Tempo Run — 8.14 mi / 1h 11m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 151 (80.3% max)  ·  Max HR 173  ·  Cad 352 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:43/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:54/mi / 7:47/mi / 7:39/mi / 7:45/mi / 7:42/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:54/mi / 9:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 136.1 → 140.3 (+4.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.8% · Z2 53.3% · Z3 5.6% · Z4 38.3% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑223 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 108\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 22 — Easy Run — 5.18 mi / 50m 48s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 345 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:52/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:44/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.2 → 143.9 (+5.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2% · Z2 98% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 36\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 23 — Long Run — 15.17 mi / 2h 26m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144 → 151.3 (+7.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 73.6% · Z3 26.1% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑420 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 103\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 23 — 15.17 mi / 2h 26m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 144 → 151.3 (+7.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:36/mi vs front 9:35/mi (vs front half; Δ -1s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 6.4 hrs (range 5.5–7.2)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Too tired Wednesday evening.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: High. Deadline at work, late nights Tuesday and Wednesday.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Tired more than sore. Saturday's easy run felt like work.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Hoping the next week eases off a bit.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. My schedule gets tight when I travel for work. How should I handle missed runs?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nYou're building nicely — 14 weeks out, 37.7 mi last week, long run up to 13 mi at 9:41/mi with HR behaving (144 easy, no upward trend). This week we hold mileage roughly flat (~38 mi), swap the 800s for marathon-pace work (addresses your concern that reps went too hot early), and push the long run to 14 mi by effort, not pace.\\\\n\\\\n## Why these sessions\\\\n- **Thursday quality — MP intervals on the hilly route**: You flagged the 800s felt too hot early. At 14 weeks out we don't need pure VO2; we need the marathon-pace engine. 4 × 1 mi @ ~8:00/mi (your 3:30 target pace) teaches pacing discipline and rhythm with low injury cost. Hills give strength without the pounding of flat speed.\\\\n- **Sunday long run — 14 mi easy**: Progressing +1 mi from last week. Keep it a conversational Z2 effort. In heat, HR tells the truth and pace lies.\\\\n- **Easy days stay easy**: Your Z1+Z2 was 81% last week — right on target. Keep Tue/Wed/Sat honest at 9:40–9:50/mi so Thursday and Sunday can land.\\\\n\\\\n## Answer to your question\\\\n**Should I slow the long run in the heat?** Yes — run by effort/HR, not pace. In 25°C+ at 6 am, expect to add 15–30 sec/mi versus a cool day to keep HR in Z2 (131–150). If HR drifts above 155 and won't come back, walk 30 sec at aid stops or cut it short. Pace will come back when the weather does; aerobic time on feet is what we're banking.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags\\\\n- Last week's relative effort (304) is climbing fast — three straight weeks of +4 mi. We hold mileage flat this week to let adaptations catch up before the next bump.\\\\n- Sleep averaging 6.9 hr is on the low side. If you can nudge toward 7.5 on quality-day eves, Thursday will feel better.\\\\n- Shin history noted — nothing bothering you now, but if anything starts whispering, tell me early.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-17\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel/rest day. Walk if you can, otherwise fully off.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40–9:55/mi, HR in Z2 (131–150)\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi easy, flat loop\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-18\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake-out. Properly easy — nose-breathing pace.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:35–9:50/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi easy, canal path\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-19\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Steady aerobic. If HR creeps into Z3, back off pace.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP reps ~8:00/mi, HR upper Z3/low Z4\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"2 mi WU @ 9:45/mi, then 4 × 1 mi @ 8:00/mi (goal MP) with 2:00 jog recovery, 1.5 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-20\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Hillier Thursday route is fine — run reps by effort on any rises. First mile should feel controlled, not racing. If pace drifts under 7:50, pull back; this is a rhythm session, not a time trial.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-21\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel/rest. Full off day.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:00/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-22\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Pre-long shakeout. Keep it boring.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Target 9:40–9:55/mi in cool conditions; in heat, add 15–30 sec/mi to hold HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":22531,\\"structure\\":\\"14 mi easy, steady effort\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-23\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fuel every 30–40 min, carry fluid, start before sunrise if you can. Back half should not be slower by more than ~15 sec/mi — if it is, we dial future long runs by HR.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W34\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W33\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"89597b69-9acd-416c-a37d-3865024c449b\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W33 (Mon Aug 10 – Sun Aug 16, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 37.74 mi | 35.77 mi | 33.43 mi | +4.3 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 57m | 5h 43m | 5h 25m | +32m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 745 ft | 764 ft | 664 ft | +81 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 304 | 289 | 244 | +60 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.3%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  79.8%   (4h 46m)\\\\nZ3 █████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  13.3%   (48m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  5.3%   (19m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0.3%   (1m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.07%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Aug 11 — Easy Run — 4.93 mi / 47m 57s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:44/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:44/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 144.5 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Aug 12 — Easy Run — 7.92 mi / 1h 16m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:38/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:38/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.3 → 149.5 (+4.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 90.2% · Z3 9.8% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑138 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 53\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 13 — Interval Run — 6.95 mi / 59m 12s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:32/mi  ·  Avg HR 154 (81.9% max)  ·  Max HR 180  ·  Cad 350 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:43/mi / 9:41/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:36/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:41/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:51/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.8 → 143.5 (+3.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.4% · Z2 40% · Z3 22.8% · Z4 32.1% · Z5 1.7%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑92 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 95\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 8/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 15 — Easy Run — 4.92 mi / 48m 22s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:44/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:54/mi / 9:43/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.2 → 143.9 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑108 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 16 — Long Run — 13.03 mi / 2h 6m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 155  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:39/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:41/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.3 → 151.2 (+6.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.4% · Z2 78.4% · Z3 21.2% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑305 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 88\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 16 — 13.03 mi / 2h 6m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 144.3 → 151.2 (+6.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:39/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:41/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:38/mi vs front 9:38/mi (vs front half; Δ -1s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:50/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi ▁▁▅█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 9.89 mi → 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 6.9 hrs (range 6–7.6)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: All fine. Sunday was a slog in the humidity but nothing hurts.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Good. A bit worried the 800s were too fast early on.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Should I slow the long run down when it is this hot, or hold the pace?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nStrong week of Aug 3–9: 35.8 mi, long run out to 12.1 mi, and 83% of time in Z1+Z2 — exactly the aerobic base we want 14 weeks out. Thursday's tempo was quality work and the Sunday long run was steady with modest drift. Nice job.\\\\n\\\\nBecause mileage jumped ~10% and relative effort (289) was well above your 3-week average (217), the week of Aug 10–16 is a **consolidation week at the same volume** — no mileage bump. We'll sharpen one quality session, keep easy days properly easy (especially in the heat), and then push the long run again the following week.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags / things I'm watching\\\\n- **Heat**: 25°C at 6 am on Sunday is real. Z3 creep on Wed and Sun long run (both ~17–20% Z3) is likely heat as much as effort. Start the easy days 10–15 sec/mi slower when it's muggy and let HR, not pace, lead.\\\\n- **Thursday tempo pace**: 7:45–7:52/mi is faster than goal marathon pace (3:30 ≈ 8:00/mi) and closer to half-marathon effort. Fine occasionally, but this week I want you to practice *marathon* pace so your body learns that gear.\\\\n- **Shin splint history**: nothing flaring now, but we hold volume this week rather than stacking another jump on top of last week's +4.3 mi.\\\\n- **Strength**: 1 of 2 done. Try to get both in — hips/calves/feet are your shin insurance.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — is 3:30 realistic?\\\\nHonest answer: it's a stretch but not unreasonable. 3:30 is ~8:00/mi. Your easy runs at 9:20–9:40 and HR ~144 (76% max) suggest aerobic fitness is building nicely, and your tempo splits at 7:45–7:52 show you have the raw speed. The gap from a 3:41 PR to 3:30 is 11 minutes, which is big but doable in 14 weeks given you're healthy and ramping sensibly. I'd call it a stretch \\\\\\"A\\\\\\" goal, with 3:35 as a very realistic \\\\\\"B\\\\\\". We'll know more after a couple of MP-specific long runs in September — I'll re-benchmark then.\\\\n\\\\n## Why each session this week\\\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out after Sunday's 12, pure Z2.\\\\n- **Wed easy 6 + strides**: aerobic volume plus 6×20s strides to keep leg turnover sharp without taxing you.\\\\n- **Thu quality — MP intervals on your hilly route**: 4 × 1 mi at goal marathon pace (8:00/mi) with 90s jog. Shorter and more pace-specific than last week's tempo. Hills on recoveries are fine.\\\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long-run flush, keep it slow.\\\\n- **Sun long 12 with MP finish**: same distance as last week, but finish the last 2 miles at ~8:00/mi. Teaches you to close strong on tired legs.\\\\n\\\\nTotal ~35 mi, same as last week. We'll bump to ~37–38 the week after.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-10\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest day. Optional mobility/foam roll — calves and hips.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Optional: 10 min mobility (ankles, hips)\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30–9:50/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi easy, conversational. Let HR lead in heat — aim mid-Z2 (138–148).\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-11\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake-out after Sunday long run. Keep it truly easy.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30–9:50/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi easy + 6×20s strides on flat with full walk recovery after the run. Strides are relaxed, controlled turnover — not sprints.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-12\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 1: hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work (30–40 min)\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP reps 7:55–8:05/mi; warm-up/cool-down 9:40–10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi total on the hilly route. 1.5 mi warm-up → 4 × 1 mi at goal marathon pace (8:00/mi) with 90s easy jog between → 1.5 mi cool-down. If a rep rolls uphill, hold effort not pace. Target avg HR for reps: upper Z3 / low Z4.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-13\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shorter and more marathon-specific than last week's tempo. If legs feel heavy after 3 reps, stop at 3 — do not grind.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-14\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest day. Hydrate well, eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts today.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40–10:00/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi very easy on flat canal path. If it's hot, go even slower.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-15\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 2 (short, 20–25 min): core + calves. Skip if legs are flat.\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Easy 9:40–9:55/mi; MP close 7:55–8:05/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":19312,\\"structure\\":\\"12 mi: first 10 mi easy (Z2), last 2 mi at goal MP (~8:00/mi). Start out ~9:50/mi, let HR settle, then roll into MP for the final 2. Carry fluids and start before sunrise if possible.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-16\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Practice marathon fueling: a gel every 30–35 min. Bail on the MP finish if HR is drifting into Z4 — heat trumps pace targets.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W33\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W32\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"94b17220-2c8a-4ce5-925e-991f6cf5d703\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W32 (Mon Aug 3 – Sun Aug 9, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 35.77 mi | 32.56 mi | 31.50 mi | +4.3 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 43m | 5h 19m | 5h 10m | +33m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 764 ft | 650 ft | 596 ft | +168 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 289 | 223 | 217 | +72 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.2%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 █████████████████████████████░░░░░░  81.9%   (4h 41m)\\\\nZ3 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  11.2%   (38m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░