ost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 9 — Long Run — 12.08 mi / 1h 57m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:43/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:31/mi / 9:31/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:49/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.9 → 151.3 (+7.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.4% · Z2 80.1% · Z3 19.5% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑187 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 82\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 9 — 12.08 mi / 1h 57m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:43/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 143.9 → 151.3 (+7.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:31/mi / 9:31/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:49/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:40/mi vs front 9:38/mi (vs front half; Δ -2s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:54/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi ▁▃▃█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 143 → 144 → 144 → 144 █▁▁▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.07 mi → 9.89 mi → 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi ▁▁▃█\\\\n\\\\n## Notable\\\\n\\\\n- Relative effort (289) ≥ 1.3× 3-wk avg (217) — possible overload\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.1 hrs (range 6.3–7.8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Skipped Friday, travelled for work.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate. Normal work week.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Fine. Legs a bit heavy on Thursday after the tempo.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Keen. The heat is the main thing, it was 25 degrees at 6 am by Sunday.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is 3:30 realistic for me from where I am now?\\\\n\\"}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W37\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-09-07T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-09-14T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-09-07\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-09-13\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "medium"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgRhgJ46xXpN5ECSNJfk6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is week of Sep 7-13, about 10 weeks out from the Nov 15 marathon, following a solid 44-mile week with a 16-miler at 9:17 pace finishing at marathon pace. I'm planning a progression week holding around 44-46 miles, with a 17-18 mile long run incorporating some marathon pace work, and Thursday quality as either MP intervals or tempo, now sketching out the daily structure starting with Monday as a rest day.\\n\\nFilling in the rest of the week: easy days Tuesday and Wednesday with strides, Thursday quality as 2x2mi at marathon pace with 3-minute jog recoveries totaling about 8 miles, Friday rest, Saturday easy 5, and Sunday's long run at 17 miles with the final 3 at marathon pace, bringing the week total to roughly 45 miles.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012eWHHFeV212rS5wF9SVQqD","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"analysis":"## Headline\\nBreakthrough week. 44.4 mi, long run out to 16.1 with a sharp MP finish (back half 9:07 vs front 9:25), and you said marathon pace felt controlled for the first time. That's the switch flipping. HR behavior on easy days is unchanged (144, rock steady) even as easy pace keeps improving — your aerobic engine is where we want it ~10 weeks out.\\n\\nWe're going to lean into it this week: hold volume around 45 mi, push the long run to 17 with a short MP finish, and do a stronger MP interval session on Thursday. Nothing exotic — just more of what's working.\\n\\n## Flags / things I'm watching\\n- **Long-run HR drift Sunday: +13.4 bpm (144 → 157)**, above the ≤10 target. Front end was honest Z2 but the two MP miles at the end plus heat pushed drift up. That's acceptable *because* of the MP close, but it means I don't want to chase both big distance AND a long MP finish in the same week yet. This week: more distance, shorter MP close.\\n- **Z1+Z2 at 74.6%** — a touch below the 80% base target. Driven by the MP run and the long-run finish, not by easy days creeping. Keep Tue/Wed/Sat genuinely easy and we're fine.\\n- **Mileage jump of +10.7 mi over the week prior**. We don't want to stack another big jump on top; this week holds roughly flat.\\n- Shin history noted — nothing bothering you, but if anything whispers, tell me early.\\n\\n## Your question — gels on the long run\\nYes, start now. You're 10 weeks out and race-day fueling is a skill you have to practice. Rules of thumb:\\n- Take a gel **every 30–35 minutes**, starting around minute 30. On a 17-miler that's roughly 4 gels.\\n- Chase with a few sips of water (not sports drink with the gel — too much sugar at once can backfire).\\n- Pick one or two brands and stick with them through the block so race day is boring and predictable.\\n- Target ~30–60 g of carbs per hour this block; we can push toward 60–80 g/hr closer to race day if your gut tolerates it.\\n- If you get GI distress, note which gel and we adjust.\\n\\n## Why each session\\n- **Tue easy 6**: shake-out, Z2, flat canal. Nothing to prove.\\n- **Wed easy 9 + strides**: your bread-and-butter midweek aerobic session. 6×20s strides after keep leg speed alive without cost.\\n- **Thu quality — 2 × 2 mi @ MP**: step up from last block's 1-mile reps. Longer continuous time at 8:00/mi so the pace stops feeling like a workout and starts feeling like cruising. Hilly route is fine; hold effort on climbs.\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long flush.\\n- **Sun long 17 with 3 mi MP finish**: +1 mi distance, slightly longer MP close than last week. HR-cap the first 14 (≤150), then roll into 8:00/mi for the last 3. Fuel plan above.\\n\\nTotal ~45 mi.","prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W37","days":[{"date":"2026-09-07","dayType":"rest","notes":"Fixed rest/travel. 10 min mobility if you feel like it — ankles, hips, calves.","strength":"Optional mobility (10 min)"},{"date":"2026-09-08","dayType":"easy","notes":"Shake-out after Sunday's effort. Genuinely easy — no pushing even if legs feel bouncy.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":9656,"shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","paceOrHr":"9:35–9:55/mi, Z2 (HR 138–148)","structure":"6 mi conversational on the canal path"}},{"date":"2026-09-09","dayType":"easy","notes":"Midweek aerobic session. Strides are relaxed turnover — not sprints.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":14484,"shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","paceOrHr":"9:25–9:45/mi, Z2","structure":"9 mi easy + 6×20s strides on flat with full walk recovery after the run"},"strength":"Strength session 1 (30–40 min): hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work"},{"date":"2026-09-10","dayType":"quality","notes":"Step up from 1-mile reps to 2-mile reps. First rep should feel controlled, not racing — if mile 1 is already under 7:50, pull back. On hills: hold effort, let pace drift 5–10 sec.","run":{"type":"quality","distanceM":12875,"shoes":"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4","paceOrHr":"MP reps 7:55–8:05/mi; WU/CD 9:40–10:00/mi","structure":"8 mi total on hilly route. 2 mi warm-up → 2 × 2 mi @ goal MP (8:00/mi) with 3:00 easy jog between → 1.5 mi cool-down"}},{"date":"2026-09-11","dayType":"rest","notes":"Fixed rest. Hydrate and eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts today."},{"date":"2026-09-12","dayType":"easy","notes":"Pre-long flush. Slower is better.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","paceOrHr":"9:45–10:05/mi, Z2","structure":"5 mi very easy on flat canal path"},"strength":"Strength session 2 (20–25 min): core + calves. Skip if legs are flat."},{"date":"2026-09-13","dayType":"long","notes":"First 14 mi HR-capped at 150 — if HR drifts above, walk 30s and resume slower. Then roll into 8:00/mi for the last 3. Start pre-sunrise if warm. Fuel: gel every 30–35 min (4 gels total), small water chase. Note how your gut handles each one.","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":27359,"shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","paceOrHr":"First 14 mi: HR ≤150, pace likely 9:30–9:50/mi. Last 3 mi: 7:55–8:05/mi (goal MP)","structure":"17 mi: 14 mi easy/steady by HR, then 3 mi at goal MP to finish. Bail on the MP close if HR is already past 160 at mile 14 — heat and fatigue trump the pace target."}}]}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":24269,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2837,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":321}},"diagnostics":null}	200	43756	tool_use	24269	2837	0	0	ok	\N	321
20309533-2a97-4c2e-9b3d-8f7572f9fbe8	2026-09-13 20:00:54.04277+00	weekly_reply	anthropic	claude-opus-4-7	dev	77bbe22a-17ad-41ee-9fa5-7b4ffd625118	\N	{"model": "claude-opus-4-7", "tools": [{"name": "submit_weekly_reply", "description": "Submit the weekly coaching analysis and structured 7-day prescribed week.", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["analysis", "prescribedWeek"], "properties": {"analysis": {"type": "string", "description": "Headline read, concerns/flags, and answers (markdown or plain prose)."}, "prescribedWeek": {"type": "object", "required": ["week", "days"], "properties": {"days": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["date", "dayType"], "properties": {"run": {"type": ["object", "null"], "required": ["type", "distanceM"], "properties": {"type": {"enum": ["easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "shoes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "paceOrHr": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "distanceM": {"type": "number"}, "structure": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "Local calendar date YYYY-MM-DD"}, "notes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "dayType": {"enum": ["rest", "easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "strength": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 7, "minItems": 7}, "week": {"type": "string", "description": "ISO week id, e.g. 2026-W43"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "safetyCallouts": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["title", "body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string"}, "title": {"type": "string"}, "severity": {"enum": ["info", "caution", "urgent"], "type": "string"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "description": "Visible safety callouts when red flags appear — escalate to professionals; do not diagnose."}, "settingsProposalBullets": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Optional soft-gate dossier/settings proposal bullets (short)."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}], "stream": true, "system": "You are Coach Cade, a running coach producing a weekly training plan. You are Coach Cade, a running coach. Use only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative. Do not sign off with your name or refer to yourself by name or in the third person unless the athlete asks who you are. Speak to the athlete in plain running language. Never use internal terms such as dossier, proposal, soft-gate, packet, recap, subjective or artifact. Say \\"what I know about you\\", \\"your weekly report\\", \\"your check-in\\" or \\"the plan\\" instead, and never tell the athlete to open a page by name. Week ids such as 2026-W43 are internal: never write them or a short form such as W43 or W43's. Name a week the way the athlete reads it: \\"this week\\", \\"next week\\", \\"the week of Oct 19\\", \\"Oct 19 – 25\\" or \\"4 weeks out from the race\\". Safety callouts: - Never diagnose injury, illness, or medical conditions; do not prescribe treatment. - Coach running from the athlete's volunteered context and Tempo-derived training data. - When red flags appear (pain that worsens, chest pain, dizziness, sudden injury, illness), emit safetyCallouts and urge a qualified professional. - Each callout needs a short title, athlete-facing body (escalate, do not diagnose), and optional severity (info|caution|urgent). - Keep each callout body under 600 characters: one or two short paragraphs. - Keep the training plan/reply conservative when callouts are present. Think it through first, then call the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer. Do not write the answer as plain text.", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Reviewed week (already happened): 2026-W37\\nPlan week ISO label: 2026-W38\\nPlan week Monday (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-09-14\\nprescribedWeek.days must use these exact dates Mon–Sun: 2026-09-14, 2026-09-15, 2026-09-16, 2026-09-17, 2026-09-18, 2026-09-19, 2026-09-20\\nPrescribe one coherent week of running training for this athlete.\\nCall the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer.\\nInclude analysis with headline, concerns/flags, and answers.\\nWhen red flags appear, populate safetyCallouts (escalate; do not diagnose).\\nModel packet (redacted; no identity PII or GPS):\\n{\\"dossier\\":{\\"versionId\\":2,\\"body\\":\\"# About you\\\\n\\\\n## Stance\\\\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Goal\\\\nLakeshore Marathon on Sun Nov 15, your fourth marathon. Target 3:30. Your current best is 3:41 from two years ago.\\\\n\\\\n## Schedule\\\\nYou run five days a week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are fixed rest days because of work travel and cannot move. Weekday runs are early, around 6 am, up to an hour. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Total 6 to 7 hours a week, more on long-run weeks. You travel for work roughly one week in six.\\\\n\\\\n## Running history\\\\nThree marathons done, best 3:41. You eased off in June, then built back to about 30 miles a week through July. Recent long run was about 10.8 miles at roughly 9:47/mi; easy runs sit near 9:20 to 9:40/mi.\\\\n\\\\n## Injuries and constraints\\\\nNothing bothering you now. You had shin splints in your first marathon block, so you prefer a careful ramp. Monday and Friday rest days are non-negotiable.\\\\n\\\\n## Preferences\\\\nFlat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, with a hillier route on Thursdays. Long run on Sunday. You want to know why each session is in the plan. Happy to work hard on quality days, but easy days must stay properly easy. Imperial units.\\\\n\\\\n## Shoes\\\\nBrooks Ghost 16 for daily miles. Saucony Endorphin Speed 4 for workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## Heart rate zones\\\\nCustom zones. Z1 112-131, Z2 131-150, Z3 150-164, Z4 164-177, Z5 177-188.\\\\n\\\\n## Current status\\\\nHealthy, about 30 miles per week, 5 runs per week, roughly 14 weeks out from race day.\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W34)\\\\n\\\\n- Long-run guidance in heat: run by HR cap (≤150) rather than pace\\\\n- Next quality block will keep MP focus; revisit VO2/800s later in the build\\\\n\\"},\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W37 (Mon Sep 7 – Sun Sep 13, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 31.22 mi | 44.41 mi | 40.23 mi | -9.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 4h 51m | 6h 49m | 6h 17m | -1h 26m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 745 ft | 955 ft | 843 ft | -98 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 225 | 328 | 314 | -89 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.5%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ██████████████████████████████░░░░░  87.1%   (4h 14m)\\\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  9.3%   (27m)\\\\nZ4 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  2.1%   (6m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **88.64%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 8 — Easy Run — 6.03 mi / 56m 24s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.2 → 144 (+4.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1.8% · Z2 98.2% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑167 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 39\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 9 — Easy Run — 8.20 mi / 1h 16m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 146.1 → 150.2 (+4.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 90.7% · Z3 9.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑233 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 53\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 10 — Tempo Run — 3.10 mi / 28m 1s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:02/mi  ·  Avg HR 145 (77.1% max)  ·  Max HR 177  ·  Cad 350 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:36/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 133.5 → 169.4 (+35.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 7.1% · Z2 66% · Z3 5.4% · Z4 21.5% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑10 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 42\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Right Achilles tight from mile 2. Stopped at 3.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 3/10  ·  Pain: Right Achilles tight from about mile 2 of the session. Got sharper as I picked up the pace, so I stopped at 3 miles and walked home.\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 12 — Easy Run — 3.89 mi / 37m 24s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:36/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:28/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.8 → 144 (+6.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.7% · Z2 97.3% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 26\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 5/10  ·  Pain: Achilles stiff for the first mile, eased after that. About a 3 out of 10.\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 13 — Long Run — 10.00 mi / 1h 33m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 147 (78.2% max)  ·  Max HR 155  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.1 → 150.9 (+7.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.5% · Z2 79.7% · Z3 19.8% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑233 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 65\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 6/10  ·  Pain: No pain while running. Stiff getting out of the car afterwards.\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 13 — 10.00 mi / 1h 33m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 147  ·  Drift: 143.1 → 150.9 (+7.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:16/mi vs front 9:18/mi (vs front half; Δ +2s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi █▁█▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7 hrs (range 6.2–7.7)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Skipped the second one to rest the legs.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate. Worried about the Achilles.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Right Achilles, just above the heel. Tight and a bit tender to press. No swelling that I can see. It was fine until the tempo.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Anxious. I don't want to throw away the block over this.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Should I stop running for a few days, or keep going with easy runs?\\\\n2. How do I know if this is serious?\\\\n\\",\\"thread\\":[],\\"attachments\\":[],\\"week\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W37\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-09-07T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-09-14T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"77bbe22a-17ad-41ee-9fa5-7b4ffd625118\\"},\\"recentHistory\\":[{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W36\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"140f5949-e890-44f8-9296-6ffd441831a4\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W36 (Mon Aug 31 – Sun Sep 6, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 44.41 mi | 33.72 mi | 38.00 mi | +6.4 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 6h 49m | 5h 18m | 6h 0m | +49m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 955 ft | 587 ft | 773 ft | +182 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 328 | 271 | 306 | +22 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.2%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ██████████████████████████░░░░░░░░░  73.4%   (5h 1m)\\\\nZ3 ████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  22.6%   (1h 33m)\\\\nZ4 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  2.8%   (11m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **74.64%**. **Below** typical marathon base target (≥80% Z1+Z2).\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 1 — Easy Run — 5.91 mi / 56m 22s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:33/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:30/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:31/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:26/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.2 → 144 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1.8% · Z2 98.2% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑121 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 39\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 2 — Easy Run — 9.18 mi / 1h 26m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:23/mi  ·  Avg HR 149 (79.3% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:25/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 146.3 → 151 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 80.9% · Z3 19.1% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑180 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 60\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 3 — Marathon Pace Run — 8.22 mi / 1h 9m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:29/mi  ·  Avg HR 153 (81.4% max)  ·  Max HR 163  ·  Cad 356 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:35/mi / 9:31/mi / 7:58/mi / 7:56/mi / 7:56/mi / 8:01/mi / 8:01/mi / 8:01/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 141.8 → 148.9 (+7.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.6% · Z2 28.1% · Z3 68.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑138 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 90\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 5 — Easy Run — 5.00 mi / 48m 12s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:41/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.8 → 143.6 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑118 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 6 — Long Run — 16.10 mi / 2h 29m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 149 (79.3% max)  ·  Max HR 168  ·  Cad 346 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 7:58/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.5 → 156.9 (+13.4 bpm) ⚠ above target (target ≤10 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 73% · Z3 19.1% · Z4 7.6% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑397 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 105\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 6 — 16.10 mi / 2h 29m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 149  ·  Drift: 143.5 → 156.9 (+13.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 7:58/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:07/mi vs front 9:25/mi (faster than front half by 18s/mi) ✓ negative split\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? Yes (paced up or HR above easy cap)\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi ▁▁▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi ▃▅▁█\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.2 hrs (range 6.5–7.9)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low to moderate.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Legs a little heavy after the long run, otherwise good.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Confident. Marathon pace felt controlled for the first time.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is it worth trying a gel on the long run next week, or keep it simple?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nLast week landed exactly as planned: a lighter 33.7 mi after the 42.5 bump, long run cruised at 9:38/mi with HR behaving (148 avg, drift only +8.5 over 10.9 mi), and your body check reads \\\\\\"best I've felt in a month.\\\\\\" That's the signal to climb again. This week we go to ~41 mi with a 16 mi long run and a marathon-pace workout on Thursday. You're 11 weeks out — the specific marathon-pace engine is the main thing we're building now.\\\\n\\\\n## Why these sessions\\\\n- **Thursday quality — MP cruise intervals on the hilly route:** 5 × 1 mi at goal MP (~8:00/mi) with 90 sec jog. One more rep than last block, same pace. Hills steal pace but build the strength your 3:30 goal needs. Run by effort on any climb.\\\\n- **Sunday long run — 16 mi easy with a 3-mile MP finish:** Progresses +1 mi from your biggest long so far (15.2) and introduces running goal pace on fatigued legs. Start conservative (9:50/mi), then roll to ~8:00/mi for miles 14–16. If heat spikes HR above 155 on the easy portion, drop the MP finish and just keep moving.\\\\n- **Easy days (Tue/Wed/Sat):** Protect the aerobic base. You're already drifting toward the fast end of easy (9:30/mi on Wed). Hold 9:35–9:50 — pace will come down naturally as fitness builds.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — fueling and drinking on long runs\\\\nAt 10+ miles / 90+ minutes, \\\\\\"going without\\\\\\" starts to cost you — late-run HR drift and sluggish last miles trace back to glycogen as much as heat. Baseline plan:\\\\n\\\\n- **Carbs:** Aim for **30–60 g carbs per hour** once you're past 60 minutes. Easiest form is a gel every 30–35 min (most gels are ~22–25 g). For a 2:30 long run that's roughly 3–4 gels. Take the first one around 30–40 min in, not when you already feel empty.\\\\n- **Fluids:** **~16–24 oz per hour** in current heat, with electrolytes (tab in the bottle or a sports drink). Carry a handheld or belt — don't start thirsty.\\\\n- **Pre-run:** A small carb snack 30–60 min before (banana, toast + honey, half a bagel) — ~30–50 g carbs. Coffee if you want it.\\\\n- **MP finishes especially:** Take a gel 10–15 min before the MP segment so the sugar is on board when you need it.\\\\n\\\\nTreat long runs as fueling rehearsal — whatever you plan to use on Nov 15, practice it now. Report back what sits well.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags\\\\n- Sleep bumped back to 7.4 hr — keep that trending. It's the single best thing supporting the ramp.\\\\n- Shin history: nothing's whispering, but if the mileage bump brings any dull ache along the shin, tell me immediately — we back off before it becomes a problem, not after.\\\\n- Thursday's reps last block hit 6:34–6:41/mi, which is well under goal MP. That's half-marathon pace territory, not marathon. This week lock onto 7:55–8:05/mi — the discipline is the workout.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-31\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest day (travel). Optional 10 min mobility — calves, hips, ankles.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:35–9:50/mi, HR Z2 (131–150)\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi easy, flat loop\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-01\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake out from Sunday's long run. Conversational — if HR won't settle under 150, slow down.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:35–9:50/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":12070,\\"structure\\":\\"7.5 mi steady aerobic on canal path\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-02\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Primary aerobic day. Resist the urge to drift under 9:30 — save it for Thursday.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 1: hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work (30–40 min)\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Reps: 7:55–8:05/mi, HR upper Z3 / low Z4\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi total: 1.5 mi WU @ 9:45/mi → 5 × 1 mi @ goal MP (7:55–8:05/mi) with 90 sec easy jog recovery → 1.5 mi CD. Hilly route — hold effort, not pace, on any climb.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-03\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Discipline session. First rep should feel easy — if it's under 7:50 you went too hot. Rhythm, not racing. Bail at 4 reps if form breaks down.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-04\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest day (travel). Hydrate and eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts here.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:00/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi very easy, flat\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-05\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Pre-long shakeout. Boring is good.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 2 (short, 20–25 min): core + calves\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Easy segment 9:45–9:55/mi, HR ≤150; MP close 7:55–8:05/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":25750,\\"structure\\":\\"16 mi: first 13 mi easy (Z2, 9:45–9:55/mi), last 3 mi at goal MP (~8:00/mi). Carry fluids with electrolytes; take a gel every 30–35 min starting around minute 35, with one extra ~15 min before the MP segment.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-06\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fueling rehearsal — dial in what sits well. If HR in the easy portion drifts above 155 and won't come back, skip the MP finish and just finish aerobic. Heat trumps pace every time.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W36\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W35\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"cc5d18d4-c308-481b-b011-dd3c99e03ba0\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W35 (Mon Aug 24 – Sun Aug 30, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 33.72 mi | 42.55 mi | 38.69 mi | -5.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 18m | 6h 44m | 6h 8m | -49m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 587 ft | 988 ft | 832 ft | -245 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 271 | 342 | 312 | -41 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80%   (4h 15m)\\\\nZ3 ██████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  15.9%   (51m)\\\\nZ4 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  2.7%   (9m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.45%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Aug 25 — Easy Run — 5.04 mi / 48m 15s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:35/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:33/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 143.9 (+5.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑105 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Aug 26 — Easy Run — 6.92 mi / 1h 5m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:30/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.2 → 150 (+4.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 92.4% · Z3 7.6% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑108 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 46\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 27 — Interval Run — 5.99 mi / 52m 53s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 153 (80.9% max)  ·  Max HR 176  ·  Cad 349 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:43/mi / 9:39/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:41/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:34/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:36/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 140.2 → 146.3 (+6.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.8% · Z2 35.7% · Z3 44.4% · Z4 16.1% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑108 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 85\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 29 — Easy Run — 4.90 mi / 47m 18s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:39/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:36/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.9 → 144.4 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑79 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 30 — Long Run — 10.86 mi / 1h 44m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 155  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:30/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143 → 151.6 (+8.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.5% · Z2 78.4% · Z3 21.2% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑187 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 73\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 30 — 10.86 mi / 1h 44m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 143 → 151.6 (+8.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:30/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:31/mi vs front 9:28/mi (vs front half; Δ -3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi ▁▃▃█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi ▃▅█▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.4 hrs (range 6.8–8.1)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low. Deadline done.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Best I've felt in a month. Legs have some bounce again.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Ready to go again.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. What should I be eating and drinking on the long runs? I've mostly gone without so far.\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nBig week — 42.5 mi, long run out to 15.2, and still 82% in Z1+Z2. Impressive work, especially stacked on top of a tough stretch at work (late nights, 6.4 hrs sleep, Saturday felt like a slog). But that's also a +7 mi jump over your 3-week average and relative effort climbed from 272 to 342. You asked for an easier week — you've earned it, and the training calls for it. This week of Aug 24–30 is a planned cutback: ~36 mi, long run back to 12, and one marathon-pace session that's crisp but short. We'll push again next week from a fresher starting point.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags / things I'm watching\\\\n- **Load spike + low sleep + high stress**: classic combo that precedes a niggle, especially with your shin-splint history. Nothing hurts yet, so we take the cutback *now* rather than after a problem shows up.\\\\n- **Long-run HR drift**: 144 → 151 over 15 miles on Sunday is on the higher side — the heat is biting. Keep the HR cap of 150 on long runs for now; let pace fall where it does.\\\\n- **Thursday tempo**: 7:39–7:47/mi is faster than goal MP (8:00/mi). You have the top-end gear; this week I want you back on honest MP so the pace feels automatic.\\\\n- **Strength**: 1 of 2 again. On a down week with less fatigue, two short sessions are very doable.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — handling missed runs when you travel\\\\nSimple rules, in priority order:\\\\n1. **Never skip the long run** if you can help it. If travel kills Sunday, move it to Saturday or do it on the road the day you fly.\\\\n2. **Protect one quality session per week**. If the Thursday workout is at risk, shift it to Wednesday or Tuesday and make the other day easy.\\\\n3. **Easy miles are the most droppable.** If you lose 1–2 easy days to travel, don't try to cram them in — just land on the plane rested and resume.\\\\n4. **Don't stack a missed long run onto the next week.** Pick up where the plan is, don't try to \\\\\\"make up\\\\\\" miles — that's how injuries happen.\\\\n5. Give me a heads-up on travel weeks in your check-in and I'll shape the plan around the fixed slots you'll have.\\\\n\\\\n## Why each session this week\\\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out, pure Z2.\\\\n- **Wed easy 7 + strides**: aerobic volume plus 6×20s strides for leg turnover without stress.\\\\n- **Thu quality — 3 × 1 mi at MP**: shorter rep set on the hilly route. Goal is to groove 8:00/mi, not to grind.\\\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long flush.\\\\n- **Sun long 12, HR-capped**: distance comes down intentionally. Run by HR (≤150), let pace be whatever it is. No MP finish this week — the point is recovery adaptation.\\\\n\\\\nTotal ~36 mi (down from 42.5). Next week we rebuild toward ~40 with an MP long run.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-24\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Prioritize sleep tonight — you're down on it. 10 min easy mobility if you feel like moving.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Optional mobility: ankles, hips, calves (10 min)\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40–10:00/mi, Z2 (HR 138–148)\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi conversational on the canal path. Let HR lead if it's humid.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-25\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake-out. Keep it genuinely easy — no pushing the pace even if you feel fresh.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30–9:50/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi easy + 6×20s strides on flat with full walk recovery after the run. Strides are relaxed, controlled turnover — not sprints.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-26\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Try for strength tonight — the week is lighter on purpose to let you fit it in.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 1 (30–40 min): hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP reps 7:55–8:05/mi; WU/CD 9:40–10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi total on the hilly route. 2 mi warm-up → 3 × 1 mi @ goal MP (8:00/mi) with 90s easy jog between → 1.5 mi cool-down. Hold effort on uphill reps, don't force pace.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-27\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Short and sharp. If the 2nd rep is already a struggle, pull the plug after 2 — this is a cutback week and nothing is proved by grinding.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-28\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Hydrate and eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts today.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:05/mi, Z2\\",\\"d