9:51/mi / 6:41/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:51/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.8 → 143.5 (+3.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.4% · Z2 40% · Z3 22.8% · Z4 32.1% · Z5 1.7%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑92 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 95\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 8/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 15 — Easy Run — 4.92 mi / 48m 22s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:44/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:54/mi / 9:43/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.2 → 143.9 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑108 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 16 — Long Run — 13.03 mi / 2h 6m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 155  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:39/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:41/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.3 → 151.2 (+6.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.4% · Z2 78.4% · Z3 21.2% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑305 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 88\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 16 — 13.03 mi / 2h 6m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 144.3 → 151.2 (+6.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:39/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:41/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:38/mi vs front 9:38/mi (vs front half; Δ -1s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:50/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi ▁▁▅█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 9.89 mi → 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 6.9 hrs (range 6–7.6)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: All fine. Sunday was a slog in the humidity but nothing hurts.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Good. A bit worried the 800s were too fast early on.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Should I slow the long run down when it is this hot, or hold the pace?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nStrong week of Aug 3–9: 35.8 mi, long run out to 12.1 mi, and 83% of time in Z1+Z2 — exactly the aerobic base we want 14 weeks out. Thursday's tempo was quality work and the Sunday long run was steady with modest drift. Nice job.\\\\n\\\\nBecause mileage jumped ~10% and relative effort (289) was well above your 3-week average (217), the week of Aug 10–16 is a **consolidation week at the same volume** — no mileage bump. We'll sharpen one quality session, keep easy days properly easy (especially in the heat), and then push the long run again the following week.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags / things I'm watching\\\\n- **Heat**: 25°C at 6 am on Sunday is real. Z3 creep on Wed and Sun long run (both ~17–20% Z3) is likely heat as much as effort. Start the easy days 10–15 sec/mi slower when it's muggy and let HR, not pace, lead.\\\\n- **Thursday tempo pace**: 7:45–7:52/mi is faster than goal marathon pace (3:30 ≈ 8:00/mi) and closer to half-marathon effort. Fine occasionally, but this week I want you to practice *marathon* pace so your body learns that gear.\\\\n- **Shin splint history**: nothing flaring now, but we hold volume this week rather than stacking another jump on top of last week's +4.3 mi.\\\\n- **Strength**: 1 of 2 done. Try to get both in — hips/calves/feet are your shin insurance.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — is 3:30 realistic?\\\\nHonest answer: it's a stretch but not unreasonable. 3:30 is ~8:00/mi. Your easy runs at 9:20–9:40 and HR ~144 (76% max) suggest aerobic fitness is building nicely, and your tempo splits at 7:45–7:52 show you have the raw speed. The gap from a 3:41 PR to 3:30 is 11 minutes, which is big but doable in 14 weeks given you're healthy and ramping sensibly. I'd call it a stretch \\\\\\"A\\\\\\" goal, with 3:35 as a very realistic \\\\\\"B\\\\\\". We'll know more after a couple of MP-specific long runs in September — I'll re-benchmark then.\\\\n\\\\n## Why each session this week\\\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out after Sunday's 12, pure Z2.\\\\n- **Wed easy 6 + strides**: aerobic volume plus 6×20s strides to keep leg turnover sharp without taxing you.\\\\n- **Thu quality — MP intervals on your hilly route**: 4 × 1 mi at goal marathon pace (8:00/mi) with 90s jog. Shorter and more pace-specific than last week's tempo. Hills on recoveries are fine.\\\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long-run flush, keep it slow.\\\\n- **Sun long 12 with MP finish**: same distance as last week, but finish the last 2 miles at ~8:00/mi. Teaches you to close strong on tired legs.\\\\n\\\\nTotal ~35 mi, same as last week. We'll bump to ~37–38 the week after.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-10\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest day. Optional mobility/foam roll — calves and hips.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Optional: 10 min mobility (ankles, hips)\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30–9:50/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi easy, conversational. Let HR lead in heat — aim mid-Z2 (138–148).\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-11\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake-out after Sunday long run. Keep it truly easy.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30–9:50/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi easy + 6×20s strides on flat with full walk recovery after the run. Strides are relaxed, controlled turnover — not sprints.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-12\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 1: hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work (30–40 min)\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP reps 7:55–8:05/mi; warm-up/cool-down 9:40–10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi total on the hilly route. 1.5 mi warm-up → 4 × 1 mi at goal marathon pace (8:00/mi) with 90s easy jog between → 1.5 mi cool-down. If a rep rolls uphill, hold effort not pace. Target avg HR for reps: upper Z3 / low Z4.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-13\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shorter and more marathon-specific than last week's tempo. If legs feel heavy after 3 reps, stop at 3 — do not grind.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-14\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest day. Hydrate well, eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts today.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40–10:00/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi very easy on flat canal path. If it's hot, go even slower.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-15\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 2 (short, 20–25 min): core + calves. Skip if legs are flat.\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Easy 9:40–9:55/mi; MP close 7:55–8:05/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":19312,\\"structure\\":\\"12 mi: first 10 mi easy (Z2), last 2 mi at goal MP (~8:00/mi). Start out ~9:50/mi, let HR settle, then roll into MP for the final 2. Carry fluids and start before sunrise if possible.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-16\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Practice marathon fueling: a gel every 30–35 min. Bail on the MP finish if HR is drifting into Z4 — heat trumps pace targets.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W33\\"}}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W38\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-09-14T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-09-21T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-09-14\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-09-20\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "medium"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgRhk7QWfR4bAU6Tf1L8n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Given the Achilles pain flagging sharp with pace, I should treat this conservatively — keep things easy, drop the tempo work, trim the long run, and consider cross-training, with a clear note to see a professional if it doesn't improve. I'm sketching the Sep 14-20 week with fixed rest days on Monday and Friday, starting with a short, flat easy test run Tuesday to gauge response before deciding on anything more.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BUVDY9QmLwkDkiNDYZVHu9","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"analysis":"## Headline\\nWe're pulling back this week. The Achilles signal on Thursday — tight from mile 2, sharper when you picked up the pace, enough to stop and walk home — is exactly the kind of thing we treat conservatively right now, not push through. You still got a solid 10-miler in on Sunday with no pain while running, which is a good sign, but stiffness afterward tells me the tissue is irritated. We lose nothing by taking 7–10 easy days here. We lose the whole block if we poke it.\\n\\nPlan this week: no tempo, no MP work, no hills, all flat, all Ghost 16. Shorter easy runs, a modest long run capped by feel, and a hard stop rule if symptoms escalate. We're 9 weeks from Lakeshore — plenty of runway to rebuild quality if the Achilles settles.\\n\\n## Your questions\\n\\n**\\"Should I stop running for a few days, or keep going with easy runs?\\"**\\nIf pain is ≤3/10, not sharp, and eases within the first mile (like Saturday), easy running on flats is usually fine and can actually help. If it's sharp, worsens as you run, changes your gait, or lingers/worsens after — stop that day and take 2–3 full days off. The tempo-day pattern (fine easy, bad with pace) is the key signal: speed is off the menu until it's quiet for a full week.\\n\\n**\\"How do I know if this is serious?\\"**\\nI'm a coach, not a clinician, so I can't diagnose this — and I won't try. What I can tell you is which signs mean \\"see a sports physio or sports medicine doc this week, don't wait\\": sharp or stabbing pain, pain that worsens run-over-run, morning pain in the first steps out of bed that doesn't ease, visible swelling or a lump, pain squeezing the tendon, or any change in how your foot pushes off. If any of those show up, please book an appointment — early assessment on Achilles stuff is cheap insurance. See the callout below.\\n\\n## Flags\\n- Tempo Thursday: tightness → sharper with pace → stopped at 3 mi. Clear signal from the tissue.\\n- Sunday long run was pain-free running but stiff after — tendon is grumbling, not screaming. That's the window to be smart.\\n- Mileage already came off (31 vs 44) — don't rush it back. Reload gradually once symptoms are quiet.\\n- Sleep 7 hrs, stress moderate, anxious about the block — I hear you. One cautious week does not throw away a marathon. Grinding on an angry Achilles can.\\n- Shoes: all easy miles in Ghost 16. Keep the Endorphin Speed 4 in the closet until we're back doing workouts.\\n\\n## How to read this week\\n- Each run, do a 5-minute walk warm-up before you start running. Flat routes only — the hilly Thursday loop is out.\\n- Pain rules every day: ≤3/10 and not sharp = continue; sharp, worsening, or altering your gait = stop and walk home. Report back what you felt in the check-in.\\n- No strides, no pickups, no hills, no MP touches. Pure easy aerobic.\\n- If two consecutive runs hurt more than the one before, stop running and get it looked at before the next session.","prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W38","days":[{"date":"2026-09-14","dayType":"rest","notes":"Fixed rest. Gentle calf and ankle mobility is fine — no aggressive stretching of the Achilles, no eccentric heel drops this week unless a clinician has prescribed them."},{"date":"2026-09-15","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":6437,"paceOrHr":"9:40–10:00/mi, HR Z2","structure":"5-min brisk walk warm-up, then 4 mi very easy on the flat canal path. No strides. No pickups.","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"notes":"This is the test run. If the Achilles stays ≤3/10 and quiets as you go, finish the 4. If it sharpens or alters your stride, walk home and we treat Wednesday as rest."},{"date":"2026-09-16","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"paceOrHr":"9:40–10:00/mi, HR Z2","structure":"5-min walk warm-up, then 5 mi flat canal path, conversational.","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"notes":"Only run this if Tuesday was clean. If any pain lingered after Tuesday, swap today for rest or 30 min easy cross-train (bike/elliptical, no running).","strength":"Short core + hip session, 20 min. Skip any heavy calf loading this week."},{"date":"2026-09-17","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":6437,"paceOrHr":"9:45–10:05/mi, HR Z2","structure":"5-min walk warm-up, then 4 mi flat and easy. Not the hilly route — flat only.","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"notes":"This replaces the tempo. No pace work, no hills. If the Achilles has been quiet all week this is just an easy aerobic day; if it's grumbling, make it 30 min easy cross-train instead and don't force the run."},{"date":"2026-09-18","dayType":"rest","notes":"Fixed rest. Normal eating, hydrate. Use the day to honestly check in with how the tendon feels on stairs and first steps in the morning — that's useful info."},{"date":"2026-09-19","dayType":"easy","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":6437,"paceOrHr":"9:45–10:05/mi, HR Z2","structure":"5-min walk warm-up, then 4 mi flat and easy.","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"notes":"Pre-long shakeout. If anything felt off Thursday, cut this to 3 mi or skip."},{"date":"2026-09-20","dayType":"long","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":14484,"paceOrHr":"9:45–10:00/mi, HR ≤150","structure":"9 mi flat and easy, out-and-back on the canal path. No MP work, no fast finish. Walk 30s at mile 3 and mile 6 as a check-in — how does the Achilles feel? If any sharpness, cut it short and walk back.","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"notes":"Down from 10 last week on purpose. Keep practicing fueling — gel every 30–35 min, fluids with electrolytes. This is a feel-it-out long run, not a progression."}]},"safetyCallouts":[{"title":"Get the Achilles looked at if these signs show up","body":"I can coach around a grumbling tendon, but I can't diagnose it — and Achilles issues are worth catching early. Please book a sports physio or sports medicine appointment this week if you notice any of: sharp or stabbing pain while running, pain that worsens run-over-run, pain or stiffness in the first steps out of bed that doesn't ease within a few minutes, visible swelling or a lump on the tendon, tenderness when you pinch the tendon between thumb and finger, or any change in how your foot pushes off. Early assessment is cheap insurance for the marathon block.","severity":"caution"},{"title":"Stop-the-run rules this week","body":"During any run, stop and walk home if: pain goes above 3/10, becomes sharp, worsens as you run, or changes your stride. One or two cautious days won't cost you the race. Pushing through an angry tendon can. Tell me in your next check-in exactly what you felt and when — that detail shapes next week's plan.","severity":"info"}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26647,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3221,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":309}},"diagnostics":null}	200	53627	tool_use	26647	3221	0	0	ok	\N	309
fdb17644-6fe1-4179-8dbb-9e47f9cb54e8	2026-09-20 20:00:44.489188+00	weekly_reply	anthropic	claude-opus-4-7	dev	0876b9b6-d823-4b3e-97fb-b670672066db	\N	{"model": "claude-opus-4-7", "tools": [{"name": "submit_weekly_reply", "description": "Submit the weekly coaching analysis and structured 7-day prescribed week.", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["analysis", "prescribedWeek"], "properties": {"analysis": {"type": "string", "description": "Headline read, concerns/flags, and answers (markdown or plain prose)."}, "prescribedWeek": {"type": "object", "required": ["week", "days"], "properties": {"days": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["date", "dayType"], "properties": {"run": {"type": ["object", "null"], "required": ["type", "distanceM"], "properties": {"type": {"enum": ["easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "shoes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "paceOrHr": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "distanceM": {"type": "number"}, "structure": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "Local calendar date YYYY-MM-DD"}, "notes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "dayType": {"enum": ["rest", "easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "strength": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 7, "minItems": 7}, "week": {"type": "string", "description": "ISO week id, e.g. 2026-W43"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "safetyCallouts": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["title", "body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string"}, "title": {"type": "string"}, "severity": {"enum": ["info", "caution", "urgent"], "type": "string"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "description": "Visible safety callouts when red flags appear — escalate to professionals; do not diagnose."}, "settingsProposalBullets": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Optional soft-gate dossier/settings proposal bullets (short)."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}], "stream": true, "system": "You are Coach Cade, a running coach producing a weekly training plan. You are Coach Cade, a running coach. Use only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative. Do not sign off with your name or refer to yourself by name or in the third person unless the athlete asks who you are. Speak to the athlete in plain running language. Never use internal terms such as dossier, proposal, soft-gate, packet, recap, subjective or artifact. Say \\"what I know about you\\", \\"your weekly report\\", \\"your check-in\\" or \\"the plan\\" instead, and never tell the athlete to open a page by name. Week ids such as 2026-W43 are internal: never write them or a short form such as W43 or W43's. Name a week the way the athlete reads it: \\"this week\\", \\"next week\\", \\"the week of Oct 19\\", \\"Oct 19 – 25\\" or \\"4 weeks out from the race\\". Safety callouts: - Never diagnose injury, illness, or medical conditions; do not prescribe treatment. - Coach running from the athlete's volunteered context and Tempo-derived training data. - When red flags appear (pain that worsens, chest pain, dizziness, sudden injury, illness), emit safetyCallouts and urge a qualified professional. - Each callout needs a short title, athlete-facing body (escalate, do not diagnose), and optional severity (info|caution|urgent). - Keep each callout body under 600 characters: one or two short paragraphs. - Keep the training plan/reply conservative when callouts are present. Think it through first, then call the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer. Do not write the answer as plain text.", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Reviewed week (already happened): 2026-W38\\nPlan week ISO label: 2026-W39\\nPlan week Monday (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-09-21\\nprescribedWeek.days must use these exact dates Mon–Sun: 2026-09-21, 2026-09-22, 2026-09-23, 2026-09-24, 2026-09-25, 2026-09-26, 2026-09-27\\nPrescribe one coherent week of running training for this athlete.\\nCall the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer.\\nInclude analysis with headline, concerns/flags, and answers.\\nWhen red flags appear, populate safetyCallouts (escalate; do not diagnose).\\nModel packet (redacted; no identity PII or GPS):\\n{\\"dossier\\":{\\"versionId\\":2,\\"body\\":\\"# About you\\\\n\\\\n## Stance\\\\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Goal\\\\nLakeshore Marathon on Sun Nov 15, your fourth marathon. Target 3:30. Your current best is 3:41 from two years ago.\\\\n\\\\n## Schedule\\\\nYou run five days a week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are fixed rest days because of work travel and cannot move. Weekday runs are early, around 6 am, up to an hour. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Total 6 to 7 hours a week, more on long-run weeks. You travel for work roughly one week in six.\\\\n\\\\n## Running history\\\\nThree marathons done, best 3:41. You eased off in June, then built back to about 30 miles a week through July. Recent long run was about 10.8 miles at roughly 9:47/mi; easy runs sit near 9:20 to 9:40/mi.\\\\n\\\\n## Injuries and constraints\\\\nNothing bothering you now. You had shin splints in your first marathon block, so you prefer a careful ramp. Monday and Friday rest days are non-negotiable.\\\\n\\\\n## Preferences\\\\nFlat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, with a hillier route on Thursdays. Long run on Sunday. You want to know why each session is in the plan. Happy to work hard on quality days, but easy days must stay properly easy. Imperial units.\\\\n\\\\n## Shoes\\\\nBrooks Ghost 16 for daily miles. Saucony Endorphin Speed 4 for workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## Heart rate zones\\\\nCustom zones. Z1 112-131, Z2 131-150, Z3 150-164, Z4 164-177, Z5 177-188.\\\\n\\\\n## Current status\\\\nHealthy, about 30 miles per week, 5 runs per week, roughly 14 weeks out from race day.\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W34)\\\\n\\\\n- Long-run guidance in heat: run by HR cap (≤150) rather than pace\\\\n- Next quality block will keep MP focus; revisit VO2/800s later in the build\\\\n\\"},\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W38 (Mon Sep 14 – Sun Sep 20, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 25.95 mi | 31.22 mi | 36.45 mi | -10.5 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 4h 4m | 4h 51m | 5h 39m | -1h 35m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 525 ft | 745 ft | 762 ft | -237 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 171 | 225 | 275 | -104 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 143 | 144 | 144 | -1 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 ███████████████████████████████░░░░  89.7%   (3h 39m)\\\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  8.8%   (22m)\\\\nZ4 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **91.18%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 15 — Easy Run — 4.13 mi / 38m 32s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 144.2 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑82 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 6/10  ·  Pain: Slight tightness for the first half mile, about a 2 out of 10.\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 16 — Easy Run — 4.83 mi / 45m 6s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:12/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.8 → 150.6 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 84.3% · Z3 15.7% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 32\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10  ·  Pain: A hint of it at the start only.\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 17 — Easy Run — 4.99 mi / 46m 53s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:23/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138 → 143.7 (+5.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑135 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Achilles fine on the flat. Easy only this week.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 19 — Easy Run — 4.07 mi / 38m 48s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:31/mi  ·  Avg HR 141 (75% max)  ·  Max HR 146  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.9 → 143.2 (+5.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑112 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 20 — Long Run — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147 (78.2% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0