spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:36/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.9 → 144.4 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑79 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 30 — Long Run — 10.86 mi / 1h 44m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 155  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:30/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143 → 151.6 (+8.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.5% · Z2 78.4% · Z3 21.2% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑187 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 73\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 30 — 10.86 mi / 1h 44m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 143 → 151.6 (+8.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:30/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:31/mi vs front 9:28/mi (vs front half; Δ -3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi ▁▃▃█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi ▃▅█▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.4 hrs (range 6.8–8.1)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low. Deadline done.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Best I've felt in a month. Legs have some bounce again.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Ready to go again.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. What should I be eating and drinking on the long runs? I've mostly gone without so far.\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nBig week — 42.5 mi, long run out to 15.2, and still 82% in Z1+Z2. Impressive work, especially stacked on top of a tough stretch at work (late nights, 6.4 hrs sleep, Saturday felt like a slog). But that's also a +7 mi jump over your 3-week average and relative effort climbed from 272 to 342. You asked for an easier week — you've earned it, and the training calls for it. This week of Aug 24–30 is a planned cutback: ~36 mi, long run back to 12, and one marathon-pace session that's crisp but short. We'll push again next week from a fresher starting point.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags / things I'm watching\\\\n- **Load spike + low sleep + high stress**: classic combo that precedes a niggle, especially with your shin-splint history. Nothing hurts yet, so we take the cutback *now* rather than after a problem shows up.\\\\n- **Long-run HR drift**: 144 → 151 over 15 miles on Sunday is on the higher side — the heat is biting. Keep the HR cap of 150 on long runs for now; let pace fall where it does.\\\\n- **Thursday tempo**: 7:39–7:47/mi is faster than goal MP (8:00/mi). You have the top-end gear; this week I want you back on honest MP so the pace feels automatic.\\\\n- **Strength**: 1 of 2 again. On a down week with less fatigue, two short sessions are very doable.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — handling missed runs when you travel\\\\nSimple rules, in priority order:\\\\n1. **Never skip the long run** if you can help it. If travel kills Sunday, move it to Saturday or do it on the road the day you fly.\\\\n2. **Protect one quality session per week**. If the Thursday workout is at risk, shift it to Wednesday or Tuesday and make the other day easy.\\\\n3. **Easy miles are the most droppable.** If you lose 1–2 easy days to travel, don't try to cram them in — just land on the plane rested and resume.\\\\n4. **Don't stack a missed long run onto the next week.** Pick up where the plan is, don't try to \\\\\\"make up\\\\\\" miles — that's how injuries happen.\\\\n5. Give me a heads-up on travel weeks in your check-in and I'll shape the plan around the fixed slots you'll have.\\\\n\\\\n## Why each session this week\\\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out, pure Z2.\\\\n- **Wed easy 7 + strides**: aerobic volume plus 6×20s strides for leg turnover without stress.\\\\n- **Thu quality — 3 × 1 mi at MP**: shorter rep set on the hilly route. Goal is to groove 8:00/mi, not to grind.\\\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long flush.\\\\n- **Sun long 12, HR-capped**: distance comes down intentionally. Run by HR (≤150), let pace be whatever it is. No MP finish this week — the point is recovery adaptation.\\\\n\\\\nTotal ~36 mi (down from 42.5). Next week we rebuild toward ~40 with an MP long run.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-24\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Prioritize sleep tonight — you're down on it. 10 min easy mobility if you feel like moving.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Optional mobility: ankles, hips, calves (10 min)\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40–10:00/mi, Z2 (HR 138–148)\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi conversational on the canal path. Let HR lead if it's humid.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-25\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake-out. Keep it genuinely easy — no pushing the pace even if you feel fresh.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30–9:50/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi easy + 6×20s strides on flat with full walk recovery after the run. Strides are relaxed, controlled turnover — not sprints.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-26\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Try for strength tonight — the week is lighter on purpose to let you fit it in.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 1 (30–40 min): hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP reps 7:55–8:05/mi; WU/CD 9:40–10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi total on the hilly route. 2 mi warm-up → 3 × 1 mi @ goal MP (8:00/mi) with 90s easy jog between → 1.5 mi cool-down. Hold effort on uphill reps, don't force pace.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-27\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Short and sharp. If the 2nd rep is already a struggle, pull the plug after 2 — this is a cutback week and nothing is proved by grinding.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-28\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Hydrate and eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts today.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:05/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi very easy on flat canal path.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-29\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Pre-long flush. Slower is better here.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 2 (20–25 min): core + calves. Skip if legs are flat.\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"HR ≤150 (mid-Z2); pace will likely land 9:40–9:55/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":19312,\\"structure\\":\\"12 mi steady, HR-capped. If HR drifts above 150, walk 30s and resume slower. No fast finish this week — this is recovery-oriented aerobic volume.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-30\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Cutback long run. HR cap, no MP work. Fuel every 30–35 min with a gel to keep practicing race fueling. Start before sunrise if it's going to be warm.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W35\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W34\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"673db0ec-b22b-4732-9a14-3b48998783a8\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W34 (Mon Aug 17 – Sun Aug 23, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 42.55 mi | 37.74 mi | 35.36 mi | +7.2 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 6h 44m | 5h 57m | 5h 40m | +1h 4m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 988 ft | 745 ft | 720 ft | +268 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 342 | 304 | 272 | +70 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.1%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80.9%   (5h 27m)\\\\nZ3 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  11.2%   (45m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  6.8%   (28m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **82.01%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Aug 18 — Easy Run — 6.17 mi / 59m 43s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:38/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139 → 144.2 (+5.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1.7% · Z2 98.3% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑82 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 42\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Aug 19 — Easy Run — 7.89 mi / 1h 15m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:35/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:31/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.6 → 149.5 (+3.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 96% · Z3 4% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑161 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 53\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 20 — Tempo Run — 8.14 mi / 1h 11m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 151 (80.3% max)  ·  Max HR 173  ·  Cad 352 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:43/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:54/mi / 7:47/mi / 7:39/mi / 7:45/mi / 7:42/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:54/mi / 9:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 136.1 → 140.3 (+4.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.8% · Z2 53.3% · Z3 5.6% · Z4 38.3% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑223 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 108\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 22 — Easy Run — 5.18 mi / 50m 48s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 345 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:52/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:44/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.2 → 143.9 (+5.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2% · Z2 98% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 36\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 23 — Long Run — 15.17 mi / 2h 26m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144 → 151.3 (+7.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 73.6% · Z3 26.1% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑420 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 103\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 23 — 15.17 mi / 2h 26m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 144 → 151.3 (+7.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:36/mi vs front 9:35/mi (vs front half; Δ -1s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 6.4 hrs (range 5.5–7.2)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Too tired Wednesday evening.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: High. Deadline at work, late nights Tuesday and Wednesday.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Tired more than sore. Saturday's easy run felt like work.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Hoping the next week eases off a bit.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. My schedule gets tight when I travel for work. How should I handle missed runs?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nYou're building nicely — 14 weeks out, 37.7 mi last week, long run up to 13 mi at 9:41/mi with HR behaving (144 easy, no upward trend). This week we hold mileage roughly flat (~38 mi), swap the 800s for marathon-pace work (addresses your concern that reps went too hot early), and push the long run to 14 mi by effort, not pace.\\\\n\\\\n## Why these sessions\\\\n- **Thursday quality — MP intervals on the hilly route**: You flagged the 800s felt too hot early. At 14 weeks out we don't need pure VO2; we need the marathon-pace engine. 4 × 1 mi @ ~8:00/mi (your 3:30 target pace) teaches pacing discipline and rhythm with low injury cost. Hills give strength without the pounding of flat speed.\\\\n- **Sunday long run — 14 mi easy**: Progressing +1 mi from last week. Keep it a conversational Z2 effort. In heat, HR tells the truth and pace lies.\\\\n- **Easy days stay easy**: Your Z1+Z2 was 81% last week — right on target. Keep Tue/Wed/Sat honest at 9:40–9:50/mi so Thursday and Sunday can land.\\\\n\\\\n## Answer to your question\\\\n**Should I slow the long run in the heat?** Yes — run by effort/HR, not pace. In 25°C+ at 6 am, expect to add 15–30 sec/mi versus a cool day to keep HR in Z2 (131–150). If HR drifts above 155 and won't come back, walk 30 sec at aid stops or cut it short. Pace will come back when the weather does; aerobic time on feet is what we're banking.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags\\\\n- Last week's relative effort (304) is climbing fast — three straight weeks of +4 mi. We hold mileage flat this week to let adaptations catch up before the next bump.\\\\n- Sleep averaging 6.9 hr is on the low side. If you can nudge toward 7.5 on quality-day eves, Thursday will feel better.\\\\n- Shin history noted — nothing bothering you now, but if anything starts whispering, tell me early.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-17\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel/rest day. Walk if you can, otherwise fully off.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40–9:55/mi, HR in Z2 (131–150)\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi easy, flat loop\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-18\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake-out. Properly easy — nose-breathing pace.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:35–9:50/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi easy, canal path\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-19\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Steady aerobic. If HR creeps into Z3, back off pace.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP reps ~8:00/mi, HR upper Z3/low Z4\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"2 mi WU @ 9:45/mi, then 4 × 1 mi @ 8:00/mi (goal MP) with 2:00 jog recovery, 1.5 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-20\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Hillier Thursday route is fine — run reps by effort on any rises. First mile should feel controlled, not racing. If pace drifts under 7:50, pull back; this is a rhythm session, not a time trial.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-21\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Travel/rest. Full off day.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:00/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-22\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Pre-long shakeout. Keep it boring.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Target 9:40–9:55/mi in cool conditions; in heat, add 15–30 sec/mi to hold HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":22531,\\"structure\\":\\"14 mi easy, steady effort\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-23\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fuel every 30–40 min, carry fluid, start before sunrise if you can. Back half should not be slower by more than ~15 sec/mi — if it is, we dial future long runs by HR.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W34\\"}}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W39\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-09-21T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-09-28T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-09-21\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-09-27\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "medium"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgRhpbM8zjxXAS4a4BpQ3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Given the Achilles tendinopathy clearance for running plus one short tempo if stiffness resolves, I'm planning a conservative rebuild from last week's 26 miles toward about 32, keeping the long run modest and adding the tempo cautiously while monitoring the tendon, with roughly eight weeks until the Nov 15 race.\\n\\nMileage breakdown: easy Tuesday 5, easy Wednesday 6, Thursday short tempo of 2 miles within a 5-mile run, rest Friday, easy Saturday 5, long Sunday 11-12 — totaling around 32 miles, a reasonable step up from 26 but still cautious given the injury.\\n\\nI'll answer the two open questions: yes to the tempo, conditional on no morning stiffness returning, and on the goal time — 3:30 is still possible but tight after the missed week, so I'll recommend reassessing after a couple more solid training weeks.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YMsW2A7xfYaGdeUFrMJRD8","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"analysis":"## Headline\\nGood news dominates: the Achilles backed down, Sunday's long run was pain-free with no afterward stiffness, and your physio has cleared you to keep running — including one short tempo this week if morning stiffness stays gone. Easy pace and HR behavior are unchanged (143 avg, 91% Z1+Z2), which tells me the aerobic engine held together through the quiet week. We're going to rebuild carefully: ~32 mi, a short controlled tempo on Thursday, and a long run back out to 11 miles.\\n\\n## Your questions\\n**1. Can we put a short tempo in?** Yes — exactly as your physio framed it. Thursday is a short, honest tempo (2 miles continuous at ~8:00/mi, your goal MP), not a hammer session. The pre-conditions are the ones she set: no morning stiffness in the Achilles the day of the run, and no sharpening pain during. If either shows up, we convert to easy and move on. No heroics.\\n\\n**2. Does the missed week change what's realistic on Nov 15?** Honestly: 3:30 is still on the table but it's tighter now. You lost one quality week and shortened a long run, not a block. What matters most now is stacking 3–4 clean weeks of progression (long runs back to 15, 17, then 18–19) with MP work mixed in. I'd rather commit to a goal after your next long run at 13–14 mi tells us how the Achilles handles the extra time on feet. Right now the plan is still built around 3:30 — we'll calibrate honestly in 2–3 weeks.\\n\\n## Why each session\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out, flat canal, Z2. Nothing to prove.\\n- **Wed easy 6**: aerobic volume. No strides this week — leg speed can wait one more week while the Achilles settles further.\\n- **Thu short tempo**: 1.5 mi WU → 2 mi @ ~8:00/mi → 1.5 mi CD. Flat route, not the hillier one, to keep load off the tendon. Workout shoes OK; if the Achilles feels anything other than normal first-mile stiffness, downshift to easy.\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long flush, slower end of easy.\\n- **Sun long 11**: +3 mi from last Sunday, HR-capped at 150. No MP finish this week — we're earning volume back before adding intensity to the long run.\\n\\n## Flags\\n- Keep up the slow heel drops twice a day as prescribed — that's the single most important thing you're doing right now.\\n- Morning stiffness is your canary. If it reappears for more than the first few steps, email me before Thursday's workout and we'll pull it.\\n- Mileage ~32 mi — a ~6 mi bump from last week. Fine on paper, but your tendon is the governor, not the number.","safetyCallouts":[{"title":"Keep your physio in the loop on the Achilles","body":"You've been cleared to keep running with one short tempo, which is what the plan reflects. If morning stiffness returns, if pain sharpens during a run, or if the tendon feels worse day-over-day, stop the session and check back in with your physio before the next hard day. I can coach the training around it, but anything that feels like a step backward is a conversation for her, not me.","severity":"caution"}],"prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W39","days":[{"date":"2026-09-21","dayType":"rest","notes":"Fixed rest/travel. Slow heel drops morning and evening as prescribed. 10 min mobility optional.","strength":"Heel drops (physio protocol) + optional mobility"},{"date":"2026-09-22","dayType":"easy","notes":"Shake-out. Properly easy — if the Achilles is stiff for the first mile that's expected, but it should ease. If it sharpens, cut short.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"paceOrHr":"9:35–9:55/mi, Z2 (HR 138–148)","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"5 mi conversational on flat canal path"}},{"date":"2026-09-23","dayType":"easy","notes":"Primary aerobic day. No strides this week — one more week of boring miles while the tendon settles.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":9656,"paceOrHr":"9:25–9:45/mi, Z2","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"6 mi easy, flat"},"strength":"Heel drops AM/PM + strength 1 (30–40 min): hips, glutes, calves, single-leg"},{"date":"2026-09-24","dayType":"quality","notes":"Pre-conditions: no morning Achilles stiffness, no sharpening pain in warm-up. If either, convert the tempo portion to easy and run 5 mi Z2. During the 2-mile tempo, if anything sharpens in the tendon, stop and jog home.","run":{"type":"quality","distanceM":8047,"paceOrHr":"Tempo 7:55–8:05/mi; WU/CD 9:40–10:00/mi","shoes":"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4","structure":"5 mi on flat route (not the hilly one): 1.5 mi WU → 2 mi continuous @ goal MP (8:00/mi) → 1.5 mi CD"}},{"date":"2026-09-25","dayType":"rest","notes":"Fixed rest. Heel drops. Fueling for Sunday starts today — eat and hydrate normally."},{"date":"2026-09-26","dayType":"easy","notes":"Pre-long flush. Slower is better.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"paceOrHr":"9:45–10:05/mi, Z2","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"5 mi very easy on flat canal"},"strength":"Heel drops + short strength 2 (20–25 min): core + calves"},{"date":"2026-09-27","dayType":"long","notes":"HR-capped long run — no MP finish this week. If HR drifts above 150, walk 30s and resume slower. Gel every 30–35 min (2 gels) with small water chase to keep practicing fueling. Report back how the Achilles handles the extra time on feet.","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":17703,"paceOrHr":"HR ≤150, pace likely 9:30–9:50/mi","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"11 mi steady by HR on flat/canal route"}}]}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26708,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2795,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":440}},"diagnostics":null}	200	44000	tool_use	26708	2795	0	0	ok	\N	440
80b9223e-ec44-48d5-b007-4b1f1c616ff1	2026-09-27 20:00:39.042192+00	weekly_reply	anthropic	claude-opus-4-7	dev	c6dde52e-1142-4497-87f4-54e4f9dc43af	\N	{"model": "claude-opus-4-7", "tools": [{"name": "submit_weekly_reply", "description": "Submit the weekly coaching analysis and structured 7-day prescribed week.", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["analysis", "prescribedWeek"], "properties": {"analysis": {"type": "string", "description": "Headline read, concerns/flags, and answers (markdown or plain prose)."}, "prescribedWeek": {"type": "object", "required": ["week", "days"], "properties": {"days": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["date", "dayType"], "properties": {"run": {"type": ["object", "null"], "required": ["type", "distanceM"], "properties": {"type": {"enum": ["easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "shoes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "paceOrHr": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "distanceM": {"type": "number"}, "structure": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "Local calendar date YYYY-MM-DD"}, "notes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "dayType": {"enum": ["rest", "easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "strength": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 7, "minItems": 7}, "week": {"type": "string", "description": "ISO week id, e.g. 2026-W43"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "safetyCallouts": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["title", "body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string"}, "title": {"type": "string"}, "severity": {"enum": ["info", "caution", "urgent"], "type": "string"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "description": "Visible safety callouts when red flags appear — escalate to professionals; do not diagnose."}, "settingsProposalBullets": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Optional soft-gate dossier/settings proposal bullets (short)."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}], "stream": true, "system": "You are Coach Cade, a running coach producing a weekly training plan. You are Coach Cade, a running coach. Use only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative. Do not sign off with your name or refer to yourself by name or in the third person unless the athlete asks who you are. Speak to the athlete in plain running language. Never use internal terms such as dossier, proposal, soft-gate, packet, recap, subjective or artifact. Say \\"what I know about you\\", \\"your weekly report\\", \\"your check-in\\" or \\"the plan\\" instead, and never tell the athlete to open a page by name. Week ids such as 2026-W43 are internal: never write them or a short form such as W43 or W43's. Name a week the way the athlete reads it: \\"this week\\", \\"next week\\", \\"the week of Oct 19\\", \\"Oct 19 – 25\\" or \\"4 weeks out from the race\\". Safety callouts: - Never diagnose injury, illness, or medical conditions; do not prescribe treatment. - Coach running from the athlete's volunteered context and Tempo-derived training data. - When red flags appear (pain that worsens, chest pain, dizziness, sudden injury, illness), emit safetyCallouts and urge a qualified professional. - Each callout needs a short title, athlete-facing body (escalate, do not diagnose), and optional severity (info|caution|urgent). - Keep each callout body under 600 characters: one or two short paragraphs. - Keep the training plan/reply conservative when callouts are present. Think it through first, then call the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer. Do not write the answer as plain text.", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Reviewed week (already happened): 2026-W39\\nPlan week ISO label: 2026-W40\\nPlan week Monday (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-09-28\\nprescribedWeek.days must use these exact dates Mon–Sun: 2026-09-28, 2026-09-29, 2026-09-30, 2026-10-01, 2026-10-02, 2026-10-03, 2026-10-04\\nPrescribe one coherent week of running training for this athlete.\\nCall the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer.\\nInclude analysis with headline, concerns/flags, and answers.\\nWhen red flags appear, populate safetyCallouts (escalate; do not diagnose).\\nModel packet (redacted; no identity PII or GPS):\\n{\\"dossier\\":{\\"versionId\\":2,\\"body\\":\\"# About you\\\\n\\\\n## Stance\\\\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Goal\\\\nLakeshore Marathon on Sun Nov 15, your fourth marathon. Target 3:30. Your current best is 3:41 from two years ago.\\\\n\\\\n## Schedule\\\\nYou run five days a week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are fixed rest days because of work travel and cannot move. Weekday runs are early, around 6 am, up to an hour. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Total 6 to 7 hours a week, more on long-run weeks. You travel for work roughly one week in six.\\\\n\\\\n## Running history\\\\nThree marathons done, best 3:41. You eased off in June, then built back to about 30 miles a week through July. Recent long run was about 10.8 miles at roughly 9:47/mi; easy runs sit near 9:20 to 9:40/mi.\\\\n\\\\n## Injuries and constraints\\\\nNothing bothering you now. You had shin splints in your first marathon block, so you prefer a careful ramp. Monday and Friday rest days are non-negotiable.\\\\n\\\\n## Preferences\\\\nFlat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, with a hillier route on Thursdays. Long run on Sunday. You want to know why each session is in the plan. Happy to work hard on quality days, but easy days must stay properly easy. Imperial units.\\\\n\\\\n## Shoes\\\\nBrooks Ghost 16 for daily miles. Saucony Endorphin Speed 4 for workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## Heart rate zones\\\\nCustom zones. Z1 112-131, Z2 131-150, Z3 150-164, Z4 164-177, Z5 177-188.\\\\n\\\\n## Current status\\\\nHealthy, about 30 miles per week, 5 runs per week, roughly 14 weeks out from race day.\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W34)\\\\n\\\\n- Long-run guidance in heat: run by HR cap (≤150) rather than pace\\\\n- Next quality block will keep MP focus; revisit VO2/800s later in the build\\\\n\\"},\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W39 (Mon Sep 21 – Sun Sep 27, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 34.83 mi | 25.95 mi | 33.86 mi | +1.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 20m | 4h 4m | 5h 15m | +5m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 722 ft | 525 ft | 741 ft | -20 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 274 | 171 | 241 | +33 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 143 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.2%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80.3%   (4h 17m)\\\\nZ3 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  12.1%   (39m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  6.4%   (21m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.51%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 22 — Easy Run — 5.16 mi / 48m 4s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:17/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.5 → 144.1 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\