5 ft | 762 ft | -237 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 171 | 225 | 275 | -104 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 143 | 144 | 144 | -1 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 ███████████████████████████████░░░░  89.7%   (3h 39m)\\\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  8.8%   (22m)\\\\nZ4 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **91.18%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 15 — Easy Run — 4.13 mi / 38m 32s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 144.2 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑82 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 6/10  ·  Pain: Slight tightness for the first half mile, about a 2 out of 10.\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 16 — Easy Run — 4.83 mi / 45m 6s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:12/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.8 → 150.6 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 84.3% · Z3 15.7% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 32\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10  ·  Pain: A hint of it at the start only.\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 17 — Easy Run — 4.99 mi / 46m 53s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:23/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138 → 143.7 (+5.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑135 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Achilles fine on the flat. Easy only this week.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 19 — Easy Run — 4.07 mi / 38m 48s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:31/mi  ·  Avg HR 141 (75% max)  ·  Max HR 146  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.9 → 143.2 (+5.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑112 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 20 — Long Run — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147 (78.2% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.7% · Z2 80.1% · Z3 19.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 52\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 20 — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147  ·  Drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:18/mi vs front 9:15/mi (vs front half; Δ -3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi ▁▃██\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 143 ▁▁▁█\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi ▃█▃▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.5 hrs (range 6.9–8.2)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2 (Calf raises and slow heel drops.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low. Easier at work.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: The Achilles is a lot better. Nothing at all on Saturday or Sunday, and not stiff afterwards. Saw a sports physio on Wednesday: mild Achilles tendinopathy, nothing torn. She cleared me to keep running, gave me slow heel drops twice a day, and said one short tempo next week is fine if the morning stiffness stays gone.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Better. Frustrated about the missing miles but I can live with it.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. The physio is happy for me to try a short tempo next week. Can we put one in?\\\\n2. Does the missed week change what is realistic for race day?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nWe're pulling back this week. The Achilles signal on Thursday — tight from mile 2, sharper when you picked up the pace, enough to stop and walk home — is exactly the kind of thing we treat conservatively right now, not push through. You still got a solid 10-miler in on Sunday with no pain while running, which is a good sign, but stiffness afterward tells me the tissue is irritated. We lose nothing by taking 7–10 easy days here. We lose the whole block if we poke it.\\\\n\\\\nPlan this week: no tempo, no MP work, no hills, all flat, all Ghost 16. Shorter easy runs, a modest long run capped by feel, and a hard stop rule if symptoms escalate. We're 9 weeks from Lakeshore — plenty of runway to rebuild quality if the Achilles settles.\\\\n\\\\n## Your questions\\\\n\\\\n**\\\\\\"Should I stop running for a few days, or keep going with easy runs?\\\\\\"**\\\\nIf pain is ≤3/10, not sharp, and eases within the first mile (like Saturday), easy running on flats is usually fine and can actually help. If it's sharp, worsens as you run, changes your gait, or lingers/worsens after — stop that day and take 2–3 full days off. The tempo-day pattern (fine easy, bad with pace) is the key signal: speed is off the menu until it's quiet for a full week.\\\\n\\\\n**\\\\\\"How do I know if this is serious?\\\\\\"**\\\\nI'm a coach, not a clinician, so I can't diagnose this — and I won't try. What I can tell you is which signs mean \\\\\\"see a sports physio or sports medicine doc this week, don't wait\\\\\\": sharp or stabbing pain, pain that worsens run-over-run, morning pain in the first steps out of bed that doesn't ease, visible swelling or a lump, pain squeezing the tendon, or any change in how your foot pushes off. If any of those show up, please book an appointment — early assessment on Achilles stuff is cheap insurance. See the callout below.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags\\\\n- Tempo Thursday: tightness → sharper with pace → stopped at 3 mi. Clear signal from the tissue.\\\\n- Sunday long run was pain-free running but stiff after — tendon is grumbling, not screaming. That's the window to be smart.\\\\n- Mileage already came off (31 vs 44) — don't rush it back. Reload gradually once symptoms are quiet.\\\\n- Sleep 7 hrs, stress moderate, anxious about the block — I hear you. One cautious week does not throw away a marathon. Grinding on an angry Achilles can.\\\\n- Shoes: all easy miles in Ghost 16. Keep the Endorphin Speed 4 in the closet until we're back doing workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## How to read this week\\\\n- Each run, do a 5-minute walk warm-up before you start running. Flat routes only — the hilly Thursday loop is out.\\\\n- Pain rules every day: ≤3/10 and not sharp = continue; sharp, worsening, or altering your gait = stop and walk home. Report back what you felt in the check-in.\\\\n- No strides, no pickups, no hills, no MP touches. Pure easy aerobic.\\\\n- If two consecutive runs hurt more than the one before, stop running and get it looked at before the next session.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-14\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Gentle calf and ankle mobility is fine — no aggressive stretching of the Achilles, no eccentric heel drops this week unless a clinician has prescribed them.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40–10:00/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min brisk walk warm-up, then 4 mi very easy on the flat canal path. No strides. No pickups.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-15\\",\\"notes\\":\\"This is the test run. If the Achilles stays ≤3/10 and quiets as you go, finish the 4. If it sharpens or alters your stride, walk home and we treat Wednesday as rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40–10:00/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 5 mi flat canal path, conversational.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-16\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Only run this if Tuesday was clean. If any pain lingered after Tuesday, swap today for rest or 30 min easy cross-train (bike/elliptical, no running).\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Short core + hip session, 20 min. Skip any heavy calf loading this week.\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:05/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 4 mi flat and easy. Not the hilly route — flat only.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-17\\",\\"notes\\":\\"This replaces the tempo. No pace work, no hills. If the Achilles has been quiet all week this is just an easy aerobic day; if it's grumbling, make it 30 min easy cross-train instead and don't force the run.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-18\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Normal eating, hydrate. Use the day to honestly check in with how the tendon feels on stairs and first steps in the morning — that's useful info.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:05/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 4 mi flat and easy.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-19\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Pre-long shakeout. If anything felt off Thursday, cut this to 3 mi or skip.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:00/mi, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":14484,\\"structure\\":\\"9 mi flat and easy, out-and-back on the canal path. No MP work, no fast finish. Walk 30s at mile 3 and mile 6 as a check-in — how does the Achilles feel? If any sharpness, cut it short and walk back.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-20\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Down from 10 last week on purpose. Keep practicing fueling — gel every 30–35 min, fluids with electrolytes. This is a feel-it-out long run, not a progression.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W38\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W37\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"77bbe22a-17ad-41ee-9fa5-7b4ffd625118\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W37 (Mon Sep 7 – Sun Sep 13, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 31.22 mi | 44.41 mi | 40.23 mi | -9.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 4h 51m | 6h 49m | 6h 17m | -1h 26m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 745 ft | 955 ft | 843 ft | -98 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 225 | 328 | 314 | -89 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.5%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ██████████████████████████████░░░░░  87.1%   (4h 14m)\\\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  9.3%   (27m)\\\\nZ4 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  2.1%   (6m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **88.64%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 8 — Easy Run — 6.03 mi / 56m 24s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.2 → 144 (+4.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1.8% · Z2 98.2% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑167 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 39\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 9 — Easy Run — 8.20 mi / 1h 16m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 146.1 → 150.2 (+4.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 90.7% · Z3 9.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑233 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 53\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 10 — Tempo Run — 3.10 mi / 28m 1s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:02/mi  ·  Avg HR 145 (77.1% max)  ·  Max HR 177  ·  Cad 350 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:36/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 133.5 → 169.4 (+35.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 7.1% · Z2 66% · Z3 5.4% · Z4 21.5% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑10 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 42\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Right Achilles tight from mile 2. Stopped at 3.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 3/10  ·  Pain: Right Achilles tight from about mile 2 of the session. Got sharper as I picked up the pace, so I stopped at 3 miles and walked home.\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 12 — Easy Run — 3.89 mi / 37m 24s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:36/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:28/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.8 → 144 (+6.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.7% · Z2 97.3% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 26\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 5/10  ·  Pain: Achilles stiff for the first mile, eased after that. About a 3 out of 10.\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 13 — Long Run — 10.00 mi / 1h 33m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 147 (78.2% max)  ·  Max HR 155  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.1 → 150.9 (+7.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.5% · Z2 79.7% · Z3 19.8% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑233 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 65\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 6/10  ·  Pain: No pain while running. Stiff getting out of the car afterwards.\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 13 — 10.00 mi / 1h 33m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 147  ·  Drift: 143.1 → 150.9 (+7.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:16/mi vs front 9:18/mi (vs front half; Δ +2s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi █▁█▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7 hrs (range 6.2–7.7)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Skipped the second one to rest the legs.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate. Worried about the Achilles.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Right Achilles, just above the heel. Tight and a bit tender to press. No swelling that I can see. It was fine until the tempo.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Anxious. I don't want to throw away the block over this.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Should I stop running for a few days, or keep going with easy runs?\\\\n2. How do I know if this is serious?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nBreakthrough week. 44.4 mi, long run out to 16.1 with a sharp MP finish (back half 9:07 vs front 9:25), and you said marathon pace felt controlled for the first time. That's the switch flipping. HR behavior on easy days is unchanged (144, rock steady) even as easy pace keeps improving — your aerobic engine is where we want it ~10 weeks out.\\\\n\\\\nWe're going to lean into it this week: hold volume around 45 mi, push the long run to 17 with a short MP finish, and do a stronger MP interval session on Thursday. Nothing exotic — just more of what's working.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags / things I'm watching\\\\n- **Long-run HR drift Sunday: +13.4 bpm (144 → 157)**, above the ≤10 target. Front end was honest Z2 but the two MP miles at the end plus heat pushed drift up. That's acceptable *because* of the MP close, but it means I don't want to chase both big distance AND a long MP finish in the same week yet. This week: more distance, shorter MP close.\\\\n- **Z1+Z2 at 74.6%** — a touch below the 80% base target. Driven by the MP run and the long-run finish, not by easy days creeping. Keep Tue/Wed/Sat genuinely easy and we're fine.\\\\n- **Mileage jump of +10.7 mi over the week prior**. We don't want to stack another big jump on top; this week holds roughly flat.\\\\n- Shin history noted — nothing bothering you, but if anything whispers, tell me early.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — gels on the long run\\\\nYes, start now. You're 10 weeks out and race-day fueling is a skill you have to practice. Rules of thumb:\\\\n- Take a gel **every 30–35 minutes**, starting around minute 30. On a 17-miler that's roughly 4 gels.\\\\n- Chase with a few sips of water (not sports drink with the gel — too much sugar at once can backfire).\\\\n- Pick one or two brands and stick with them through the block so race day is boring and predictable.\\\\n- Target ~30–60 g of carbs per hour this block; we can push toward 60–80 g/hr closer to race day if your gut tolerates it.\\\\n- If you get GI distress, note which gel and we adjust.\\\\n\\\\n## Why each session\\\\n- **Tue easy 6**: shake-out, Z2, flat canal. Nothing to prove.\\\\n- **Wed easy 9 + strides**: your bread-and-butter midweek aerobic session. 6×20s strides after keep leg speed alive without cost.\\\\n- **Thu quality — 2 × 2 mi @ MP**: step up from last block's 1-mile reps. Longer continuous time at 8:00/mi so the pace stops feeling like a workout and starts feeling like cruising. Hilly route is fine; hold effort on climbs.\\\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long flush.\\\\n- **Sun long 17 with 3 mi MP finish**: +1 mi distance, slightly longer MP close than last week. HR-cap the first 14 (≤150), then roll into 8:00/mi for the last 3. Fuel plan above.\\\\n\\\\nTotal ~45 mi.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-07\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest/travel. 10 min mobility if you feel like it — ankles, hips, calves.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Optional mobility (10 min)\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:35–9:55/mi, Z2 (HR 138–148)\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi conversational on the canal path\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-08\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake-out after Sunday's effort. Genuinely easy — no pushing even if legs feel bouncy.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:25–9:45/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":14484,\\"structure\\":\\"9 mi easy + 6×20s strides on flat with full walk recovery after the run\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-09\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Midweek aerobic session. Strides are relaxed turnover — not sprints.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 1 (30–40 min): hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP reps 7:55–8:05/mi; WU/CD 9:40–10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi total on hilly route. 2 mi warm-up → 2 × 2 mi @ goal MP (8:00/mi) with 3:00 easy jog between → 1.5 mi cool-down\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-10\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Step up from 1-mile reps to 2-mile reps. First rep should feel controlled, not racing — if mile 1 is already under 7:50, pull back. On hills: hold effort, let pace drift 5–10 sec.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-11\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Hydrate and eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts today.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:05/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi very easy on flat canal path\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-12\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Pre-long flush. Slower is better.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 2 (20–25 min): core + calves. Skip if legs are flat.\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"First 14 mi: HR ≤150, pace likely 9:30–9:50/mi. Last 3 mi: 7:55–8:05/mi (goal MP)\\",\\"distanceM\\":27359,\\"structure\\":\\"17 mi: 14 mi easy/steady by HR, then 3 mi at goal MP to finish. Bail on the MP close if HR is already past 160 at mile 14 — heat and fatigue trump the pace target.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-13\\",\\"notes\\":\\"First 14 mi HR-capped at 150 — if HR drifts above, walk 30s and resume slower. Then roll into 8:00/mi for the last 3. Start pre-sunrise if warm. Fuel: gel every 30–35 min (4 gels total), small water chase. Note how your gut handles each one.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W37\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W36\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"140f5949-e890-44f8-9296-6ffd441831a4\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W36 (Mon Aug 31 – Sun Sep 6, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 44.41 mi | 33.72 mi | 38.00 mi | +6.4 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 6h 49m | 5h 18m | 6h 0m | +49m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 955 ft | 587 ft | 773 ft | +182 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 328 | 271 | 306 | +22 |\\\\n| Avg eas