%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑230 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 78\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 27 — 11.94 mi / 1h 51m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 142.7 → 151.6 (+8.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:12/mi vs front 9:15/mi (vs front half; Δ +3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi → 9:20/mi ▁▅▅█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 143 → 144 ▁▁█▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi → 11.94 mi █▃▁▃\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.4 hrs (range 6.8–8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Nothing. I kept checking for the Achilles on the tempo and it was fine.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Relieved and ready to build again.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is there anything I should keep doing for the Achilles through race day?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nGood news dominates: the Achilles backed down, Sunday's long run was pain-free with no afterward stiffness, and your physio has cleared you to keep running — including one short tempo this week if morning stiffness stays gone. Easy pace and HR behavior are unchanged (143 avg, 91% Z1+Z2), which tells me the aerobic engine held together through the quiet week. We're going to rebuild carefully: ~32 mi, a short controlled tempo on Thursday, and a long run back out to 11 miles.\\\\n\\\\n## Your questions\\\\n**1. Can we put a short tempo in?** Yes — exactly as your physio framed it. Thursday is a short, honest tempo (2 miles continuous at ~8:00/mi, your goal MP), not a hammer session. The pre-conditions are the ones she set: no morning stiffness in the Achilles the day of the run, and no sharpening pain during. If either shows up, we convert to easy and move on. No heroics.\\\\n\\\\n**2. Does the missed week change what's realistic on Nov 15?** Honestly: 3:30 is still on the table but it's tighter now. You lost one quality week and shortened a long run, not a block. What matters most now is stacking 3–4 clean weeks of progression (long runs back to 15, 17, then 18–19) with MP work mixed in. I'd rather commit to a goal after your next long run at 13–14 mi tells us how the Achilles handles the extra time on feet. Right now the plan is still built around 3:30 — we'll calibrate honestly in 2–3 weeks.\\\\n\\\\n## Why each session\\\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out, flat canal, Z2. Nothing to prove.\\\\n- **Wed easy 6**: aerobic volume. No strides this week — leg speed can wait one more week while the Achilles settles further.\\\\n- **Thu short tempo**: 1.5 mi WU → 2 mi @ ~8:00/mi → 1.5 mi CD. Flat route, not the hillier one, to keep load off the tendon. Workout shoes OK; if the Achilles feels anything other than normal first-mile stiffness, downshift to easy.\\\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long flush, slower end of easy.\\\\n- **Sun long 11**: +3 mi from last Sunday, HR-capped at 150. No MP finish this week — we're earning volume back before adding intensity to the long run.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags\\\\n- Keep up the slow heel drops twice a day as prescribed — that's the single most important thing you're doing right now.\\\\n- Morning stiffness is your canary. If it reappears for more than the first few steps, email me before Thursday's workout and we'll pull it.\\\\n- Mileage ~32 mi — a ~6 mi bump from last week. Fine on paper, but your tendon is the governor, not the number.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-21\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest/travel. Slow heel drops morning and evening as prescribed. 10 min mobility optional.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Heel drops (physio protocol) + optional mobility\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:35–9:55/mi, Z2 (HR 138–148)\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi conversational on flat canal path\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-22\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake-out. Properly easy — if the Achilles is stiff for the first mile that's expected, but it should ease. If it sharpens, cut short.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:25–9:45/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi easy, flat\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-23\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Primary aerobic day. No strides this week — one more week of boring miles while the tendon settles.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Heel drops AM/PM + strength 1 (30–40 min): hips, glutes, calves, single-leg\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Tempo 7:55–8:05/mi; WU/CD 9:40–10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi on flat route (not the hilly one): 1.5 mi WU → 2 mi continuous @ goal MP (8:00/mi) → 1.5 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-24\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Pre-conditions: no morning Achilles stiffness, no sharpening pain in warm-up. If either, convert the tempo portion to easy and run 5 mi Z2. During the 2-mile tempo, if anything sharpens in the tendon, stop and jog home.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-25\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Heel drops. Fueling for Sunday starts today — eat and hydrate normally.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:05/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi very easy on flat canal\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-26\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Pre-long flush. Slower is better.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Heel drops + short strength 2 (20–25 min): core + calves\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"HR ≤150, pace likely 9:30–9:50/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":17703,\\"structure\\":\\"11 mi steady by HR on flat/canal route\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-27\\",\\"notes\\":\\"HR-capped long run — no MP finish this week. If HR drifts above 150, walk 30s and resume slower. Gel every 30–35 min (2 gels) with small water chase to keep practicing fueling. Report back how the Achilles handles the extra time on feet.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W39\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W38\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"0876b9b6-d823-4b3e-97fb-b670672066db\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W38 (Mon Sep 14 – Sun Sep 20, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 25.95 mi | 31.22 mi | 36.45 mi | -10.5 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 4h 4m | 4h 51m | 5h 39m | -1h 35m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 525 ft | 745 ft | 762 ft | -237 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 171 | 225 | 275 | -104 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 143 | 144 | 144 | -1 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 ███████████████████████████████░░░░  89.7%   (3h 39m)\\\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  8.8%   (22m)\\\\nZ4 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **91.18%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 15 — Easy Run — 4.13 mi / 38m 32s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 144.2 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑82 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 6/10  ·  Pain: Slight tightness for the first half mile, about a 2 out of 10.\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 16 — Easy Run — 4.83 mi / 45m 6s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:12/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.8 → 150.6 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 84.3% · Z3 15.7% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 32\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10  ·  Pain: A hint of it at the start only.\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 17 — Easy Run — 4.99 mi / 46m 53s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:23/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138 → 143.7 (+5.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑135 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Achilles fine on the flat. Easy only this week.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 19 — Easy Run — 4.07 mi / 38m 48s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:31/mi  ·  Avg HR 141 (75% max)  ·  Max HR 146  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.9 → 143.2 (+5.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑112 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 20 — Long Run — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147 (78.2% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.7% · Z2 80.1% · Z3 19.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 52\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 20 — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147  ·  Drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:18/mi vs front 9:15/mi (vs front half; Δ -3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi ▁▃██\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 143 ▁▁▁█\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi ▃█▃▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.5 hrs (range 6.9–8.2)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2 (Calf raises and slow heel drops.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low. Easier at work.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: The Achilles is a lot better. Nothing at all on Saturday or Sunday, and not stiff afterwards. Saw a sports physio on Wednesday: mild Achilles tendinopathy, nothing torn. She cleared me to keep running, gave me slow heel drops twice a day, and said one short tempo next week is fine if the morning stiffness stays gone.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Better. Frustrated about the missing miles but I can live with it.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. The physio is happy for me to try a short tempo next week. Can we put one in?\\\\n2. Does the missed week change what is realistic for race day?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nWe're pulling back this week. The Achilles signal on Thursday — tight from mile 2, sharper when you picked up the pace, enough to stop and walk home — is exactly the kind of thing we treat conservatively right now, not push through. You still got a solid 10-miler in on Sunday with no pain while running, which is a good sign, but stiffness afterward tells me the tissue is irritated. We lose nothing by taking 7–10 easy days here. We lose the whole block if we poke it.\\\\n\\\\nPlan this week: no tempo, no MP work, no hills, all flat, all Ghost 16. Shorter easy runs, a modest long run capped by feel, and a hard stop rule if symptoms escalate. We're 9 weeks from Lakeshore — plenty of runway to rebuild quality if the Achilles settles.\\\\n\\\\n## Your questions\\\\n\\\\n**\\\\\\"Should I stop running for a few days, or keep going with easy runs?\\\\\\"**\\\\nIf pain is ≤3/10, not sharp, and eases within the first mile (like Saturday), easy running on flats is usually fine and can actually help. If it's sharp, worsens as you run, changes your gait, or lingers/worsens after — stop that day and take 2–3 full days off. The tempo-day pattern (fine easy, bad with pace) is the key signal: speed is off the menu until it's quiet for a full week.\\\\n\\\\n**\\\\\\"How do I know if this is serious?\\\\\\"**\\\\nI'm a coach, not a clinician, so I can't diagnose this — and I won't try. What I can tell you is which signs mean \\\\\\"see a sports physio or sports medicine doc this week, don't wait\\\\\\": sharp or stabbing pain, pain that worsens run-over-run, morning pain in the first steps out of bed that doesn't ease, visible swelling or a lump, pain squeezing the tendon, or any change in how your foot pushes off. If any of those show up, please book an appointment — early assessment on Achilles stuff is cheap insurance. See the callout below.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags\\\\n- Tempo Thursday: tightness → sharper with pace → stopped at 3 mi. Clear signal from the tissue.\\\\n- Sunday long run was pain-free running but stiff after — tendon is grumbling, not screaming. That's the window to be smart.\\\\n- Mileage already came off (31 vs 44) — don't rush it back. Reload gradually once symptoms are quiet.\\\\n- Sleep 7 hrs, stress moderate, anxious about the block — I hear you. One cautious week does not throw away a marathon. Grinding on an angry Achilles can.\\\\n- Shoes: all easy miles in Ghost 16. Keep the Endorphin Speed 4 in the closet until we're back doing workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## How to read this week\\\\n- Each run, do a 5-minute walk warm-up before you start running. Flat routes only — the hilly Thursday loop is out.\\\\n- Pain rules every day: ≤3/10 and not sharp = continue; sharp, worsening, or altering your gait = stop and walk home. Report back what you felt in the check-in.\\\\n- No strides, no pickups, no hills, no MP touches. Pure easy aerobic.\\\\n- If two consecutive runs hurt more than the one before, stop running and get it looked at before the next session.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-14\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Gentle calf and ankle mobility is fine — no aggressive stretching of the Achilles, no eccentric heel drops this week unless a clinician has prescribed them.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40–10:00/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min brisk walk warm-up, then 4 mi very easy on the flat canal path. No strides. No pickups.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-15\\",\\"notes\\":\\"This is the test run. If the Achilles stays ≤3/10 and quiets as you go, finish the 4. If it sharpens or alters your stride, walk home and we treat Wednesday as rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40–10:00/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 5 mi flat canal path, conversational.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-16\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Only run this if Tuesday was clean. If any pain lingered after Tuesday, swap today for rest or 30 min easy cross-train (bike/elliptical, no running).\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Short core + hip session, 20 min. Skip any heavy calf loading this week.\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:05/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 4 mi flat and easy. Not the hilly route — flat only.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-17\\",\\"notes\\":\\"This replaces the tempo. No pace work, no hills. If the Achilles has been quiet all week this is just an easy aerobic day; if it's grumbling, make it 30 min easy cross-train instead and don't force the run.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-18\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Normal eating, hydrate. Use the day to honestly check in with how the tendon feels on stairs and first steps in the morning — that's useful info.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:05/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 4 mi flat and easy.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-19\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Pre-long shakeout. If anything felt off Thursday, cut this to 3 mi or skip.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:00/mi, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":14484,\\"structure\\":\\"9 mi flat and easy, out-and-back on the canal path. No MP work, no fast finish. Walk 30s at mile 3 and mile 6 as a check-in — how does the Achilles feel? If any sharpness, cut it short and walk back.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-20\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Down from 10 last week on purpose. Keep practicing fueling — gel every 30–35 min, fluids with electrolytes. This is a feel-it-out long run, not a progression.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W38\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W37\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"77bbe22a-17ad-41ee-9fa5-7b4ffd625118\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W37 (Mon Sep 7 – Sun Sep 13, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 31.22 mi | 44.41 mi | 40.23 mi | -9.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 4h 51m | 6h 49m | 6h 17m | -1h 26m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 745 ft | 955 ft | 843 ft | -98 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 225 | 328 | 314 | -89 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.5%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ██████████████████████████████░░░░░  87.1%   (4h 14m)\\\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  9.3%   (27m)\\\\nZ4 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  2.1%   (6m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **88.64%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 8 — Easy Run — 6.03 mi / 56m 24s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.2 → 144 (+4.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1.8% · Z2 98.2% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑167 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 39\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 9 — Easy Run — 8.20 mi / 1h 16m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 146.1 → 150.2 (+4.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 90.7% · Z3 9.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑233 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 53\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 10 — Tempo Run — 3.10 mi / 28m 1s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:02/mi  ·  Avg HR 145 (77.1% max)  ·  Max HR 177  ·  Cad 350 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:36/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 133.5 → 169.4 (+35.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 7.1% · Z2 66% · Z3 5.4% · Z4 21.5% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑10 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 42\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Right Achilles tight from mile 2. Stopped at 3.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 3/10  ·  Pain: Right Achilles tight from about mile 2 of the session. Got sharper as I picked up the pace, so I stopped at 3 miles and walked home.\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 12 — Easy Run — 3.89 mi / 37m 24s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:36/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:28/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.8 → 144 (+6.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.7% · Z2 97.3% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 26\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 5/10  ·  Pain: Achilles stiff for the first mile, eased after that. About a 3 out of 10.\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 13 — Long Run — 10.00 mi / 1h 33m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 147 (78.2% max)  ·  Max HR 155  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.1 → 150.9 (+7.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.5% · Z2 79.7% · Z3 19.8% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑233 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 65\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 6/10  ·  Pain: No pain while running. Stiff getting out of the car afterwards.\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 13 — 10.00 mi / 1h 33m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 147  ·  Drift: 143.1 → 150.9 (+7.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:16/mi vs front 9:18/mi (vs front half; Δ +2s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi █▁█▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7 hrs (range 6.2–7.7)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Skipped the second one to rest the legs.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate. Worried about the Achilles.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Right Achilles, just above the heel. Tight and a bit tender to press. No swelling that I can see. It was fine until the tempo.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Anxious. I don't want to throw away the block over this.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Should I stop running for a few days, or keep going with easy runs?\\\\n2. How do I know if this is serious?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nBreakthrough week. 44.4 mi, long run out to 16.1 with a sharp MP finish (back half 9:07 vs front 9:25), and you said marathon pace felt controlled for the first time. That's the switch flipping. HR behavior on easy days is unchanged (144, rock steady) even as easy pace keeps improving — your aerobic engine is where we want it ~10 weeks out.\\\\n\\\\nWe're going to lean into it this week: hold volume around 45 mi, push the long run to 17 with a short MP finish, and do a stronger MP interval session on Thursday. Nothing exotic — just more of what's working.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags / things I'm watching\\\\n- **Long-run HR drift Sunday: +13.4 bpm (144 → 157)**, above the ≤10 target. Front end was honest Z2 but the two MP miles at the end plus heat pushed drift up. That's acceptable *because* of the MP close, but it means I don't want to chase both big distance AND a long MP finish in the same week yet. This week: more distance, shorter MP close.\\\\n- **Z1+Z2 at 74.6%** — a touch below the 80% base target. Driven by the MP run and the long-run finish, not by easy days creeping. Keep Tue/Wed/Sat genuinely easy and we're fine.\\\\n- **Mileage jump of +10.7 mi over the week prior**. We don't want to stack another big jump on top; this week holds roughly flat.\\\\n- Shin history noted — nothing bothering you, but if anything whispers, tell me early.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — gels on the long run\\\\nYes, start now. You're 10 weeks out and race-day fueling is a skill you have to practice. Rules of thumb:\\\\n- Take a gel **every 30–35 minutes**, starting around minute 30. On a 17-miler that's roughly 4 gels.\\\\n- Chase with a few sips of water (not sports drink with the gel — too much sugar at once can backfire).\\\\n- Pick one or two brands and stick with them through the block so race day is boring and predictable.\\\\n- Target ~30–60 g of carbs per hour this block; we can push toward 60–80 g/hr closer to race day if your gut tolerates it.\\\\n- If you get GI distress, note which gel and we adjust.\\\\n\\\\n## Why each session\\\\n- **Tue easy 6**: shake-out, Z2, flat canal. Nothing to prove.\\\\n- **Wed easy 9 + strides**: your bread-and-butter midweek aerobic session. 6×20s strides after keep leg speed alive without cost.\\\\n- **Thu quality — 2 × 2 mi @ MP**: step up from last block's 1-mile reps. Longer continuous time at 8:00/mi so the pace stops feeling like a workout and starts feeling like cruising. Hilly route is fine; hold effort on climbs.\\\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long flush.\\\\n- **Sun long 17 with 3 mi MP finish**: +1 mi distance, slightly longer MP close than last week. HR-cap the first 14 (≤150), then roll into 8:00/mi for the last 3. Fuel plan above.\\\\n\\\\nTotal ~45 mi.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-07\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest/travel. 10 min mobility if you feel like it — ankles, hips, calves.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Optional mobility (10 min)\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:35–9:55/mi, Z2 (HR 138–148)\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi conversational on the canal path\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-08\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake-out after Sunday's effort. Genuinely easy — no pushing even if legs feel bouncy.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:25–9:45/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":14484,\\"structure\\":\\"9 mi easy + 6×20s strides on flat with full walk recovery after the run\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-09\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Midweek aerobic session. Strides are relaxed turnover — not sprints.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 1 (30–40 min): hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP reps 7:55–8:05/mi; WU/CD 9:40–10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi total on hilly route. 2 mi warm-up → 2 × 2 mi @ goal MP (8:00/mi) with 3:00 easy jog between → 1.5 mi cool-down\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-10\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Step up from 1-mile reps to 2-mile reps. First rep should feel controlled, not racing — if mile 1 is already under 7:50, pull back. On hills: hold effort, let pace drift 5–10 sec.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-11\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Hydrate and eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts today.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:05/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi very easy on flat canal path\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-12\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Pre-long flush. Slower is better.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 2 (20–25 min): core + calves. Skip if legs are flat.\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"First 14 mi: HR ≤150, pace likely 9:30–9:50/mi. Last 3 mi: 7:55–8:05/mi (goal MP)\\",\\"distanceM\\":27359,\\"structure\\":\\"17 mi: 14 mi easy/steady by HR, then 3 mi at goal MP to finish. Bail on the MP close if HR is already past 160 at mile 14 — heat and fatigue trump the pace target.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-13\\",\\"notes\\":\\"First 14 mi HR-capped at 150 — if HR drifts above, walk 30s and resume slower. Then roll into 8:00/mi for the last 3. Start pre-sunrise if warm. Fuel: gel every 30–35 min (4 gels total), small water chase. Note how your gut handles each one.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W37\\"}}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W42\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-10-19T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-10-12\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-10-18\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "xhigh"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgRi3mUCvVstFdTAgdaga","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm reviewing the athlete's situation: targeting a 3:30 marathon on Nov 15 with a 3:41 PR, following a 5-day weekly schedule with fixed rest days, having just completed a strong 44.97-mile week capped by a 20-miler with a marathon-pace finish, now about five weeks from race day.\\n\\nCounting forward from this week (Oct 12-18) to race day confirms exactly four weeks remain, placing this week at the start of a critical peak phase. Something stands out though—Thursday's workout was logged as an \\"Interval Run\\" of 8.11 miles with alternating fast/recovery splits hitting Z4/Z5 heart rates and a max of 184 bpm, which looks like 5x1 mile VO2max repeats rather than the planned 2x2 miles at marathon pace, meaning the athlete substituted a harder session than prescribed.\\n\\nThis conflicts with the coach's stated plan to keep quality work MP-focused and save VO2/800s for later, so the athlete pushed too hard here. I'm also noting several other flags: elevated long-run HR drift (+16.9 bpm), back-to-back weeks of +10% mileage jumps, reduced sleep (6.8 hrs vs 7.5), heavy legs Monday, low Z1/Z2 time at 68.7%, and a relative effort of 340 (1.3x the 3-week average). The athlete is asking whether their 3:30 goal is still realistic and whether post-20-miler leg heaviness is normal—but there's good news too: this was their longest run in two years, the Achilles stayed quiet, and they negative split the effort.\\n\\nNow I'm mapping out the remaining training timeline: race day is Nov 15, today is Oct 12, which gives exactly 4 weeks plus race week (Oct 12-18, Oct 19-25, Oct 26-Nov 1, Nov 2-8, Nov 9-15). With a standard 2-3 week taper, this current week should function as a recovery week given the fatigue signals from the 20-miler and the hard interval session.\\n\\nLooking at the recent training load - 44 miles with a 17.18 long run one week, then 45 miles with a 20.09 long run the next - plus the athlete's reported heavy legs, reduced sleep, and 1.3x relative effort, I'm leaning toward calling this week a down week before one more peak week (Oct 19-25) with a 20-22 mile long run, then starting the taper the following week.\\n\\nI'm sketching out the week: rest Monday, easy 5 Tuesday, easy 7 Wednesday, MP-focused quality Thursday (maybe 2x3mi or 3x2mi at marathon pace), rest Friday, easy 4-5 Saturday, and a cutback long run of 14-15 aerobic miles Sunday without an MP finish, bringing total volume down to roughly 35-37 miles. Alternatively, I could frame this as a second big week with one more push planned after, though the heavy legs suggest recovery is the better call right now.\\n\\nGiven the pattern of 30 → 44 → 45 miles, a step-back week to about 37-38 with controlled quality makes sense. For Thursday I need to correct the drift toward VO2 work -- the athlete ran intervals way faster than marathon pace, so I want to redirect that session strictly toward MP, likely 2-3 x 2mi at 8:00 pace with jog recovery or a continuous MP-tempo block.\\n\\nMapping out the week: Tuesday easy 5mi, Wednesday easy 7mi plus strides, Thursday the MP quality session (2mi WU + 3x2mi @ MP w/ jog + cooldown, ~8mi), Saturday easy 4mi, Sunday a cutback long run of 14mi with HR capped and no MP finish, totaling roughly 38 miles. On the 3:30 goal, I think it's still viable -- the 20-miler with a back-half at 8:45/mi touching Z3 shows real fitness, and one more solid week after recovery followed by taper should get there. The heavy legs are expected given the 20-miler came right after a hard Thursday interval session, so I want to dial back the intensity.\\n\\nI also need to address that the athlete freelanced on the VO2 session -- planned was 2x2mi at MP but they ran 5x1mi fast instead, so I should coach that back toward the prescribed structure. As for safety flags, nothing stands out here: no Achilles pain, no injury or illness signals, just normal post-big-week fatigue, so I'll skip any safety callout and frame this as a training conservatism message instead.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Vv32YLLh8zHUbGihXsNfCw","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"analysis":"## Headline\\nBig week in the books — 45 miles, your longest run in two years, and a long run with a genuine negative split (back half 8:45/mi vs front 9:13/mi). That's a confidence builder. The 3:30 target is still live. But two things from this week tell me we pull the reins a little this week before we go hard again: your Thursday session went off-script into VO2 territory (max HR 184, 24% of the run in Z5), and the Sunday drift was +16.9 bpm — well above the +10 target. Combine that with sleep slipping to 6.8 hrs, legs heavy into Monday, and relative effort 1.3× your three-week average, and the smart play is a modest step-back now so we can hit one more quality block before taper.\\n\\nSo this week: ~37 miles, strictly MP-focused quality (no VO2 reps), long run back to 14 miles with the HR cap and no MP finish. Call it a reset. Then we go bigger again the week of Oct 19 with a long run around 18–20 and a longer MP block.\\n\\n## Your questions\\n\\n**1. Is 3:30 still sensible?**\\nYes, with one caveat. The evidence from the 20-miler is strong — those last four miles rolled at 7:58–8:04/mi off tired legs, with HR climbing but not blown. That's a real signal you can hold goal pace. The caveat: we need to see one more good quality block (an 18–20 mi long run with a solid MP close, and MP intervals that stay *at* MP) before I'll say it with full confidence. We'll know in about two weeks. Keep the goal, earn the goal.\\n\\n**2. Heavy legs Monday after a 20-miler — normal?**\\nTotally normal, especially this one. You stacked a hard interval session Thursday (max HR 184 — that's VO2 territory, not MP) and then went 20 miles with a hot finish three days later. Of course Monday felt like mud. What I'd watch: legs should feel materially better by Wednesday. If they don't, tell me and we'll cut Thursday's quality back.\\n\\n## About Thursday last week\\nThe plan was 2 × 2 mi at goal MP (~8:00/mi). What you ran was effectively 5 × 1 mi hard with jog recovery, with the fast miles down at 6:55–7:02 — that's closer to 10K effort than MP. One red zone session won't hurt you, but we have an explicit plan to save VO2 work for later in the build (if at all). Right now, every quality mile needs to be teaching your legs *marathon pace feel*. That means staying at 7:55–8:05/mi on the fast portions, not racing them. This Thursday is the test — if you're under 7:50 on the first rep, back off.\\n\\n## Why each session this week\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out from the 20, flat canal, Z2 only. Walk if the first mile is grim.\\n- **Wed easy 7 + 6×20s strides**: aerobic volume with a touch of leg speed. Strides are relaxed turnover, not sprints.\\n- **Thu MP intervals (3 × 2 mi)**: this is the correction session. Six total MP miles at 7:55–8:05/mi with 3:00 easy jog between. More MP volume than last planned, but *at MP*, not faster. Hilly Thursday route is fine; hold effort on climbs.\\n- **Sat easy 4**: pre-long flush, slower is better.\\n- **Sun long 14, HR ≤150, no MP finish**: deliberate step-back. We earned a quieter Sunday. Pure aerobic time on feet so you arrive at next week fresh enough to go bigger.\\n\\n## Flags\\n- Z1+Z2 only 68.7% last week — below the 80% base target. The culprit was Thursday's VO2 drift plus a hot long-run finish. Keep easy days genuinely easy and this fixes itself this week.\\n- Long-run drift +16.9 bpm — above target. Partly heat/fatigue, partly the picked-up finish. The HR cap on Sunday is non-negotiable this week.\\n- Sleep 6.8 hrs is low for someone running 45 mi/wk. Protect sleep this week — it's part of the training.\\n- Shin history noted. Nothing bothering you now; if anything whispers after the 20-miler, tell me.","prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W42","days":[{"date":"2026-10-12","dayType":"rest","notes":"Fixed rest/travel. Legs will be heavy today — that's expected after Sunday. 10 min easy mobility (ankles, hips, calves) if you feel like it. Prioritize sleep tonight.","strength":"Optional mobility (10 min)"},{"date":"2026-10-13","dayType":"easy","notes":"Shake-out from Sunday. Properly easy, flat canal. If the first mile feels like concrete, walk a minute and restart — do not force pace. 5-min walk warm-up before running.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"paceOrHr":"9:30–9:50/mi, HR Z2 (138–148)","structure":"5-min walk warm-up, then 5 mi conversational on canal path","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"}},{"date":"2026-10-14","dayType":"easy","notes":"Primary aerobic day. Strides are 20s of relaxed turnover on flat ground with full walk recovery — not sprints. Keep HR honest Z2 on the run itself.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":11265,"paceOrHr":"9:25–9:45/mi, HR Z2","structure":"5-min walk warm-up, then 7 mi easy + 6×20s strides after the run with full walk recovery","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"strength":"Strength session 1 (30–40 min): hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work"},{"date":"2026-10-15","dayType":"quality","notes":"This is the correction after last Thursday. Every MP mile sits 7:55–8:05/mi — if mile 1 of rep 1 is faster than 7:50, pull back immediately. The point is to practice goal pace, not race it. Max HR should stay in mid-Z3 to low-Z4; if you see 170+ you're pushing too hard. Hilly route is fine — hold effort on climbs, let pace drift 5–10 sec, don't chase. If legs are still trashed from Sunday, cut to 2 × 2 mi instead of 3 × 2 mi.","run":{"type":"quality","distanceM":14484,"paceOrHr":"MP reps 7:55–8:05/mi (mid-Z3/low-Z4); WU/CD 9:40–10:00/mi","structure":"5-min walk warm-up, then 9 mi total: 2 mi WU → 3 × 2 mi @ goal MP (8:00/mi) with 3:00 easy jog between → 1 mi CD","shoes":"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4"}},{"date":"2026-10-16","dayType":"rest","notes":"Fixed rest. Hydrate and eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts today."},{"date":"2026-10-17","dayType":"easy","notes":"Pre-long flush. Slower is better. Not the day for strides or pickups.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":6437,"paceOrHr":"9:45–10:05/mi, HR Z2","structure":"5-min walk warm-up, then 4 mi very easy on flat canal path","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"strength":"Short strength 2 (20–25 min): core + calves. Skip if legs feel flat."},{"date":"2026-10-18","dayType":"long","notes":"Deliberate step-back from 20. No MP finish this week — just honest aerobic time on feet with the HR cap. If HR drifts above 150 and won't come back down, walk 30s and resume slower. Fuel every 30–35 min with a gel (3 gels total), fluids with electrolytes. The goal is to arrive at next Sunday fresh enough to go bigger again.","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":22531,"paceOrHr":"HR ≤150; pace likely 9:30–9:50/mi","structure":"5-min walk warm-up, then 14 mi steady by HR on flat canal path, out-and-back","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"}}]},"safetyCallouts":[]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":27257,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5507,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2370}},"diagnostics":null}	200	82496	tool_use	27257	5507	0	0	ok	\N	2370
f4251962-d2dd-41e2-8ec4-325ae91a40ab	2026-10-13 00:10:26.253534+00	mid_week_chat	anthropic	claude-opus-4-7	dev	d63887bf-dede-4062-886f-8fc6cda22144	\N	{"model": "claude-opus-4-7", "tools": [{"name": "submit_mid_week_chat_reply", "description": "Submit the mid-week coach reply (attached-run feedback and optional remaining-day plan patches when present).", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string", "description": "Athlete-facing mid-week coach prose. When attachments are present, include concrete run feedback from metrics/splits."}, "safetyCallouts": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["title", "body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string", "maxLength": 600, "description": "At most 600 characters. One or two short paragraphs; the reply carries the detail."}, "title": {"type": "string", "maxLength": 120}, "severity": {"enum": ["info", "caution", "urgent"], "type": "string"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 5, "description": "Visible safety callouts when red flags appear — escalate to professionals; do not diagnose."}, "allowPastDayPatches": {"type": "boolean", "description": "When true, past-day patches may be applied. Default false — past days stay stable."}, "prescribedDayPatches": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["date", "dayType"], "properties": {"run": {"type": ["object", "null"], "required": ["type", "distanceM"], "properties": {"type": {"enum": ["easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "shoes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "paceOrHr": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "distanceM": {"type": "number"}, "structure": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "Local calendar date YYYY-MM-DD within the plan week"}, "notes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "dayType": {"enum": ["rest", "easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "strength": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "description": "Optional day replacements for remaining plan days (date >= local today). Full PrescribedDay objects."}, "settingsProposalBullets": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Optional soft-gate dossier/settings proposal bullets when the mid-week note is a significant memory update. Never silent-apply."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}], "stream": true, "system": "You are Coach Cade, a running coach answering a mid-week check-in. You are Coach Cade, a running coach. Use only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative. Do not sign off with your name or refer to yourself by name or in the third person unless the athlete asks who you are. Speak to the athlete in plain running language. Never use internal terms such as dossier, proposal, soft-gate, packet, recap, subjective or artifact. Say \\"what I know about you\\", \\"your weekly report\\", \\"your check-in\\" or \\"the plan\\" instead, and never tell the athlete to open a page by name. Week ids such as 2026-W43 are internal: never write them or a short form such as W43 or W43's. Name a week the way the athlete reads it: \\"this week\\", \\"next week\\", \\"the week of Oct 19\\", \\"Oct 19 – 25\\" or \\"4 weeks out from the race\\". Safety callouts: - Never diagnose injury, illness, or medical conditions; do not prescribe treatment. - Coach running from the athlete's volunteered context and Tempo-derived training data. - When red flags appear (pain that worsens, chest pain, dizziness, sudden injury, illness), emit safetyCallouts and urge a qualified professional. - Each callout needs a short title, athlete-facing body (escalate, do not diagnose), and optional severity (info|caution|urgent). - Keep each callout body under 600 characters: one or two short paragraphs. - Keep the training plan/reply conservative when callouts are present. When workout attachments are present, give concrete coaching feedback on those runs using metrics and splits only (no GPS or route geometry). When the athlete asks to change remaining plan days, emit prescribedDayPatches with full day objects for those dates only (do not rewrite past days unless allowPastDayPatches is true). Do not rewrite the full week plan unless asked. For significant memory updates, emit settingsProposalBullets (soft-gate); never silent-apply dossier changes. Think it through first, then call the submit_mid_week_chat_reply tool exactly once with your full answer. Do not write the answer as plain text.", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Call the submit_mid_week_chat_reply tool exactly once with your full answer.\\nNo workout attachments — answer the athlete's mid-week note.\\nCurrent prescribed week is in the packet. To change remaining days, emit prescribedDayPatches using only these dates: 2026-10-12, 2026-10-13, 2026-10-14, 2026-10-15, 2026-10-16, 2026-10-17, 2026-10-18. Past days stay stable unless allowPastDayPatches is true.\\nDo not rewrite the full prescribed week unless the athlete asks.\\nWhen the athlete reports a significant memory update (new constraint, niggle, schedule change), populate settingsProposalBullets for soft-gate Accept — never mutate the dossier directly.\\nWhen red flags appear, populate safetyCallouts (escalate; do not diagnose).\\nModel packet (redacted; no identity PII or GPS):\\n{\\"dossier\\":{\\"versionId\\":2,\\"body\\":\\"# About you\\\\n\\\\n## Stance\\\\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Goal\\\\nLakeshore Marathon on Sun Nov 15, your fourth marathon. Target 3:30. Your current best is 3:41 from two years ago.\\\\n\\\\n## Schedule\\\\nYou run five days a week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday and Sunday. Monday and Friday are fixed rest days because of work travel and cannot move. Weekday runs are early, around 6 am, up to an hour. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run. Total 6 to 7 hours a week, more on long-run weeks. You travel for work roughly one week in six.\\\\n\\\\n## Running history\\\\nThree marathons done, best 3:41. You eased off in June, then built back to about 30 miles a week through July. Recent long run was about 10.8 miles at roughly 9:47/mi; easy runs sit near 9:20 to 9:40/mi.\\\\n\\\\n## Injuries and constraints\\\\nNothing bothering you now. You had shin splints in your first marathon block, so you prefer a careful ramp. Monday and Friday rest days are non-negotiable.\\\\n\\\\n## Preferences\\\\nFlat paved loops and a canal path for most runs, with a hillier route on Thursdays. Long run on Sunday. You want to know why each session is in the plan. Happy to work hard on quality days, but easy days must stay properly easy. Imperial units.\\\\n\\\\n## Shoes\\\\nBrooks Ghost 16 for daily miles. Saucony Endorphin Speed 4 for workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## Heart rate zones\\\\nCustom zones. Z1 112-131, Z2 131-150, Z3 150-164, Z4 164-177, Z5 177-188.\\\\n\\\\n## Current status\\\\nHealthy, about 30 miles per week, 5 runs per week, roughly 14 weeks out from race day.\\\\n\\\\n## Coach update (2026-W34)\\\\n\\\\n- Long-run guidance in heat: run by HR cap (≤150) rather than pace\\\\n- Next quality block will keep MP focus; revisit VO2/800s later in the build\\\\n\\"},\\"recapMarkdown\\":null,\\"thread\\":[{\\"role\\":\\"athlete\\",\\"body\\":\\"Legs are heavy today after the 20 miler. Tuesday is an easy 6 as planned. Is it fine to keep it properly slow?\\",\\"createdAt\\":\\"2026-10-26T23:29:51.230Z\\"}],\\"attachments\\":[],\\"week\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W42\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-10-19T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"d63887bf-dede-4062-886f-8fc6cda22144\\"},\\"recentHistory\\":[{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W41\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"6de0ee3e-ff03-4b5c-a998-09eedbead69f\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W41 (Mon Oct 5 – Sun Oct 11, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 44.97 mi | 43.98 mi | 34.92 mi | +10.1 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 6h 40m | 6h 36m | 5h 20m | +1h 20m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 955 ft | 787 ft | 678 ft | +277 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 340 | 317 | 254 | +86 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (6m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░  67.3%   (4h 30m)\\\\nZ3 ██████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  16.7%   (1h 7m)\\\\nZ4 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  10.7%   (43m)\\\\nZ5 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  3.9%   (16m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **68.7%**. **Below** typical marathon base target (≥80% Z1+Z2).\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Oct 6 — Easy Run — 4.88 mi / 45m 7s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:15/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:10/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.6 → 143.9 (+5.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.3% · Z2 96.7% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑89 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 32\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Oct 7 — Easy Run — 7.94 mi / 1h 12m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:07/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:04/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:02/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:02/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 146 → 149.8 (+3.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 95.2% · Z3 4.8% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑220 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 51\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Oct 8 — Interval Run — 8.11 mi / 1h 5m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:01/mi  ·  Avg HR 163 (86.7% max)  ·  Max HR 184  ·  Cad 354 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:23/mi / 7:02/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:57/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:55/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:57/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:58/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 150.9 → 155.6 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.1% · Z2 25.5% · Z3 13.1% · Z4 34.6% · Z5 23.8%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑164 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 104\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 9/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Oct 10 — Easy Run — 3.96 mi / 36m 45s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:15/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.8 → 143.9 (+6.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 4.1% · Z2 95.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑72 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 26\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Oct 11 — Long Run — 20.09 mi / 3h 1m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:02/mi  ·  Avg HR 151 (80.3% max)  ·  Max HR 169  ·  Cad 347 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:17/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 7:58/mi / 8:03/mi / 7:60/mi / 8:04/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.5 → 161.4 (+16.9 bpm) ⚠ above target (target ≤10 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 58.2% · Z3 30.3% · Z4 11.3% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑410 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 127\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Oct 11 — 20.09 mi / 3h 1m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:02/mi  ·  Avg HR 151  ·  Drift: 144.5 → 161.4 (+16.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:17/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 7:58/mi / 8:03/mi / 7:60/mi / 8:04/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 8:45/mi vs front 9:13/mi (faster than front half by 28s/mi) ✓ negative split\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? Yes (paced up or HR above easy cap)\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:24/mi → 9:20/mi → 9:14/mi → 9:12/mi ▁▃██ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 143 → 144 → 144 → 144 █▁▁▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 7.93 mi → 11.94 mi → 17.18 mi → 20.09 mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n## Notable\\\\n\\\\n- Relative effort (340) ≥ 1.3× 3-wk avg (254) — possible overload\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 6.8 hrs (range 6–7.5)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Skipped Friday.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Legs heavy, especially after the 20 miler. The Achilles was fine the whole way.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Tired but pleased. The 20 miler was the longest training run I've done in two years.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is my 3:30 target still sensible after this block?\\\\n2. Is heavy legs on Monday normal after a 20 miler?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nThat was a big, honest week — 44 mi with a 17.2 mi long run that finished with 3 miles at marathon pace, and you came through it saying \\\\\\"I could have held it.\\\\\\" That's exactly the feedback I wanted. The aerobic engine is doing its job: easy HR still parked at 144, easy pace trending from 9:23 to 9:14 across the month, and MP felt like a controlled gear rather than a strain.\\\\n\\\\nThat said, two things on the dashboard tell me we don't double down this week — we consolidate:\\\\n\\\\n1. **Long-run drift was +15.9 bpm** (target ≤10). The front half was fine, but your HR climbed from 144 to 160 across the back end, pushed by the MP close on tired legs. That's acceptable *because* of the MP finish, but it's a cost.\\\\n2. **Relative effort 317 vs 223 three-week average** — a one-week overload flag. Fine on its own; a problem if we stack another big jump on top.\\\\n\\\\nAdd in that you went from 35 mi to 44 mi in one jump, and the shin history in the back of my mind, and the right move is a slight pullback this week: hold volume roughly flat (~42 mi), keep the Thursday MP work (step it up a notch), and bring the long run down to 15 mi with no MP finish — pure aerobic, HR-capped. Then next week we push again.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — how the final weeks look\\\\n\\\\nYou're 6 weeks out from Lakeshore after this one. Here's the shape:\\\\n\\\\n- **This week (Oct 5–11, 6 weeks out)** — consolidate. ~42 mi, long 15 easy, Thursday 3×2 mi @ MP.\\\\n- **Oct 12–18 (5 weeks out)** — peak long run. ~46 mi, long 19–20 mi with a 4–5 mi MP block in the back half. This is the key workout of the block.\\\\n- **Oct 19–25 (4 weeks out)** — biggest MP volume week. ~45 mi, long 17–18 mi with 6–8 mi at MP, plus a strong Thursday quality.\\\\n- **Oct 26–Nov 1 (3 weeks out)** — taper begins. ~36 mi, long 14 mi easy with a short MP touch, Thursday sharpens (shorter, race-pace focused).\\\\n- **Nov 2–8 (2 weeks out)** — deeper taper. ~28 mi, long 10–11 mi, one short MP session midweek.\\\\n- **Nov 9–15 (race week)** — ~18–20 mi total including the race. Short shake-outs, a few MP strides on Thursday, race Sunday.\\\\n\\\\nThe engine's built. From here it's three more progression weeks, then three weeks of carefully protecting what you've got.\\\\n\\\\n## Why each session this week\\\\n- **Tue easy 6**: shake out from Sunday. Nothing to prove — if HR won't drop under 150, slow down.\\\\n- **Wed easy 8 + strides**: midweek aerobic volume + 6×20s to keep leg speed sharp without cost. Flat canal path.\\\\n- **Thu quality — 3×2 mi @ MP**: step up from last week's single 2-mile block to three. 6 total miles at 8:00/mi is where we start living. Hilly route is fine; hold effort on climbs.\\\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long flush.\\\\n- **Sun long 15, HR ≤150, no MP finish**: deliberate step back after last Sunday's 17 w/ MP. Pure aerobic, fuel practice, protect the legs for the 19–20 mi peak long run the following week.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags\\\\n- Last week's HR drift and overload flag are why this week consolidates. Not a problem — a signal to pace the build.\\\\n- Keep Tue/Wed/Sat genuinely easy. 9:14 is drifting toward the fast end of easy; aim 9:30–9:50. The engine builds while you resist running fast on easy days.\\\\n- Shin history is quiet. Report any whisper early, not after.\\\\n- Fueling on Sunday: still practice — 2–3 gels across a 15-miler plus electrolytes. The gut needs the reps too.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-05\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest/travel. Optional 10 min mobility — ankles, calves, hips. Hydrate well after Sunday's long effort.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30–9:50/mi, Z2 (HR 138–148)\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi conversational on flat canal path\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-06\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake-out after Sunday's 17 w/ MP finish. Genuinely easy — if HR won't settle under 150, slow down. No pushing.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30–9:50/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi easy on flat canal + 6×20s relaxed strides after the run with full walk recovery\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-07\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Primary aerobic day. Strides are relaxed turnover, not sprints — keeps leg speed alive for Thursday.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 1 (30–40 min): hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP reps 7:55–8:05/mi; WU/CD 9:40–10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":14484,\\"structure\\":\\"9 mi total on hilly route: 1.5 mi WU → 3 × 2 mi @ goal MP (8:00/mi) with 3:00 easy jog between → 1.5 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-08\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Step up from one 2-mi block to three. Rep 1 should feel controlled — if mile 1 is under 7:50 you went too hot, dial back. On climbs: hold effort, let pace drift 5–10s. Bail at 2 reps if form breaks down or legs are flat.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-09\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest/travel. Hydrate and eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts today.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:05/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi very easy on flat canal\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-10\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Pre-long flush. Slower is better. If legs feel heavy from Thursday, cut to 4 mi and move on.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Short strength 2 (20–25 min): core + calves. Skip if legs are flat.\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"HR ≤150, pace likely 9:30–9:50/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":24140,\\"structure\\":\\"15 mi steady by HR on flat/canal route. No MP finish this week.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-11\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Deliberate step back from last Sunday's 17 w/ MP — we're protecting legs for the 19–20 mi peak long run next week. If HR drifts above 150, walk 30s and resume slower. Fuel: gel every 30–35 min (3 gels), small water chase, carry electrolytes. Report back how HR drift looks and how fueling sat.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W41\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W40\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"42d956f4-8b0a-4145-98ff-a058741c4904\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W40 (Mon Sep 28 – Sun Oct 4, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 43.98 mi | 34.83 mi | 30.66 mi | +13.3 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 6h 36m | 5h 20m | 4h 45m | +1h 51m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 787 ft | 722 ft | 664 ft | +124 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 317 | 274 | 223 | +94 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.1%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ██████████████████████████░░░░░░░░░  74.8%   (4h 57m)\\\\nZ3 ███████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  18.9%   (1h 15m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  5.1%   (20m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **75.95%**. **Below** typical marathon base target (≥80% Z1+Z2).\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 29 — Easy Run — 5.85 mi / 54m 5s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:15/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:14/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:07/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.1 → 144 (+4.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1.8% · Z2 98.2% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑108 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 38\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 30 — Easy Run — 7.97 mi / 1h 12m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:07/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:06/mi / 9:06/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:02/mi / 9:06/mi / 9:02/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145 → 149.7 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 94.5% · Z3 5.5% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑148 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 51\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Oct 1 — Marathon Pace Run — 7.89 mi / 1h 7m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:32/mi  ·  Avg HR 151 (80.3% max)  ·  Max HR 163  ·  Cad 355 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:15/mi / 9:22/mi / 7:55/mi / 7:60/mi / 7:53/mi / 7:56/mi / 8:01/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:26/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138 → 145.1 (+7.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.2% · Z2 39.8% · Z3 58% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑161 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 87\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Oct 3 — Easy Run — 5.09 mi / 47m 35s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:23/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.4 → 144.5 (+6.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.2% · Z2 96.8% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑92 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Oct 4 — Long Run — 17.18 mi / 2h 34m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:01/mi  ·  Avg HR 150 (80.3% max)  ·  Max HR 170  ·  Cad 347 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:01/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:06/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:06/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:15/mi / 7:60/mi / 8:03/mi / 8:04/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.3 → 160.1 (+15.9 bpm) ⚠ above target (target ≤10 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 65.9% · Z3 20.7% · Z4 13.2% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑279 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 108\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Oct 4 — 17.18 mi / 2h 34m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:01/mi  ·  Avg HR 150  ·  Drift: 144.3 → 160.1 (+15.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:01/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:06/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:06/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:15/mi / 7:60/mi / 8:03/mi / 8:04/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 8:48/mi vs front 9:10/mi (faster than front half by 23s/mi) ✓ negative split\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? Yes (paced up or HR above easy cap)\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi → 9:20/mi → 9:14/mi ▁▁▃█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 143 → 144 → 144 ▁█▁▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi → 11.94 mi → 17.18 mi ▃▁▃█\\\\n\\\\n## Notable\\\\n\\\\n- Relative effort (317) ≥ 1.3× 3-wk avg (223) — possible overload\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.5 hrs (range 7–8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Legs tired after the long run but nothing sore. Achilles quiet.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Good. The last three miles at marathon pace were hard but I could have held it.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. How should the final weeks before the race look?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nClean, confident week. 34.8 mi, tempo went well with Achilles quiet (your own note: \\\\\\"kept checking… it was fine\\\\\\"), long run out to 11.9 with a mild negative split and HR drift back inside acceptable range (+8.8 over nearly 2 hrs). Z1+Z2 at 81.5% — right where I want it. You're healthy, hitting marathon-base targets, and 7 weeks from Lakeshore. Time to build again, carefully.\\\\n\\\\nThis week: ~38 mi, step the long run to 13.5, and reintroduce real marathon-pace work on Thursday — 2 × 2 mi at goal MP (~8:00/mi). We're not going back to the aggressive block we had before the Achilles flare; we're layering MP volume gradually so the tendon stays happy.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — Achilles maintenance through race day\\\\nKeep doing what's clearly working, don't invent new stuff:\\\\n- **Slow heel drops** daily — the physio's protocol is doing its job; keep it going right through race week. On the Monday of race week drop to once a day, and skip them the day before the race.\\\\n- **5-minute walk warm-up before every run.** Boring, free, protective. Keep it in.\\\\n- **First-steps-in-the-morning check** — that's your canary. If morning stiffness ever returns and doesn't ease within a few minutes, tell me in the check-in before your next run.\\\\n- **Shoe rotation** — Ghost 16 for easy, Endorphin Speed 4 only on quality days. Don't let an easy run accidentally happen in the Speed 4.\\\\n- **One rebuild rule I'm applying**: we add either distance OR intensity in a given week, not big jumps of both. This week it's a modest distance bump plus returning MP; next week we'll either hold intensity and push the long run, or hold distance and sharpen quality.\\\\n\\\\nIf anything whispers at you — sharper than a 2/10, lingers after runs, or alters your gait — back to the physio before pushing on. Keep her in the loop as we get closer to race day too.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags\\\\n- Thursday tempo HR max hit 174 (upper Z4). Intended effort was tempo, not threshold — this week's MP reps should sit mid-Z3 to low Z4, not spike. If you see 170+ on an MP mile, you're pushing too hard.\\\\n- Long-run drift still slightly on the high side (+8.8). Not alarming given back-half pickup, but keep the HR cap of ≤150 on long runs this week — pace will be whatever it is.\\\\n- Mileage jump +8.9 mi over prior week was a bit sharp — this week we only add ~3 mi on top so the ramp isn't stacking.\\\\n- Sleep 7.4, strength 2 of 2, stress low — all green. Protect that.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-28\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest/travel. 10 min mobility if you feel like it — calves and ankles. Slow heel drops as prescribed.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Optional mobility (10 min)\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30–9:50/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 5 mi conversational on the canal path\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-29\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake-out from Sunday. Conversational, flat canal path. 5-min walk warm-up before you start running.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\