e: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **68.7%**. **Below** typical marathon base target (≥80% Z1+Z2).\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Oct 6 — Easy Run — 4.88 mi / 45m 7s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:15/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:10/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.6 → 143.9 (+5.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.3% · Z2 96.7% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑89 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 32\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Oct 7 — Easy Run — 7.94 mi / 1h 12m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:07/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:04/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:02/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:02/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 146 → 149.8 (+3.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 95.2% · Z3 4.8% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑220 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 51\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Oct 8 — Interval Run — 8.11 mi / 1h 5m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:01/mi  ·  Avg HR 163 (86.7% max)  ·  Max HR 184  ·  Cad 354 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:23/mi / 7:02/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:57/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:55/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:57/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:58/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 150.9 → 155.6 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.1% · Z2 25.5% · Z3 13.1% · Z4 34.6% · Z5 23.8%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑164 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 104\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 9/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Oct 10 — Easy Run — 3.96 mi / 36m 45s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:15/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.8 → 143.9 (+6.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 4.1% · Z2 95.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑72 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 26\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Oct 11 — Long Run — 20.09 mi / 3h 1m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:02/mi  ·  Avg HR 151 (80.3% max)  ·  Max HR 169  ·  Cad 347 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:17/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 7:58/mi / 8:03/mi / 7:60/mi / 8:04/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.5 → 161.4 (+16.9 bpm) ⚠ above target (target ≤10 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 58.2% · Z3 30.3% · Z4 11.3% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑410 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 127\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Oct 11 — 20.09 mi / 3h 1m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:02/mi  ·  Avg HR 151  ·  Drift: 144.5 → 161.4 (+16.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:17/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 7:58/mi / 8:03/mi / 7:60/mi / 8:04/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 8:45/mi vs front 9:13/mi (faster than front half by 28s/mi) ✓ negative split\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? Yes (paced up or HR above easy cap)\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:24/mi → 9:20/mi → 9:14/mi → 9:12/mi ▁▃██ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 143 → 144 → 144 → 144 █▁▁▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 7.93 mi → 11.94 mi → 17.18 mi → 20.09 mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n## Notable\\\\n\\\\n- Relative effort (340) ≥ 1.3× 3-wk avg (254) — possible overload\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 6.8 hrs (range 6–7.5)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Skipped Friday.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Legs heavy, especially after the 20 miler. The Achilles was fine the whole way.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Tired but pleased. The 20 miler was the longest training run I've done in two years.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is my 3:30 target still sensible after this block?\\\\n2. Is heavy legs on Monday normal after a 20 miler?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nThat was a big, honest week — 44 mi with a 17.2 mi long run that finished with 3 miles at marathon pace, and you came through it saying \\\\\\"I could have held it.\\\\\\" That's exactly the feedback I wanted. The aerobic engine is doing its job: easy HR still parked at 144, easy pace trending from 9:23 to 9:14 across the month, and MP felt like a controlled gear rather than a strain.\\\\n\\\\nThat said, two things on the dashboard tell me we don't double down this week — we consolidate:\\\\n\\\\n1. **Long-run drift was +15.9 bpm** (target ≤10). The front half was fine, but your HR climbed from 144 to 160 across the back end, pushed by the MP close on tired legs. That's acceptable *because* of the MP finish, but it's a cost.\\\\n2. **Relative effort 317 vs 223 three-week average** — a one-week overload flag. Fine on its own; a problem if we stack another big jump on top.\\\\n\\\\nAdd in that you went from 35 mi to 44 mi in one jump, and the shin history in the back of my mind, and the right move is a slight pullback this week: hold volume roughly flat (~42 mi), keep the Thursday MP work (step it up a notch), and bring the long run down to 15 mi with no MP finish — pure aerobic, HR-capped. Then next week we push again.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — how the final weeks look\\\\n\\\\nYou're 6 weeks out from Lakeshore after this one. Here's the shape:\\\\n\\\\n- **This week (Oct 5–11, 6 weeks out)** — consolidate. ~42 mi, long 15 easy, Thursday 3×2 mi @ MP.\\\\n- **Oct 12–18 (5 weeks out)** — peak long run. ~46 mi, long 19–20 mi with a 4–5 mi MP block in the back half. This is the key workout of the block.\\\\n- **Oct 19–25 (4 weeks out)** — biggest MP volume week. ~45 mi, long 17–18 mi with 6–8 mi at MP, plus a strong Thursday quality.\\\\n- **Oct 26–Nov 1 (3 weeks out)** — taper begins. ~36 mi, long 14 mi easy with a short MP touch, Thursday sharpens (shorter, race-pace focused).\\\\n- **Nov 2–8 (2 weeks out)** — deeper taper. ~28 mi, long 10–11 mi, one short MP session midweek.\\\\n- **Nov 9–15 (race week)** — ~18–20 mi total including the race. Short shake-outs, a few MP strides on Thursday, race Sunday.\\\\n\\\\nThe engine's built. From here it's three more progression weeks, then three weeks of carefully protecting what you've got.\\\\n\\\\n## Why each session this week\\\\n- **Tue easy 6**: shake out from Sunday. Nothing to prove — if HR won't drop under 150, slow down.\\\\n- **Wed easy 8 + strides**: midweek aerobic volume + 6×20s to keep leg speed sharp without cost. Flat canal path.\\\\n- **Thu quality — 3×2 mi @ MP**: step up from last week's single 2-mile block to three. 6 total miles at 8:00/mi is where we start living. Hilly route is fine; hold effort on climbs.\\\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long flush.\\\\n- **Sun long 15, HR ≤150, no MP finish**: deliberate step back after last Sunday's 17 w/ MP. Pure aerobic, fuel practice, protect the legs for the 19–20 mi peak long run the following week.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags\\\\n- Last week's HR drift and overload flag are why this week consolidates. Not a problem — a signal to pace the build.\\\\n- Keep Tue/Wed/Sat genuinely easy. 9:14 is drifting toward the fast end of easy; aim 9:30–9:50. The engine builds while you resist running fast on easy days.\\\\n- Shin history is quiet. Report any whisper early, not after.\\\\n- Fueling on Sunday: still practice — 2–3 gels across a 15-miler plus electrolytes. The gut needs the reps too.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-05\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest/travel. Optional 10 min mobility — ankles, calves, hips. Hydrate well after Sunday's long effort.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30–9:50/mi, Z2 (HR 138–148)\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi conversational on flat canal path\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-06\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake-out after Sunday's 17 w/ MP finish. Genuinely easy — if HR won't settle under 150, slow down. No pushing.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30–9:50/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi easy on flat canal + 6×20s relaxed strides after the run with full walk recovery\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-07\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Primary aerobic day. Strides are relaxed turnover, not sprints — keeps leg speed alive for Thursday.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 1 (30–40 min): hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP reps 7:55–8:05/mi; WU/CD 9:40–10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":14484,\\"structure\\":\\"9 mi total on hilly route: 1.5 mi WU → 3 × 2 mi @ goal MP (8:00/mi) with 3:00 easy jog between → 1.5 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-08\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Step up from one 2-mi block to three. Rep 1 should feel controlled — if mile 1 is under 7:50 you went too hot, dial back. On climbs: hold effort, let pace drift 5–10s. Bail at 2 reps if form breaks down or legs are flat.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-09\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest/travel. Hydrate and eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts today.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:05/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi very easy on flat canal\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-10\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Pre-long flush. Slower is better. If legs feel heavy from Thursday, cut to 4 mi and move on.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Short strength 2 (20–25 min): core + calves. Skip if legs are flat.\\"},{\\