 drift: 144.3 → 160.1 (+15.9 bpm) ⚠ above target (target ≤10 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 65.9% · Z3 20.7% · Z4 13.2% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑279 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 108\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Oct 4 — 17.18 mi / 2h 34m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:01/mi  ·  Avg HR 150  ·  Drift: 144.3 → 160.1 (+15.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:01/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:06/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:06/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:15/mi / 7:60/mi / 8:03/mi / 8:04/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 8:48/mi vs front 9:10/mi (faster than front half by 23s/mi) ✓ negative split\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? Yes (paced up or HR above easy cap)\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi → 9:20/mi → 9:14/mi ▁▁▃█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 143 → 144 → 144 ▁█▁▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi → 11.94 mi → 17.18 mi ▃▁▃█\\\\n\\\\n## Notable\\\\n\\\\n- Relative effort (317) ≥ 1.3× 3-wk avg (223) — possible overload\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.5 hrs (range 7–8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Legs tired after the long run but nothing sore. Achilles quiet.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Good. The last three miles at marathon pace were hard but I could have held it.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. How should the final weeks before the race look?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nClean, confident week. 34.8 mi, tempo went well with Achilles quiet (your own note: \\\\\\"kept checking… it was fine\\\\\\"), long run out to 11.9 with a mild negative split and HR drift back inside acceptable range (+8.8 over nearly 2 hrs). Z1+Z2 at 81.5% — right where I want it. You're healthy, hitting marathon-base targets, and 7 weeks from Lakeshore. Time to build again, carefully.\\\\n\\\\nThis week: ~38 mi, step the long run to 13.5, and reintroduce real marathon-pace work on Thursday — 2 × 2 mi at goal MP (~8:00/mi). We're not going back to the aggressive block we had before the Achilles flare; we're layering MP volume gradually so the tendon stays happy.\\\\n\\\\n## Your question — Achilles maintenance through race day\\\\nKeep doing what's clearly working, don't invent new stuff:\\\\n- **Slow heel drops** daily — the physio's protocol is doing its job; keep it going right through race week. On the Monday of race week drop to once a day, and skip them the day before the race.\\\\n- **5-minute walk warm-up before every run.** Boring, free, protective. Keep it in.\\\\n- **First-steps-in-the-morning check** — that's your canary. If morning stiffness ever returns and doesn't ease within a few minutes, tell me in the check-in before your next run.\\\\n- **Shoe rotation** — Ghost 16 for easy, Endorphin Speed 4 only on quality days. Don't let an easy run accidentally happen in the Speed 4.\\\\n- **One rebuild rule I'm applying**: we add either distance OR intensity in a given week, not big jumps of both. This week it's a modest distance bump plus returning MP; next week we'll either hold intensity and push the long run, or hold distance and sharpen quality.\\\\n\\\\nIf anything whispers at you — sharper than a 2/10, lingers after runs, or alters your gait — back to the physio before pushing on. Keep her in the loop as we get closer to race day too.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags\\\\n- Thursday tempo HR max hit 174 (upper Z4). Intended effort was tempo, not threshold — this week's MP reps should sit mid-Z3 to low Z4, not spike. If you see 170+ on an MP mile, you're pushing too hard.\\\\n- Long-run drift still slightly on the high side (+8.8). Not alarming given back-half pickup, but keep the HR cap of ≤150 on long runs this week — pace will be whatever it is.\\\\n- Mileage jump +8.9 mi over prior week was a bit sharp — this week we only add ~3 mi on top so the ramp isn't stacking.\\\\n- Sleep 7.4, strength 2 of 2, stress low — all green. Protect that.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-28\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest/travel. 10 min mobility if you feel like it — calves and ankles. Slow heel drops as prescribed.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Optional mobility (10 min)\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30–9:50/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 5 mi conversational on the canal path\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-29\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake-out from Sunday. Conversational, flat canal path. 5-min walk warm-up before you start running.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:25–9:45/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 7 mi easy + 6×20s strides after the run\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-30\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Primary aerobic day. Strides are relaxed turnover, not sprints — on flat ground with full walk recovery between.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 1 (30–40 min): hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP reps 7:55–8:05/mi (mid-Z3/low-Z4); WU/CD 9:40–10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 8 mi total: 2 mi WU → 2 × 2 mi @ goal MP (8:00/mi) with 3:00 easy jog between → 1.5 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-01\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Returning to MP intervals. First rep should feel controlled, not racing — if mile 1 is under 7:50 you went too hot. Hilly Thursday route is fine; hold effort on climbs and let pace drift 5–10 sec. If anything grumbles in the Achilles during warm-up, convert to an easy 6 and we'll try again next week.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-02\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Hydrate and eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts here.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:05/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 4 mi very easy on flat canal path\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-03\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Pre-long flush. Slower is better.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 2 (20–25 min): core + calves\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"HR ≤150; pace likely 9:30–9:50/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":21726,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 13.5 mi steady on the canal path, HR-capped. Out-and-back.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-04\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Long run back to 13.5. No MP finish this week — just honest aerobic time on feet with HR cap. Fuel every 30–35 min with a gel (3 gels total), fluids with electrolytes. Start pre-sunrise if warm. If HR drifts above 150 and won't come back, walk 30s and resume slower.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W40\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W39\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"c6dde52e-1142-4497-87f4-54e4f9dc43af\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W39 (Mon Sep 21 – Sun Sep 27, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 34.83 mi | 25.95 mi | 33.86 mi | +1.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 20m | 4h 4m | 5h 15m | +5m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 722 ft | 525 ft | 741 ft | -20 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 274 | 171 | 241 | +33 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 143 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.2%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80.3%   (4h 17m)\\\\nZ3 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  12.1%   (39m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  6.4%   (21m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.51%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 22 — Easy Run — 5.16 mi / 48m 4s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:17/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.5 → 144.1 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 23 — Easy Run — 6.86 mi / 1h 3m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:07/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.1 → 150.3 (+5.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 86.4% · Z3 13.6% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑240 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 45\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 24 — Tempo Run — 7.01 mi / 1h 1m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:43/mi  ·  Avg HR 150 (79.8% max)  ·  Max HR 174  ·  Cad 350 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi / 7:35/mi / 7:35/mi / 7:39/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 136.1 → 138.7 (+2.6 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.5% · Z2 57.5% · Z3 6.5% · Z4 33.5% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑121 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 92\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Achilles no issue.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 26 — Easy Run — 3.85 mi / 36m 18s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 141 (75% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:23/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:18/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.4 → 143.2 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.8% · Z2 97.2% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑30 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 25\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 27 — Long Run — 11.94 mi / 1h 51m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 142.7 → 151.6 (+8.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.5% · Z2 76.1% · Z3 23.5% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑230 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 78\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 27 — 11.94 mi / 1h 51m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 142.7 → 151.6 (+8.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:12/mi vs front 9:15/mi (vs front half; Δ +3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi → 9:20/mi ▁▅▅█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 143 → 144 ▁▁█▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi → 11.94 mi █▃▁▃\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.4 hrs (range 6.8–8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Nothing. I kept checking for the Achilles on the tempo and it was fine.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Relieved and ready to build again.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is there anything I should keep doing for the Achilles through race day?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nGood news dominates: the Achilles backed down, Sunday's long run was pain-free with no afterward stiffness, and your physio has cleared you to keep running — including one short tempo this week if morning stiffness stays gone. Easy pace and HR behavior are unchanged (143 avg, 91% Z1+Z2), which tells me the aerobic engine held together through the quiet week. We're going to rebuild carefully: ~32 mi, a short controlled tempo on Thursday, and a long run back out to 11 miles.\\\\n\\\\n## Your questions\\\\n**1. Can we put a short tempo in?** Yes — exactly as your physio framed it. Thursday is a short, honest tempo (2 miles continuous at ~8:00/mi, your goal MP), not a hammer session. The pre-conditions are the ones she set: no morning stiffness in the Achilles the day of the run, and no sharpening pain during. If either shows up, we convert to easy and move on. No heroics.\\\\n\\\\n**2. Does the missed week change what's realistic on Nov 15?** Honestly: 3:30 is still on the table but it's tighter now. You lost one quality week and shortened a long run, not a block. What matters most now is stacking 3–4 clean weeks of progression (long runs back to 15, 17, then 18–19) with MP work mixed in. I'd rather commit to a goal after your next long run at 13–14 mi tells us how the Achilles handles the extra time on feet. Right now the plan is still built around 3:30 — we'll calibrate honestly in 2–3 weeks.\\\\n\\\\n## Why each session\\\\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out, flat canal, Z2. Nothing to prove.\\\\n- **Wed easy 6**: aerobic volume. No strides this week — leg speed can wait one more week while the Achilles settles further.\\\\n- **Thu short tempo**: 1.5 mi WU → 2 mi @ ~8:00/mi → 1.5 mi CD. Flat route, not the hillier one, to keep load off the tendon. Workout shoes OK; if the Achilles feels anything other than normal first-mile stiffness, downshift to easy.\\\\n- **Sat easy 5**: pre-long flush, slower end of easy.\\\\n- **Sun long 11**: +3 mi from last Sunday, HR-capped at 150. No MP finish this week — we're earning volume back before adding intensity to the long run.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags\\\\n- Keep up the slow heel drops twice a day as prescribed — that's the single most important thing you're doing right now.\\\\n- Morning stiffness is your canary. If it reappears for more than the first few steps, email me before Thursday's workout and we'll pull it.\\\\n- Mileage ~32 mi — a ~6 mi bump from last week. Fine on paper, but your tendon is the governor, not the number.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-21\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest/travel. Slow heel drops morning and evening as prescribed. 10 min mobility optional.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Heel drops (physio protocol) + optional mobility\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:35–9:55/mi, Z2 (HR 138–148)\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi conversational on flat canal path\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-22\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake-out. Properly easy — if the Achilles is stiff for the first mile that's expected, but it should ease. If it sharpens, cut short.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:25–9:45/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi easy, flat\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-23\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Primary aerobic day. No strides this week — one more week of boring miles while the tendon settles.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Heel drops AM/PM + strength 1 (30–40 min): hips, glutes, calves, single-leg\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Tempo 7:55–8:05/mi; WU/CD 9:40–10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi on flat route (not the hilly one): 1.5 mi WU → 2 mi continuous @ goal MP (8:00/mi) → 1.5 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-24\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Pre-conditions: no morning Achilles stiffness, no sharpening pain in warm-up. If either, convert the tempo portion to easy and run 5 mi Z2. During the 2-mile tempo, if anything sharpens in the tendon, stop and jog home.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-25\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Heel drops. Fueling for Sunday starts today — eat and hydrate normally.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:05/mi, Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi very easy on flat canal\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-26\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Pre-long flush. Slower is better.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Heel drops + short strength 2 (20–25 min): core + calves\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"HR ≤150, pace likely 9:30–9:50/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":17703,\\"structure\\":\\"11 mi steady by HR on flat/canal route\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-27\\",\\"notes\\":\\"HR-capped long run — no MP finish this week. If HR drifts above 150, walk 30s and resume slower. Gel every 30–35 min (2 gels) with small water chase to keep practicing fueling. Report back how the Achilles handles the extra time on feet.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W39\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W38\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"0876b9b6-d823-4b3e-97fb-b670672066db\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W38 (Mon Sep 14 – Sun Sep 20, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 25.95 mi | 31.22 mi | 36.45 mi | -10.5 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 4h 4m | 4h 51m | 5h 39m | -1h 35m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 525 ft | 745 ft | 762 ft | -237 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 171 | 225 | 275 | -104 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 143 | 144 | 144 | -1 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 ███████████████████████████████░░░░  89.7%   (3h 39m)\\\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  8.8%   (22m)\\\\nZ4 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **91.18%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 15 — Easy Run — 4.13 mi / 38m 32s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 144.2 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑82 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 6/10  ·  Pain: Slight tightness for the first half mile, about a 2 out of 10.\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 16 — Easy Run — 4.83 mi / 45m 6s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:12/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.8 → 150.6 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 84.3% · Z3 15.7% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 32\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10  ·  Pain: A hint of it at the start only.\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 17 — Easy Run — 4.99 mi / 46m 53s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:23/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138 → 143.7 (+5.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑135 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Achilles fine on the flat. Easy only this week.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 19 — Easy Run — 4.07 mi / 38m 48s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:31/mi  ·  Avg HR 141 (75% max)  ·  Max HR 146  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.9 → 143.2 (+5.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑112 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 20 — Long Run — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147 (78.2% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.7% · Z2 80.1% · Z3 19.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 52\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 20 — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147  ·  Drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:18/mi vs front 9:15/mi (vs front half; Δ -3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi ▁▃██\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 143 ▁▁▁█\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi ▃█▃▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.5 hrs (range 6.9–8.2)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2 (Calf raises and slow heel drops.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low. Easier at work.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: The Achilles is a lot better. Nothing at all on Saturday or Sunday, and not stiff afterwards. Saw a sports physio on Wednesday: mild Achilles tendinopathy, nothing torn. She cleared me to keep running, gave me slow heel drops twice a day, and said one short tempo next week is fine if the morning stiffness stays gone.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Better. Frustrated about the missing miles but I can live with it.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. The physio is happy for me to try a short tempo next week. Can we put one in?\\\\n2. Does the missed week change what is realistic for race day?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Headline\\\\nWe're pulling back this week. The Achilles signal on Thursday — tight from mile 2, sharper when you picked up the pace, enough to stop and walk home — is exactly the kind of thing we treat conservatively right now, not push through. You still got a solid 10-miler in on Sunday with no pain while running, which is a good sign, but stiffness afterward tells me the tissue is irritated. We lose nothing by taking 7–10 easy days here. We lose the whole block if we poke it.\\\\n\\\\nPlan this week: no tempo, no MP work, no hills, all flat, all Ghost 16. Shorter easy runs, a modest long run capped by feel, and a hard stop rule if symptoms escalate. We're 9 weeks from Lakeshore — plenty of runway to rebuild quality if the Achilles settles.\\\\n\\\\n## Your questions\\\\n\\\\n**\\\\\\"Should I stop running for a few days, or keep going with easy runs?\\\\\\"**\\\\nIf pain is ≤3/10, not sharp, and eases within the first mile (like Saturday), easy running on flats is usually fine and can actually help. If it's sharp, worsens as you run, changes your gait, or lingers/worsens after — stop that day and take 2–3 full days off. The tempo-day pattern (fine easy, bad with pace) is the key signal: speed is off the menu until it's quiet for a full week.\\\\n\\\\n**\\\\\\"How do I know if this is serious?\\\\\\"**\\\\nI'm a coach, not a clinician, so I can't diagnose this — and I won't try. What I can tell you is which signs mean \\\\\\"see a sports physio or sports medicine doc this week, don't wait\\\\\\": sharp or stabbing pain, pain that worsens run-over-run, morning pain in the first steps out of bed that doesn't ease, visible swelling or a lump, pain squeezing the tendon, or any change in how your foot pushes off. If any of those show up, please book an appointment — early assessment on Achilles stuff is cheap insurance. See the callout below.\\\\n\\\\n## Flags\\\\n- Tempo Thursday: tightness → sharper with pace → stopped at 3 mi. Clear signal from the tissue.\\\\n- Sunday long run was pain-free running but stiff after — tendon is grumbling, not screaming. That's the window to be smart.\\\\n- Mileage already came off (31 vs 44) — don't rush it back. Reload gradually once symptoms are quiet.\\\\n- Sleep 7 hrs, stress moderate, anxious about the block — I hear you. One cautious week does not throw away a marathon. Grinding on an angry Achilles can.\\\\n- Shoes: all easy miles in Ghost 16. Keep the Endorphin Speed 4 in the closet until we're back doing workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## How to read this week\\\\n- Each run, do a 5-minute walk warm-up before you start running. Flat routes only — the hilly Thursday loop is out.\\\\n- Pain rules every day: ≤3/10 and not sharp = continue; sharp, worsening, or altering your gait = stop and walk home. Report back what you felt in the check-in.\\\\n- No strides, no pickups, no hills, no MP touches. Pure easy aerobic.\\\\n- If two consecutive runs hurt more than the one before, stop running and get it looked at before the next session.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-14\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Gentle calf and ankle mobility is fine — no aggressive stretching of the Achilles, no eccentric heel drops this week unless a clinician has prescribed them.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40–10:00/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min brisk walk warm-up, then 4 mi very easy on the flat canal path. No strides. No pickups.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-15\\",\\"notes\\":\\"This is the test run. If the Achilles stays ≤3/10 and quiets as you go, finish the 4. If it sharpens or alters your stride, walk home and we treat Wednesday as rest.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40–10:00/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 5 mi flat canal path, conversational.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-16\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Only run this if Tuesday was clean. If any pain lingered after Tuesday, swap today for rest or 30 min easy cross-train (bike/elliptical, no running).\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Short core + hip session, 20 min. Skip any heavy calf loading this week.\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:05/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 4 mi flat and easy. Not the hilly route — flat only.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-17\\",\\"notes\\":\\"This replaces the tempo. No pace work, no hills. If the Achilles has been quiet all week this is just an easy aerobic day; if it's grumbling, make it 30 min easy cross-train instead and don't force the run.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-18\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Normal eating, hydrate. Use the day to honestly check in with how the tendon feels on stairs and first steps in the morning — that's useful info.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:05/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 4 mi flat and easy.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-19\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Pre-long shakeout. If anything felt off Thursday, cut this to 3 mi or skip.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:00/mi, HR ≤150\\",\\"distanceM\\":14484,\\"structure\\":\\"9 mi flat and easy, out-and-back on the canal path. No MP work, no fast finish. Walk 30s at mile 3 and mile 6 as a check-in — how does the Achilles feel? If any sharpness, cut it short and walk back.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-20\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Down from 10 last week on purpose. Keep practicing fueling — gel every 30–35 min, fluids with electrolytes. This is a feel-it-out long run, not a progression.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W38\\"}}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-12\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest/travel. Legs will be heavy today — that's expected after Sunday. 10 min easy mobility (ankles, hips, calves) if you feel like it. Prioritize sleep tonight.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Optional mobility (10 min)\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30–9:50/mi, HR Z2 (138–148)\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 5 mi conversational on canal path\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-13\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Shake-out from Sunday. Properly easy, flat canal. If the first mile feels like concrete, walk a minute and restart — do not force pace. 5-min walk warm-up before running.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:25–9:45/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 7 mi easy + 6×20s strides after the run with full walk recovery\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-14\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Primary aerobic day. Strides are 20s of relaxed turnover on flat ground with full walk recovery — not sprints. Keep HR honest Z2 on the run itself.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Strength session 1 (30–40 min): hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30–9:50/mi, HR Z2 (138–148)\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"Short warm-up walk if time allows, then 4 mi easy on flat canal. Target ~38–40 min total.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-15\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Thursday compressed to a 40-min easy window because of a work breakfast. MP work moved into Sunday's long run as a 4-mile block. Flat canal only — no strides, no pickups, no hills today. If HR won't settle under 150 in the first mile, slow down more.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-16\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Hydrate and eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts today.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45–10:05/mi, HR Z2\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 4 mi very easy on flat canal path\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-17\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Pre-long flush. Slower is better. Not the day for strides or pickups.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Short strength 2 (20–25 min): core + calves. Skip if legs feel flat.\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Easy portion HR ≤150, pace ~9:30–9:50/mi; MP block 7:55–8:05/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":24140,\\"structure\\":\\"5-min walk warm-up, then 15 mi on flat canal: 10 mi easy (Z2, HR ≤150) → 4 mi @ goal MP (8:00/mi, 7:55–8:05 window) → 1 mi easy CD. Fuel: gel at ~5 min pre-start, then every 30–35 min (4 gels total), fluids with electrolytes.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-18\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Long run upgraded from 14 easy to 15 with a 4-mile MP block in the back half, to replace Thursday's MP work. This is a bigger stimulus than it looks because the MP comes on tired-ish legs — do not over-pace. If the MP block falls apart (pace slips past 8:15 and won't come back, or HR won't drop under 165 between reps-worth of effort), convert the last 4 mi back to easy and jog home. Report back on how the block felt and how fueling sat during MP effort.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W42\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "xhigh"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgRj47242aj2XvHrPn7EU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm looking at the attached \\"Medium-long 9\\" workout from 2026-10-14, checking the distance, duration, and pace figures to understand the actual effort involved before comparing it to what the athlete reported.\\n\\nChecking the splits confirms the pace is around 9:00-9:07/mi, with average HR 148 and max 154, which sits in solid Z2 edging into low Z3. The prescribed Wednesday workout called for 7 miles easy plus strides, but the athlete instead ran 9.15 miles at that pace and HR.\\n\\nThere's a brief Achilles twinge around mile 7 that settled quickly, described as \\"nothing like September\\" — reassuring given the tendinopathy history, but worth staying cautious about. The athlete also wants to shift all long runs and marathon-pace work to the Endorphin Speed shoe for the rest of the block.\\n\\nMy coaching guidance has consistently favored the Ghost 16 for long runs, explicitly ruling out a mid-run switch to the Speed 4. A plated, more aggressive shoe changes loading patterns and geometry in ways that could stress the Achilles further, so this shoe request deserves careful pushback rather than automatic approval.\\n\\nI'm inclined to split the difference: approve the Endorphin Speed 4 for long runs that include marathon-pace work since that's genuine race simulation, but keep pure easy long runs in the Ghost 16 to protect the tendon, introducing the switch gradually rather than all at once.\\n\\nLooking back at the actual phrasing, the request covers both long runs and MP work generally, so I'm mapping it against the training block schedule — this week's 15 with 4 at MP, next week's peak MP volume at 17-18 miles, then taper starts with lighter MP touches before race week.\\n\\nSince the athlete only asked about shoes rather than requesting a plan change, I'm weighing whether a patch is actually needed. The prescribed Sunday Oct 18 run currently lists Brooks Ghost 16, so if I'm approving the Speed 4 for that long run I'll need to update that day's shoe entry — but Wednesday's run already happened today, so I shouldn't touch that one since it's in the past. I want to double check the date on the attachment to confirm it really is today's run before deciding what's actionable.\\n\\nI'll just patch Sunday with the full day object, since the rule is to only emit patches for dates actually changing. I also want to flag the shoe preference change for long runs and MP work as a settings proposal bullet, since it's significant enough to warrant a soft-gated memory update, while the brief Achilles twinge at mile 7 seems resolved and probably doesn't need a dossier update.\\n\\nOn the Achilles note, it was a mild whisper that settled, and the athlete says it felt nothing like September — not a red flag, but given the history it's worth a gentle caution about monitoring for recurrence. The workout itself came in clean: 9.15 miles in 1:23, averaging 9:04/mi with HR around 148 (max 154), splits steady throughout with a slight pickup the last two miles, and only +6 bpm of drift over the run — all well within the aerobic range of the prescribed 7 miles plus strides.\\n\\nBut the nagging pattern is there: they ran longer and faster than prescribed, which fits the drift I've flagged before — adding both distance and pace to an easy day, two days out from a key workout. HR staying controlled means the engine's fine with it, but the pacing trend itself is the thing worth naming. I'll frame the response as genuine praise for the clean metrics while gently flagging the creeping pace, plus a soft note on the Achilles and a measured take on the shoes.\\n\\nPlease dial Thursday back to the actual 9:30-9:50 range.\\n\\nOn the Achilles whisper at mile 7, good that it settled and got flagged — given the September history I'm not pulling anything from the plan over a brief sensation that cleared, but I want it watched closely per the callout.\\n\\nOn the shoe question, it's a partial yes with a staged introduction: the Endorphin Speed 4 has a different drop and more aggressive geometry than the Ghost 16, and swapping the long-run shoe mid-block while an Achilles whisper is active isn't something I'd do casually.\\n\\nSo the plan becomes using the Endorphin Speed 4 for this Sunday's full 15-mile long run with the 4-mile MP block, giving fueling and shoe practice together, and then again for the following peak long run since that one most closely mirrors race day.\\n\\nFor the taper long runs two and three weeks out, Ghost 16 is fine for the easy portion, with Speed 4 as an optional swap just for the MP touch. All regular easy runs — Tuesday, Wednesday, Saturday — stay in Ghost 16, since the Speed 4's carbon plate masks fatigue signals and would burn through shoe life fast if used daily.\\n\\nAnd the non-negotiable here is clear: any louder-than-whisper Achilles signal means switching back to Ghost 16 immediately and looping in the physio before the next long run.\\n\\nThe morning first-steps check remains the key indicator — if stiffness returns and lingers more than a few minutes, that needs to be flagged before Sunday, alongside continuing the slow heel drops. After Sunday's run, I want feedback on how the Speed 4 felt during the MP block versus the easy miles, any Achilles response, and how fueling at marathon pace sat digestively, since that will shape how the peak long run gets handled. I'm also noting the settings update: Speed 4 for long runs with MP segments and the upcoming peak long run, Ghost 16 for easy days, and continued Achilles monitoring via the morning stiffness check.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017KYjziKZrbLGsp8Gw4UfQh","name":"submit_mid_week_chat_reply","input":{"body":"Nice controlled run on paper. Quick numbers first, then shoes.\\n\\n**The run (9.15 mi, 1h 23m, 9:04/mi avg, HR 148 avg / 154 max):**\\n- Splits were metronomic: 9:07, 9:07, 9:04, 9:05, 9:05, 9:06, 9:05, 9:04, 9:00. No surges, no sloppy miles.\\n- HR drift: 147 → 153 across the full run. Only +6 bpm over 9 miles — that's a clean aerobic day. The engine was honest.\\n- You tipped briefly into low Z3 by HR at the end (153 vs Z2 ceiling 150), but marginal and expected on a long-ish midweek.\\n\\nTwo things I want to flag before we get to the shoes:\\n\\n1. **The plan was 7 mi + 6×20s strides, not a medium-long 9.** You added two miles and dropped the strides. HR says you got away with it, but on a Wednesday two days before Sunday's long run with an MP block in it, I'd rather you give me exactly what's prescribed than freelance the volume. We build this block on consistency.\\n2. **Easy pace is drifting fast again.** 9:04 is below the 9:25–9:45 window. Same nag as last week — if HR stays honest the aerobic benefit is still there, but every time \\"easy\\" creeps to 9:00 I lose a bit of the recovery stimulus. Please dial Thursday back to actual 9:30–9:50.\\n\\n**On the Achilles whisper at mile 7:** glad it settled, glad you told me. Given the September episode I want you watching it closely — see the note below. I'm not pulling anything out of the plan on the basis of a few minutes of noticeable sensation that cleared, but the rules in that note are firm.\\n\\n**On the shoe question — partial yes, with a staged introduction.**\\n\\nThe Endorphin Speed 4 has a different drop and more aggressive geometry than the Ghost 16. Swapping the shoe you spend the most time in — long runs — mid-block while an Achilles whisper just surfaced is the kind of change I'd normally make 8 weeks out, not 4–5. The upside you want (race-pace feel, legs that know the shoe) is real. The downside (changing calf/Achilles load pattern during a tendon-sensitive window) is also real. So:\\n\\n- **This Sunday (Oct 18) — Endorphin Speed 4 for the whole 15.** You get fueling-at-MP practice and shoe practice in the same run. I'm updating that day for you.\\n- **The peak long run the following Sunday (17–18 mi w/ 6–8 at MP) — Endorphin Speed 4.** That's the run that most mirrors race day; you want to be in race shoes for it.\\n- **Taper long runs (3 and 2 weeks out, mostly easy with a short MP touch) — Ghost 16 for the easy portion. Speed 4 for the MP touch is a reasonable swap if you want it.**\\n- **Easy days (Tue/Wed/Sat) stay in Ghost 16.** The Speed 4 is a workout shoe, not a daily-easy shoe — the plate masks fatigue cues and the midsole life gets eaten quickly if you put all your miles on it.\\n\\n**Non-negotiables for Sunday:**\\n- If the Achilles says anything louder than a whisper during the run, bail on the MP block, jog home, and we talk before Tuesday.\\n- First-steps-in-the-morning check is still your canary. If morning stiffness returns and doesn't ease within a few minutes, tell me before Sunday.\\n- Keep the slow heel drops going. They've been doing their job.\\n\\nReport back Sunday night with: (a) how the Speed 4 felt on the easy miles vs the MP block, (b) any Achilles signal during or after, (c) how fueling sat during MP effort. That answer dictates how aggressive we get on the peak long run.","safetyCallouts":[{"title":"Achilles — monitor, don't push through","body":"A brief whisper at mile 7 that settled is OK information, not an alarm — but the September history earns it a closer watch. Pull the plug on a run and talk to your sports physio before the next session if any of these show up: morning first-steps stiffness that doesn't ease within a few minutes, sharpening pain while running, pain that alters your stride, swelling or tenderness when you squeeze the tendon, or symptoms that worsen run-over-run. I coach the training; a clinician diagnoses the tissue. Don't guess on this one.","severity":"caution"}],"prescribedDayPatches":[{"date":"2026-10-18","dayType":"long","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":24140,"shoes":"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4","paceOrHr":"Easy portion HR ≤150, pace ~9:30–9:50/mi; MP block 7:55–8:05/mi","structure":"5-min walk warm-up, then 15 mi on flat canal: 10 mi easy (Z2, HR ≤150) → 4 mi @ goal MP (8:00/mi, 7:55–8:05 window) → 1 mi easy CD. Fuel: gel ~5 min pre-start, then every 30–35 min (4 gels total), fluids with electrolytes."},"notes":"Shoe updated to Endorphin Speed 4 for the whole run per your request — you get race-shoe practice on the easy miles AND under MP effort in one session. Do not over-pace the MP block; the Speed 4 will feel springy and the temptation is to drop under 7:55. If the MP block falls apart (pace slips past 8:15 and won't come back), convert the last 4 mi to easy and jog home. If the Achilles says anything louder than a whisper at any point, bail on MP and finish easy. Report back on shoe feel (easy vs MP), any Achilles signal, and how fueling sat during MP effort."}],"settingsProposalBullets":["Shoe preference update: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4 for long runs that include an MP block (this Sunday's 15 w/ 4 at MP, and the peak long run the following Sunday with 6–8 at MP).","Taper long runs (3 and 2 weeks out) stay in Brooks Ghost 16 for the easy portion; Endorphin Speed 4 is OK for any short MP touch within those runs.","Daily easy runs (Tue/Wed/Sat) remain in Brooks Ghost 16 — Speed 4 stays a workout-only shoe.","Achilles watchpoint re-opened: brief whisper at mile 7 of the Oct 14 run that settled; no action beyond monitoring, maintaining heel drops, and the escalation rules in the safety note."]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":29069,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6684,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4296}},"diagnostics":null}	200	101811	tool_use	29069	6684	0	0	ok	\N	4296
