d63887bf-dede-4062-886f-8fc6cda22144	{"days": [{"date": "2026-10-12", "notes": "Fixed rest/travel. Legs will be heavy today — that's expected after Sunday. 10 min easy mobility (ankles, hips, calves) if you feel like it. Prioritize sleep tonight.", "dayType": "rest", "strength": "Optional mobility (10 min)"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:30–9:50/mi, HR Z2 (138–148)", "distanceM": 8047, "structure": "5-min walk warm-up, then 5 mi conversational on canal path"}, "date": "2026-10-13", "notes": "Shake-out from Sunday. Properly easy, flat canal. If the first mile feels like concrete, walk a minute and restart — do not force pace. 5-min walk warm-up before running.", "dayType": "easy"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:25–9:45/mi, HR Z2", "distanceM": 11265, "structure": "5-min walk warm-up, then 7 mi easy + 6×20s strides after the run with full walk recovery"}, "date": "2026-10-14", "notes": "Primary aerobic day. Strides are 20s of relaxed turnover on flat ground with full walk recovery — not sprints. Keep HR honest Z2 on the run itself.", "dayType": "easy", "strength": "Strength session 1 (30–40 min): hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:30–9:50/mi, HR Z2 (138–148)", "distanceM": 6437, "structure": "Short warm-up walk if time allows, then 4 mi easy on flat canal. Target ~38–40 min total."}, "date": "2026-10-15", "notes": "Thursday compressed to a 40-min easy window because of a work breakfast. MP work moved into Sunday's long run as a 4-mile block. Flat canal only — no strides, no pickups, no hills today. If HR won't settle under 150 in the first mile, slow down more.", "dayType": "easy"}, {"date": "2026-10-16", "notes": "Fixed rest. Hydrate and eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts today.", "dayType": "rest"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:45–10:05/mi, HR Z2", "distanceM": 6437, "structure": "5-min walk warm-up, then 4 mi very easy on flat canal path"}, "date": "2026-10-17", "notes": "Pre-long flush. Slower is better. Not the day for strides or pickups.", "dayType": "easy", "strength": "Short strength 2 (20–25 min): core + calves. Skip if legs feel flat."}, {"run": {"type": "long", "shoes": "Saucony Endorphin Speed 4", "paceOrHr": "Easy portion HR ≤150, pace ~9:30–9:50/mi; MP block 7:55–8:05/mi", "distanceM": 24140, "structure": "5-min walk warm-up, then 15 mi on flat canal: 10 mi easy (Z2, HR ≤150) → 4 mi @ goal MP (8:00/mi, 7:55–8:05 window) → 1 mi easy CD. Fuel: gel ~5 min pre-start, then every 30–35 min (4 gels total), fluids with electrolytes."}, "date": "2026-10-18", "notes": "Shoe updated to Endorphin Speed 4 for the whole run per your request — you get race-shoe practice on the easy miles AND under MP effort in one session. Do not over-pace the MP block; the Speed 4 will feel springy and the temptation is to drop under 7:55. If the MP block falls apart (pace slips past 8:15 and won't come back), convert the last 4 mi to easy and jog home. If the Achilles says anything louder than a whisper at any point, bail on MP and finish easy. Report back on shoe feel (easy vs MP), any Achilles signal, and how fueling sat during MP effort.", "dayType": "long"}], "week": "2026-W42"}	## Headline\nBig week in the books — 45 miles, your longest run in two years, and a long run with a genuine negative split (back half 8:45/mi vs front 9:13/mi). That's a confidence builder. The 3:30 target is still live. But two things from this week tell me we pull the reins a little this week before we go hard again: your Thursday session went off-script into VO2 territory (max HR 184, 24% of the run in Z5), and the Sunday drift was +16.9 bpm — well above the +10 target. Combine that with sleep slipping to 6.8 hrs, legs heavy into Monday, and relative effort 1.3× your three-week average, and the smart play is a modest step-back now so we can hit one more quality block before taper.\n\nSo this week: ~37 miles, strictly MP-focused quality (no VO2 reps), long run back to 14 miles with the HR cap and no MP finish. Call it a reset. Then we go bigger again the week of Oct 19 with a long run around 18–20 and a longer MP block.\n\n## Your questions\n\n**1. Is 3:30 still sensible?**\nYes, with one caveat. The evidence from the 20-miler is strong — those last four miles rolled at 7:58–8:04/mi off tired legs, with HR climbing but not blown. That's a real signal you can hold goal pace. The caveat: we need to see one more good quality block (an 18–20 mi long run with a solid MP close, and MP intervals that stay *at* MP) before I'll say it with full confidence. We'll know in about two weeks. Keep the goal, earn the goal.\n\n**2. Heavy legs Monday after a 20-miler — normal?**\nTotally normal, especially this one. You stacked a hard interval session Thursday (max HR 184 — that's VO2 territory, not MP) and then went 20 miles with a hot finish three days later. Of course Monday felt like mud. What I'd watch: legs should feel materially better by Wednesday. If they don't, tell me and we'll cut Thursday's quality back.\n\n## About Thursday last week\nThe plan was 2 × 2 mi at goal MP (~8:00/mi). What you ran was effectively 5 × 1 mi hard with jog recovery, with the fast miles down at 6:55–7:02 — that's closer to 10K effort than MP. One red zone session won't hurt you, but we have an explicit plan to save VO2 work for later in the build (if at all). Right now, every quality mile needs to be teaching your legs *marathon pace feel*. That means staying at 7:55–8:05/mi on the fast portions, not racing them. This Thursday is the test — if you're under 7:50 on the first rep, back off.\n\n## Why each session this week\n- **Tue easy 5**: shake-out from the 20, flat canal, Z2 only. Walk if the first mile is grim.\n- **Wed easy 7 + 6×20s strides**: aerobic volume with a touch of leg speed. Strides are relaxed turnover, not sprints.\n- **Thu MP intervals (3 × 2 mi)**: this is the correction session. Six total MP miles at 7:55–8:05/mi with 3:00 easy jog between. More MP volume than last planned, but *at MP*, not faster. Hilly Thursday route is fine; hold effort on climbs.\n- **Sat easy 4**: pre-long flush, slower is better.\n- **Sun long 14, HR ≤150, no MP finish**: deliberate step-back. We earned a quieter Sunday. Pure aerobic time on feet so you arrive at next week fresh enough to go bigger.\n\n## Flags\n- Z1+Z2 only 68.7% last week — below the 80% base target. The culprit was Thursday's VO2 drift plus a hot long-run finish. Keep easy days genuinely easy and this fixes itself this week.\n- Long-run drift +16.9 bpm — above target. Partly heat/fatigue, partly the picked-up finish. The HR cap on Sunday is non-negotiable this week.\n- Sleep 6.8 hrs is low for someone running 45 mi/wk. Protect sleep this week — it's part of the training.\n- Shin history noted. Nothing bothering you now; if anything whispers after the 20-miler, tell me.	\N	2026-10-11 20:01:23.138953+00	2026-10-14 22:45:37.290675+00	\N
42d956f4-8b0a-4145-98ff-a058741c4904	{"days": [{"date": "2026-09-28", "notes": "Fixed rest/travel. 10 min mobility if you feel like it — calves and ankles. Slow heel drops as prescribed.", "dayType": "rest", "strength": "Optional mobility (10 min)"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:30–9:50/mi, HR Z2", "distanceM": 8047, "structure": "5-min walk warm-up, then 5 mi conversational on the canal path"}, "date": "2026-09-29", "notes": "Shake-out from Sunday. Conversational, flat canal path. 5-min walk warm-up before you start running.", "dayType": "easy"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:25–9:45/mi, HR Z2", "distanceM": 11265, "structure": "5-min walk warm-up, then 7 mi easy + 6×20s strides after the run"}, "date": "2026-09-30", "notes": "Primary aerobic day. Strides are relaxed turnover, not sprints — on flat ground with full walk recovery between.", "dayType": "easy", "strength": "Strength session 1 (30–40 min): hips, glutes, calves, single-leg work"}, {"run": {"type": "quality", "shoes": "Saucony Endorphin Speed 4", "paceOrHr": "MP reps 7:55–8:05/mi (mid-Z3/low-Z4); WU/CD 9:40–10:00/mi", "distanceM": 12875, "structure": "5-min walk warm-up, then 8 mi total: 2 mi WU → 2 × 2 mi @ goal MP (8:00/mi) with 3:00 easy jog between → 1.5 mi CD"}, "date": "2026-10-01", "notes": "Returning to MP intervals. First rep should feel controlled, not racing — if mile 1 is under 7:50 you went too hot. Hilly Thursday route is fine; hold effort on climbs and let pace drift 5–10 sec. If anything grumbles in the Achilles during warm-up, convert to an easy 6 and we'll try again next week.", "dayType": "quality"}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "notes": "Fixed rest. Hydrate and eat normally — fueling for Sunday starts here.", "dayType": "rest"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:45–10:05/mi, HR Z2", "distanceM": 6437, "structure": "5-min walk warm-up, then 4 mi very easy on flat canal path"}, "date": "2026-10-03", "notes": "Pre-long flush. Slower is better.", "dayType": "easy", "strength": "Strength session 2 (20–25 min): core + calves"}, {"run": {"type": "long", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "HR ≤150; pace likely 9:30–9:50/mi", "distanceM": 21726, "structure": "5-min walk warm-up, then 13.5 mi steady on the canal path, HR-capped. Out-and-back."}, "date": "2026-10-04", "notes": "Long run back to 13.5. No MP finish this week — just honest aerobic time on feet with HR cap. Fuel every 30–35 min with a gel (3 gels total), fluids with electrolytes. Start pre-sunrise if warm. If HR drifts above 150 and won't come back, walk 30s and resume slower.", "dayType": "long"}], "week": "2026-W40"}	## Headline\nClean, confident week. 34.8 mi, tempo went well with Achilles quiet (your own note: "kept checking… it was fine"), long run out to 11.9 with a mild negative split and HR drift back inside acceptable range (+8.8 over nearly 2 hrs). Z1+Z2 at 81.5% — right where I want it. You're healthy, hitting marathon-base targets, and 7 weeks from Lakeshore. Time to build again, carefully.\n\nThis week: ~38 mi, step the long run to 13.5, and reintroduce real marathon-pace work on Thursday — 2 × 2 mi at goal MP (~8:00/mi). We're not going back to the aggressive block we had before the Achilles flare; we're layering MP volume gradually so the tendon stays happy.\n\n## Your question — Achilles maintenance through race day\nKeep doing what's clearly working, don't invent new stuff:\n- **Slow heel drops** daily — the physio's protocol is doing its job; keep it going right through race week. On the Monday of race week drop to once a day, and skip them the day before the race.\n- **5-minute walk warm-up before every run.** Boring, free, protective. Keep it in.\n- **First-steps-in-the-morning check** — that's your canary. If morning stiffness ever returns and doesn't ease within a few minutes, tell me in the check-in before your next run.\n- **Shoe rotation** — Ghost 16 for easy, Endorphin Speed 4 only on quality days. Don't let an easy run accidentally happen in the Speed 4.\n- **One rebuild rule I'm applying**: we add either distance OR intensity in a given week, not big jumps of both. This week it's a modest distance bump plus returning MP; next week we'll either hold intensity and push the long run, or hold distance and sharpen quality.\n\nIf anything whispers at you — sharper than a 2/10, lingers after runs, or alters your gait — back to the physio before pushing on. Keep her in the loop as we get closer to race day too.\n\n## Flags\n- Thursday tempo HR max hit 174 (upper Z4). Intended effort was tempo, not threshold — this week's MP reps should sit mid-Z3 to low Z4, not spike. If you see 170+ on an MP mile, you're pushing too hard.\n- Long-run drift still slightly on the high side (+8.8). Not alarming given back-half pickup, but keep the HR cap of ≤150 on long runs this week — pace will be whatever it is.\n- Mileage jump +8.9 mi over prior week was a bit sharp — this week we only add ~3 mi on top so the ramp isn't stacking.\n- Sleep 7.4, strength 2 of 2, stress low — all green. Protect that.	\N	2026-09-27 20:00:39.081494+00	2026-09-27 20:00:39.081494+00	\N
